*! test_twoway_option_parity.cscript
*! Certification script: the twoway options GAPS.md F3 listed as landing in
*! the note as UNKNOWN -- ROADMAP WP-22 TR-22.3 and AC-22.2.
*!
*! Every expectation below is measured against twoway, the way
*! test_alias_semantics.cscript measures bw(): twoway is asked first, and
*! dash must do what twoway did.
*!
*! twoway's answers are measured once and replayed (WP-30 test performance,
*! B2; cert_truth.do): a certification run reads them from
*! test/fixtures/twoway_option_parity_truth.json, which
*! scripts/extract_twoway_oracle_truth.do writes by running this script
*! with twoway asked; DASH_CERT_REMEASURE=1 asks twoway in the run again and
*! fails on any answer that is no longer the fixture's (the release run).
*! Where a comment below says twoway is asked in the run, it is asked in
*! the run that measures its answers.
*!
*! The measurements behind the design (the
*! pictures twoway draws, exported to SVG and compared) are recorded in the
*! WP-22 work notes; the oracles used here are the cheap ones that decide the
*! same questions:
*!
*!   * Whether a plot type draws the CONNECTING LINE that clcolor(),
*!     clpattern() and clwidth() style.  twoway_yxview_parse.class maps
*!     CLColor() to line(color()) only, and LColor() to line(color()) AND
*!     area(linestyle(color())); a type that never draws its `line' style
*!     never evaluates clwidth(), so clwidth(-1) is refused, when drawn,
*!     exactly on the types that draw the connecting line ("gm_linewidth
*!     must be between 0.000 and 1.0e+04", r(198)) and accepted everywhere
*!     else.  Measured by SVG: on line connected lfit qfit fpfit lpoly
*!     lowess mspline mband kdensity function tsline, and on the fit line of
*!     lfitci qfitci lpolyci fpfitci, clX draws what lX draws on the line;
*!     on every other type clX draws a picture identical to no option.
*!   * Whether a plot type draws marker labels, which decides where
*!     mlabangle(400) is refused ("textangle must be between -360.000 and
*!     360.000", r(198), when drawn -- though on pcarrow and pcbarrow
*!     twoway prints the message and returns rc 0).
*!
*! Groups:
*!   TP-01  clcolor() clpattern() clwidth(), per plot type: kept in the spec
*!          where twoway draws the connecting line, dropped where it does
*!          not (twoway draws nothing for them there), never named in the
*!          note; clwidth(-1) refused, naming clwidth(), exactly where
*!          twoway refuses it.
*!   TP-02  their minimum abbreviations are twoway's -- clc() clp() clw()
*!          -- and cl() is not one (twoway r(198); dash names cl()).
*!   TP-03  lcolor() and clcolor() together: both reach the spec, where the
*!          renderer lets clcolor() style the line whatever the order
*!          (test_twoway_option_parity.py certifies the drawing).
*!   TP-04  mlabangle(): recorded, abbreviated mlabang(), a bad name passed
*!          on (twoway notes it); mlabangle(400) refused exactly on the types
*!          where twoway refuses it (pccapsym among them; pcarrow and
*!          pcbarrow draw labels yet return rc 0 in twoway).
*!   TP-05  mlabformat(): recorded, abbreviated mlabf(), any text accepted
*!          (twoway accepts mlabformat(abc) with no note).
*!   TP-06  the declared-but-not-honoured ones are named in the note by
*!          their full names, however they were abbreviated, in comma mode
*!          and after the paren-mode comma: sort(varlist) where dash does
*!          not join (scatter), xoverhangs, yoverhangs;
*!          sort sort(varlist) on line is honoured, silent and written as
*!          "sortvars" (WP-29 P0.1).  TP-06h: mlabvposition() and
*!          mlabtextstyle() are honoured (WP-30 P1.24): not named, written
*!          to the spec.
*!   TP-07  what twoway itself refuses dash refuses as twoway does (WP-32;
*!          it stayed UNKNOWN and was named in the note):
*!          xreverse yreverse xalternate yalternate xcommon ycommon
*!          lockaspect zoom() altaxis ddensity addplot() margin() region()
*!          bargap() -- declaring any of them would be a lie in the help.
*!   TP-08  mlabel(), per plot type: refused where twoway refuses it --
*!          r(103) on mspline and mband, r(111) for a variable that does
*!          not exist on every type but histogram and function -- and, on
*!          those two, which never read it, left out of the spec.
*!   TP-09  marker labels are drawn on exactly the plot types twoway draws
*!          them on (twoway's exported SVG against the saved dashboard).
*!   TP-10  a value-labelled variable is labelled with its value labels.
*!   TP-11  lcolor() never reaches a marker; mlcolor() draws its outline.
*!   TP-12  adversarial mlabel() values on mspline (CLAUDE.md rule 18): an
*!          abbreviation, a repeated name and four hundred names refused
*!          r(103) as twoway refuses them; SMCL refused and echoed as text;
*!          nothing registered.
*!   TP-13  the other side of twoway's minimums, and clwidth()'s ceiling
*!          (WP-24's second round): a spelling one letter short of the
*!          minimum is not the option -- mlaban(), sor(), xoverhan and
*!          yoverhan named as typed, mlab() read as mlabel(), in comma mode
*!          and after the paren-mode comma, as twoway reads each -- and
*!          clwidth() and lwidth() take 0 and 10000 and refuse -0.001 and
*!          10000.001, where twoway draws them.
*!   Q3506-2 (WP-35 GW-2) aspectratio() with xoverhangs or yoverhangs
*!          refused as twoway refuses it, on both routes
*!   TP-14  an option given more than once (BUGS.md, S3): each command
*!          twoway draws as another -- mcolor(red) mcolor(blue) as
*!          mcolor(blue), title(A) title(, color(red)) as title(A,
*!          color(red)), a plot group's legend() beside the one after the
*!          comma as the two joined -- SVG exports compared in the run, is
*!          registered as that other; a unique option given twice refused in
*!          twoway's words; both routes; 10,000 copies r(1003) as in twoway,
*!          and hostile values in a repeat stored as text.  TP-14f: the
*!          options dash does not declare and names in the note -- atobs,
*!          nofit, clegend(), nodropbase and the rest -- given twice where
*!          twoway takes them once, refused in twoway's words (the second
*!          copy as typed, the noX copy of a pair), in one list and, for
*!          the graph-wide ones, across plot groups and || segments; given
*!          twice where twoway takes them again, named in the note as
*!          before; twoway's verdict asked in the run; a hostile value
*!          never echoed or run; 250 copies then a pair refused quickly.
*!   TP-15  log is the graph option logging, and only lo, logi and logit
*!          are lowess's logit (twoway's serset of lowess compared with
*!          the spec, in the run); a plot option after a plot group's comma,
*!          an option in upper case, and two kernel flags or a flag beside
*!          kernel() on lpoly, lpolyci and kdensity are refused in twoway's
*!          words and code, naming the first word twoway does not take;
*!          hostile values never echoed or run; 200 words then a refusal
*!          answered quickly.
*!   TP-16  a kernel written as an option of its own -- gaussian, twoway's
*!          old syntax -- on lpoly, lpolyci and kdensity, from each
*!          shortest spelling to the full name (bi, cos, ep, epan2, gau,
*!          par, rec, tri): twoway draws the serset of kernel(<name>) (asked
*!          in the run), and dash registers kernel(<name>) with no note, in
*!          comma mode, in plot groups and in || segments; a shorter
*!          spelling, and any spelling on another type, twoway refuses and
*!          dash does not read as a kernel; a hostile value beside the flag
*!          never run; 200 unknown words then a flag answered quickly.
*!   JO-21..27  sort() as twoway checks it (WP-29 S02): a malformed name
*!          refused on all forty types, a name that is no usable variable on
*!          the 23 serset types, each in twoway's words and r(198); the 17
*!          other types take it; repeats read as twoway reads them; silent
*!          on the six joining types and tsline/tsrline, named elsewhere.
*!   AX-01  _dash_route_axis2 rewrites each family's axis(2) form to dash's
*!          second-axis key, drops axis(1), renames twoway's plurals and
*!          leaves every refused form, and hostile text, as typed (P0.5);
*!          takes an axis(3) form out for the axisn record (WP-31 C10c).
*!   AX-02  _dash_axis_num: twoway's axis number (a whole number within
*!          its integer bounds, else 1).
*!   AX-03  every axis(#) form twoway refuses dash refuses, r(198), with
*!          twoway's message (an axis no layer uses, AXIS(), a second
*!          axis(), axis-1 options on a lone yaxis(2) graph).
*!   AX-04  the first refusal is twoway's: side, family, position, the
*!          segments before the options after the comma.
*!   AX-05  a second comma is refused, invalid '<word>', r(198); a trailing
*!          empty comma is accepted.
*!   AX-06  every spelling twoway accepts (ax, axi, 02, 2.0, a, 1e300, hex,
*!          plot groups, by(), the plurals) dash accepts.
*!   AX-07  the stored spec keeps each axis's copy through the repeat merge.
*!   AX-08  10,000 copies end r(1003) quickly and leave nothing behind.
*!   MV-01  mlabvposition() (WP-30 P1.24) is refused r(103) in twoway's
*!          words on the 21 types that count their variables; MV-02 with
*!          abbreviated variables and mlabel(); MV-03 a string variable;
*!   MV-04  a missing variable r(111); MV-05 a second copy r(198); MV-06
*!          two names r(103); MV-07 an expression r(198); MV-08 the empty
*!          option and the abbreviations taken, s() kept; MV-09 not read on
*!          histogram, function, scatteri, pci, pcarrowi; MV-10 taken in
*!          silence on line, spike, area, pcspike, tsline; MV-11 (and 11b)
*!          twoway's count quirks.
*!   MV-12  mlabtextstyle() (part 2) is taken in silence on line, lfit and
*!          rscatter, the rightmost copy kept, mlabt() read; MV-13 it is a
*!          style list, one element per y.
*!   RS-01  the region refusals twoway gives, rc and words (WP-30 P1.20a).
*!   RS-02  graphregion() before plotregion(), both before legend()/axes.
*!   RS-03  every region sub-option from its minimum spelling to its name.
*!   RS-04  what twoway takes with rc 0 (a trailing comma, bad style names).
*!   RS-10  repeated region copies merge as twoway applies them.
*!   RS-11  two abbreviated copies are written under their full names.
*!   RS-12  the measured copy pairs (region_truth.json M) merge as drawn.
*!   CM-01..CM-12  connect() and cmissing() read as twoway reads them
*!          (WP-30 P1.8a; connect_truth.json): refusals, notes, spellings,
*!          copies, per-y types, the silent and the named types.
*!   BG-07  barwidth() on rcap and rcapsym is refused r(198) in twoway's words,
*!          in comma mode, in a plot group and after || (WP-30 P1.17a).
*!   BG-08  barw(), barwi(), barwidth() on rcap: the spelling typed is named.
*!   BG-09  guards: bar, rbar and spike take barwidth(); quoted and nested
*!          text is not read; rcap bw() keeps its note.
*!   NP-20  p(p3) p(p4) writes "p":"p3" (the first copy); under p() no
*!          mcolor/lcolor/mlabcolor is written and mlabel() is kept.
*!   NP-21  pstyle(p4) p(p3) writes p only.
*!   NP-22  area/rarea: lstyle() alstyle() blstyle() astyle() not named
*!          (flipped, WP-32: drawn).
*!   NP-23  pcarrow: mstyle() and mlstyle() not named (flipped, WP-32).
*!   NP-24  spike, clstyle(p3) writes no clstyle.
*!   NP-25  scatter, astyle(p3) is silent, rc 0 (WP-30 P1.14a, NP-20..25).
*!   TA-01..TA-10, TA-15, TA-16  the t-options (tlabel() .. tline())
*!          folded onto the x axis as twoway reads them: values, order,
*!          abbreviations, units, refusals, the first-plot rule, any graph,
*!          lenient literals, hostile tokens, minor ticks, x-option literals
*!          and the unit noted at build (WP-30 P1.6).  TA-11..TA-13:
*!          axis(2) and the t...2() spellings, format() overrides, %-tm.
*!
*! TP-01 to TP-08 render nothing: every dash probe registers with name(),
*! and the spec is read back out of the registry, as in
*! test_alias_semantics.cscript.  TP-09 to TP-11 compare what is DRAWN, so
*! they export twoway's picture to SVG and save the dashboard.
*!
*! Usage:  do test/test_twoway_option_parity.cscript  (or run_all_cscripts.do)

cscript "dash twoway option parity (WP-22 TR-22.3)" adodir ".."

clear all
// Certification timing: run_all_cscripts.do reads timer 100 when this
// script ends; with DASH_CERT_PROFILE set it also prints the profile.
timer clear 100
timer on 100
local _cert_prof : environment DASH_CERT_PROFILE
if "`_cert_prof'" != "" {
    capture profiler clear
    profiler on
}
set more off
set graphics off

do "cert_helpers.do"
quietly do "cert_svg.do"
qui do "../dash_parse.mata"
qui do "../dash.ado"

// twoway's answers (WP-30 test performance, B2): every question below is
// asked of twoway in a run with DASH_CERT_REMEASURE set, and read from
// fixtures/twoway_option_parity_truth.json otherwise (cert_truth.do).  Each
// case group names its questions with cert_truth_ctx, so one command asked
// with other data in memory is another question.  `_ct_l' is 1 when this
// run asks twoway, else 0.
do "cert_truth.do"
cert_truth_init twoway_option_parity
python: _dct = __import__("sys").modules["_dash_cert_truth"]
python: _dct.flag("_ct_l")

// cscript drops every global; cert_helpers.do set it again, and so does this.
global dash_nobrowser 1


sysuse auto, clear
generate lo  = mpg - 2
generate hi  = mpg + 2
generate pos = mod(_n, 12) + 1
generate t   = _n

local logfile "`c(tmpdir)'dash_twoway_option_parity.log"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Helpers
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture mata: mata drop _ztp_has()
capture mata: mata drop _ztp_hasval()
mata:
// Does the registered spec for graph `g' carry the quoted key `key'?
real scalar _ztp_has(string scalar g, string scalar key)
{
    string scalar js
    js = st_global("dash_json_" + g)
    return(strpos(js, char(34) + key + char(34) + ":") > 0)
}
// ... with the string value `val'?
real scalar _ztp_hasval(string scalar g, string scalar key, string scalar val)
{
    string scalar js, q
    js = st_global("dash_json_" + g)
    q  = char(34)
    return(strpos(js, q + key + q + ":" + q + val + q) > 0)
}
end

capture program drop _ztp_has
program define _ztp_has, rclass
    args g key
    mata: st_local("_zh", strofreal(_ztp_has(st_local("g"), st_local("key"))))
    return scalar found = `_zh'
end

// Run one dash command under a named log; r(rc) is its return code and
// r(note) whether the log carries the ignoring note at all.
// Both searches read the log with cert_log_has, which undoes Stata's
// wrapping at the column (cert_helpers.do): they used cert_file_has, which
// reads the bytes, so a note or a name split across a wrapped line was
// "absent" -- an absence check that could not see what it looked for
// (changed with TP-13, 24sep2026; every TP case passes either way on this
// tree, where no note here reaches the column).
// A twoway command's answer -- its rc and the words its log holds -- is
// asked of twoway in a live run and read back otherwise (cert_truth.do),
// the same words in the same log either way; a dash command always runs.
capture program drop _ztp_run
program define _ztp_run, rclass
    args cmdtext logpath
    capture log close _ztplog
    capture erase "`logpath'"
    capture dash clear
    mata: st_local("_ct_tw", strofreal(substr(st_local("cmdtext"), 1, 7) == "twoway "))
    local _ct_l 1
    if `_ct_tw' {
        python: _dct = __import__("sys").modules["_dash_cert_truth"]
        python: _dct.flag("_ct_l")
    }
    if `_ct_l' {
        log using "`logpath'", name(_ztplog) text replace
        capture noisily `cmdtext'
        local rc = _rc
        log close _ztplog
        if `_ct_tw' {
            python: _dct.log_put("cmdtext", "rc", "logpath")
        }
    }
    else {
        python: _dct.log_get("cmdtext", "logpath", "rc")
        if "`rc'" == "" local rc 9
    }
    cert_log_has "`logpath'", needle("ignoring unsupported")
    return scalar note = r(found)
    return scalar rc   = `rc'
end

// Is `needle' in the last probe's log?
capture program drop _ztp_logged
program define _ztp_logged, rclass
    args logpath needle
    cert_log_has "`logpath'", needle(`"`needle'"')
    return scalar found = r(found)
end

local nfail = 0
local faillist ""

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// The plot types and a varlist that makes each legal in twoway and dash.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
quietly tsset t
local types "line connected lfit qfit fpfit lpoly lowess mspline mband kdensity function tsline lfitci qfitci lpolyci fpfitci scatter area bar spike dot dropline histogram rarea rbar rspike rcap rcapsym rline rconnected rscatter tsrline pcspike pcarrow pcbarrow pcscatter scatteri pci"
foreach tt of local types {
    local v_`tt' "mpg weight"
}
foreach tt in rarea rbar rspike rcap rcapsym rline rconnected rscatter {
    local v_`tt' "lo hi weight"
}
foreach tt in pcspike pcarrow pcbarrow pcscatter pccapsym {
    local v_`tt' "mpg weight turn length"
}
local v_histogram "mpg"
local v_kdensity  "mpg"
local v_tsline    "mpg"
local v_tsrline   "lo hi"
local v_function  "y=x, range(0 1)"
local v_scatteri  "20 3000 30 4000"
local v_pci       "20 3000 30 4000"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-01 -- the cl triple, per plot type.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
cert_truth_ctx "TP-01"
foreach tt of local types {
    local v `v_`tt''
    // twoway: does this type draw the connecting line?  clwidth(-1) is
    // evaluated, and refused, only where it does.
    local sep ","
    if strpos("`v'", ",") local sep ""
    capture graph drop _all
    capture cert_tw twoway `tt' `v'`sep' clwidth(-1)
    local tw_rc = _rc
    capture graph drop _all
    local draws = (`tw_rc' == 198)
    if `tw_rc' != 0 & `tw_rc' != 198 {
        display as error "TP-01 FAIL `tt': the twoway oracle itself failed, r(`tw_rc')"
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-01(`tt')"
        continue
    }

    _ztp_run `"dash (`tt' `v'`sep' clcolor(red) clpattern(dash) clwidth(thick)), name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc   = r(rc)
    local dnote = r(note)
    local nkeys = 0
    foreach k in clcolor clpattern clwidth {
        _ztp_has zqtp `k'
        local nkeys = `nkeys' + r(found)
    }
    local bad = 0
    if `drc' != 0 {
        display as error "TP-01 FAIL `tt': dash rc=`drc'"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `dnote' {
        display as error "TP-01 FAIL `tt': clcolor()/clpattern()/clwidth() named in the note"
        local bad = 1
    }
    // Flipped (WP-35 syn:SD-20e, ruling D42): scatter's connecting line,
    // drawn with connect(), is what twoway reads the three for, so dash
    // records them there too (the renderer draws no line without
    // connect()); dropping them was wrong because twoway reads them.
    else if (`draws' | "`tt'" == "scatter") & `nkeys' != 3 {
        display as error "TP-01 FAIL `tt': twoway draws the connecting line, but the spec carries `nkeys' of the three keys"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if !`draws' & "`tt'" != "scatter" & `nkeys' != 0 {
        display as error "TP-01 FAIL `tt': twoway draws no connecting line (clX draws nothing), but the spec carries `nkeys' of the three keys"
        local bad = 1
    }

    // clwidth(-1): twoway's rc, and on a refusal the option is named as written.
    _ztp_run `"dash (`tt' `v'`sep' clwidth(-1)), name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local nrc = r(rc)
    if `nrc' != `tw_rc' {
        display as error "TP-01 FAIL `tt': clwidth(-1) is r(`tw_rc') in twoway, rc `nrc' in dash"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `nrc' == 198 {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "clwidth()"
        if r(found) != 1 {
            display as error "TP-01 FAIL `tt': clwidth(-1) refused without naming clwidth()"
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
    if `bad' {
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-01(`tt')"
    }
    else if `draws' display as text "TP-01 PASS `tt': connecting line drawn -- the triple is kept, clwidth(-1) refused"
    else            display as text "TP-01 PASS `tt': no connecting line -- the triple is dropped, as twoway draws nothing for it"
}
quietly tsset, clear

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-02 -- twoway's own minimum abbreviations.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-02"
capture cert_tw twoway line mpg weight, clc(red) clp(dash) clw(thick) nodraw
if _rc {
    display as error "TP-02 FAIL: the twoway oracle rejects clc() clp() clw(), r(`=_rc')"
    local bad = 1
}
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, clc(red) clp(dash) clw(thick) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) != 0 {
    display as error "TP-02 FAIL: clc() clp() clw() rc=`r(rc)' note=`r(note)'"
    local bad = 1
}
foreach k in clcolor clpattern clwidth {
    _ztp_has zqtp `k'
    if r(found) != 1 {
        display as error "TP-02 FAIL: the abbreviation did not record `k'"
        local bad = 1
    }
}
capture cert_tw twoway line mpg weight, cl(red) nodraw
local tw_rc = _rc
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, cl(red) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
// The positive control for every r(note) == 0 in TP-01 to TP-05: the same
// helper and needle ("ignoring unsupported", _dash_report_ignored's own
// words), on a command that must print the note.  Until 24sep2026 nothing
// in this file asserted the note present -- TP-02, TP-06 and TP-07 looked
// for option names only -- so a reworded note left every one of those
// checks nothing to find, and clcolor(), mlabangle() or mlabformat() could
// have been named in it unseen.
// Flipped: WP-32 -- cl(red), which twoway refuses, is refused in its
// words, r(198), where dash named it in the note (BUGS.md "In a few mixed
// lists dash names another word than twoway names first, and an unknown
// lower-case word is noted where twoway refuses it"); the note's positive
// control is afcolor(), which twoway takes (rc 0 on every type,
// test/fixtures/unknown_option_truth.json) and dash names.
local dnote = r(note)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option cl() not allowed"
if `tw_rc' != 198 | `drc' != 198 | `dnote' != 0 | r(found) != 1 {
    display as error "TP-02 FAIL: cl(red) is r(`tw_rc') in twoway; dash rc=`drc', note=`dnote', refused naming cl()=`r(found)'"
    local bad = 1
}
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, afcolor(red) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
local dnote = r(note)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "afcolor()"
if `drc' != 0 | `dnote' != 1 | r(found) != 1 {
    display as error "TP-02 FAIL: afcolor(red) -- dash rc=`drc', note=`dnote', named afcolor()=`r(found)'"
    local bad = 1
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-02"
}
else display as text "TP-02 PASS: clc() clp() clw() are the triple; cl() is no abbreviation of it"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-03 -- lcolor() beside clcolor(): both reach the renderer.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, clcolor(blue) lcolor(red) clwidth(thick) lwidth(vthin) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) != 0 local bad = 1
foreach k in lcolor clcolor lwidth clwidth {
    _ztp_has zqtp `k'
    if r(found) != 1 local bad = 1
}
if `bad' {
    display as error "TP-03 FAIL: lcolor()/lwidth() beside clcolor()/clwidth() did not all reach the spec"
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-03"
}
else display as text "TP-03 PASS: lcolor() and clcolor() both recorded; the renderer resolves them"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-04 -- mlabangle().
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-04"
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabang(45) nodraw
if _rc {
    display as error "TP-04 FAIL: the twoway oracle rejects mlabang(45), r(`=_rc')"
    local bad = 1
}
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabang(45) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
_ztp_has zqtp mlabangle
if r(found) != 1 | `drc' != 0 {
    display as error "TP-04 FAIL: mlabang(45) did not record mlabangle"
    local bad = 1
}
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabangle(45) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(note) != 0 {
    display as error "TP-04 FAIL: mlabangle() named in the note"
    local bad = 1
}
capture graph drop _all
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabangle(abc)
local tw_rc = _rc
capture graph drop _all
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabangle(abc) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if `tw_rc' != 0 | r(rc) != 0 {
    display as error "TP-04 FAIL: mlabangle(abc) is r(`tw_rc') in twoway (a note), rc `r(rc)' in dash"
    local bad = 1
}
// mlabangle(400), per type: refused where twoway draws marker labels.
quietly tsset t
cert_truth_ctx "TP-04 tsset"
local lab_types "scatter connected bar dot dropline rcapsym rconnected rscatter pcarrow pcbarrow pcscatter pccapsym line area spike rcap rarea rline histogram lfitci tsline"
foreach tt of local lab_types {
    local v `v_`tt''
    capture graph drop _all
    capture cert_tw twoway `tt' `v', mlabel(make) mlabangle(400)
    local tw_rc = _rc
    capture graph drop _all
    _ztp_run `"dash (`tt' `v', mlabel(make) mlabangle(400)), name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    if `drc' != `tw_rc' {
        display as error "TP-04 FAIL `tt': mlabangle(400) is r(`tw_rc') in twoway, rc `drc' in dash"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `drc' == 198 {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "mlabangle()"
        if r(found) != 1 {
            display as error "TP-04 FAIL `tt': mlabangle(400) refused without naming mlabangle()"
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
}
// scatteri labels its points from the literal list.
capture graph drop _all
capture cert_tw twoway scatteri 20 3000 "A" 30 4000 "B", mlabangle(400)
local tw_rc = _rc
capture graph drop _all
_ztp_run `"dash (scatteri 20 3000 "A" 30 4000 "B", mlabangle(400)), name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != `tw_rc' {
    display as error "TP-04 FAIL scatteri: mlabangle(400) is r(`tw_rc') in twoway, rc `r(rc)' in dash"
    local bad = 1
}
quietly tsset, clear
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-04"
}
else display as text "TP-04 PASS: mlabangle() recorded, a name passed on, 400 refused where twoway refuses it"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-05 -- mlabformat().
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-05"
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(mpg) mlabf(%9.2f) nodraw
if _rc local bad = 1
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(mpg) mlabf(%9.2f) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) != 0 local bad = 1
_ztp_has zqtp mlabformat
if r(found) != 1 local bad = 1
capture graph drop _all
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(mpg) mlabformat(abc)
local tw_rc = _rc
capture graph drop _all
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(mpg) mlabformat(abc) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if `tw_rc' != 0 | r(rc) != 0 | r(note) != 0 local bad = 1
if `bad' {
    display as error "TP-05 FAIL: mlabformat() is not recorded as twoway takes it"
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-05"
}
else display as text "TP-05 PASS: mlabformat() recorded, abbreviated mlabf(), any text accepted"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-06 -- declared, not honoured: named by the full name.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// id | dash command | twoway command | the name the note must carry
local n6 = 0
local ++n6
// Flipped (WP-29 P0.1): sort(varlist) is honoured on line, so the row
// that pins its note is on scatter, where dash still does not join.
local c6_`n6' `"dash scatter mpg weight, sort(mpg) name(zqtp)"'
local t6_`n6' `"twoway scatter mpg weight, sort(mpg) nodraw"'
// Flipped (WP-32): sort(mpg) named on scatter was wrong, because twoway
// draws the marks in mpg's order and dash now does: the spec's sortvars.
local w6_`n6' "sortvars()"
// Flipped (WP-30 P1.24): mlabv(pos) named in the note was wrong, because
// dash draws mlabvposition() per row as twoway does; it is TP-06h's row.
// Flipped (WP-30 P1.24, part 2): mlabt(heading) named in the note was
// wrong, because dash draws the scheme's heading style as twoway does; it
// is TP-06h's second row.
// Flipped (WP-31 D5): rows 2-5, xoverhang, yoverhang and the paren-mode
// forms, named in the note was wrong, because dash draws the overhangs as
// twoway does (sizing_truth.json overhang_x1): they are taken, written to
// the spec under the full name and named by nothing.
local ++n6
local c6_`n6' `"dash scatter mpg weight, xoverhang name(zqtp)"'
local t6_`n6' `"twoway scatter mpg weight, xoverhang nodraw"'
local w6_`n6' "xoverhangs()"
local ++n6
local c6_`n6' `"dash scatter mpg weight, yoverhang name(zqtp)"'
local t6_`n6' `"twoway scatter mpg weight, yoverhang nodraw"'
local w6_`n6' "yoverhangs()"
local ++n6
local c6_`n6' `"dash (scatter mpg weight) (line mpg weight), xoverhang name(zqtp)"'
local t6_`n6' `"twoway (scatter mpg weight) (line mpg weight), xoverhang nodraw"'
local w6_`n6' "xoverhangs()"
local ++n6
local c6_`n6' `"dash (scatter mpg weight) (line mpg weight), yoverhangs name(zqtp)"'
local t6_`n6' `"twoway (scatter mpg weight) (line mpg weight), yoverhangs nodraw"'
local w6_`n6' "yoverhangs()"
cert_truth_ctx "TP-06"
forvalues i = 1/`n6' {
    capture cert_tw `t6_`i''
    local tw_rc = _rc
    _ztp_run `"`c6_`i''"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    // In the note: the note itself is printed (as TP-02's control).
    local dnote = r(note)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`w6_`i''"
    local named = r(found)
    if inlist("`w6_`i''", "xoverhangs()", "yoverhangs()", "sortvars()") {
        local k6 = subinstr("`w6_`i''", "()", "", 1)
        _ztp_has zqtp `k6'
        if `tw_rc' != 0 | `drc' != 0 | `named' != 0 | r(found) != 1 {
            display as error `"TP-06 FAIL: `c6_`i'' -- twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc', `w6_`i'' named=`named', in the spec `r(found)'"'
            local nfail = `nfail' + 1
            local faillist "`faillist' TP-06(`i')"
        }
        else display as text `"TP-06 PASS: `w6_`i'' drawn, not named"'
        continue
    }
    if `tw_rc' != 0 | `drc' != 0 | `dnote' != 1 | `named' != 1 {
        display as error `"TP-06 FAIL: `c6_`i'' -- twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc', note `dnote', `w6_`i'' named=`named'"'
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-06(`i')"
    }
    else display as text `"TP-06 PASS: `w6_`i'' named in the note"'
}
// TP-06h -- declared and honoured (WP-30 P1.24): rc as twoway's, not
// named in the note, and the full name with its value in the spec.
// id | dash command | twoway command | option | value
local n6h = 0
local ++n6h
local c6h_`n6h' `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabv(pos) name(zqtp)"'
local t6h_`n6h' `"twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabv(pos) nodraw"'
local o6h_`n6h' "mlabvposition"
local v6h_`n6h' "pos"
local ++n6h
local c6h_`n6h' `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabt(heading) name(zqtp)"'
local t6h_`n6h' `"twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabt(heading) nodraw"'
local o6h_`n6h' "mlabtextstyle"
local v6h_`n6h' "heading"
cert_truth_ctx "TP-06h"
forvalues i = 1/`n6h' {
    capture cert_tw `t6h_`i''
    local tw_rc = _rc
    _ztp_run `"`c6h_`i''"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`o6h_`i''()"
    local named = r(found)
    mata: st_local("_zv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", st_local("o6h_`i'"), st_local("v6h_`i'"))))
    if `tw_rc' != `drc' | `named' != 0 | `_zv' != 1 {
        display as error `"TP-06h FAIL: `c6h_`i'' -- twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc', named `named', `o6h_`i'' `v6h_`i'' in the spec `_zv'"'
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-06h(`i')"
    }
    else display as text `"TP-06h PASS: `o6h_`i''() honoured, not named"'
}
// Flipped (WP-29 P0.1): sort sort(mpg) on line was named sort() once
// and carried nowhere, which was wrong: twoway joins the line in mpg's
// order (sort(varlist) wins over sort).  It is honoured now: rc 0, no
// note, the spec carries "sortvars" and never sort1, -syntax-'s internal
// name, which no note names either.
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, sort sort(mpg) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
local dnote = r(note)
_ztp_has zqtp sort1
local h1 = r(found)
mata: st_local("hv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "sortvars", "mpg")))
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "sort1"
local n1 = r(found)
if `drc' != 0 | `dnote' != 0 | `h1' != 0 | `hv' != 1 | `n1' != 0 {
    display as error "TP-06 FAIL: sort sort(mpg) on line -- rc `drc', note `dnote', sort1 key `h1', sortvars mpg `hv', sort1 in the log `n1'"
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-06(sort-honoured)"
}
else display as text "TP-06 PASS: sort sort(mpg) on line is honoured in silence and written as sortvars, never sort1"

// TP-06b -- a bare sort on a connected type is what dash draws, so it is not
// named (BUGS.md, S3).  twoway accepts sort on every type below (measured
// again here); with it twoway joins the points in the order of x, as dash
// joins line, connected, area and the range line and area types under it
// (tsline and tsrline join in time order whatever is given).  `dash line
// price weight, sort' said "ignoring unsupported option(s): sort()" for the
// picture it had drawn.  On a type dash does not join -- scatter, bar --
// sort is still named.  Flipped (WP-29 P0.1): sort(varlist) on a connected
// type is honoured now, so it is not named either (the last loop below).
quietly tsset t
cert_truth_ctx "TP-06b"
foreach tt in line connected area tsline rline rarea rconnected tsrline {
    local v `v_`tt''
    capture graph drop _all
    capture cert_tw twoway `tt' `v', sort nodraw
    local tw_rc = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash `tt' `v', sort name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local dnote = r(note)
    if `tw_rc' != 0 | `drc' != 0 | `dnote' != 0 {
        display as error "TP-06b FAIL: `tt', sort -- twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc', note `dnote' (want none)"
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-06b(`tt')"
    }
}
_ztp_run `"dash (line mpg weight, sort) (scatter mpg weight), name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) != 0 {
    display as error "TP-06b FAIL: a paren-mode line with sort is named or refused"
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-06b(paren)"
}
foreach c in "scatter mpg weight, sort" "bar mpg weight, sort" {
    local sep ""
    if !strpos("`c'", ",") | substr("`c'", 1, 1) == "(" local sep ","
    capture graph drop _all
    capture cert_tw twoway `c'`sep' nodraw
    local tw_rc = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'`sep' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    // Flipped: WP-32 -- a bare sort was named sort(), which was wrong
    // because twoway names a word as typed (BUGS.md "A bare sort or
    // headlabel is named sort() or headlabel() in the note").
    // Flipped (WP-32): named at all was wrong, because twoway draws the
    // marks in x order and dash now does (BUGS.md "sort on marker types and contour, and heatmap, outlines and alpattern() on contour, are named where twoway draws them").
    cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle("ignoring unsupported")
    if `tw_rc' != 0 | `drc' != 0 | r(found) != 0 {
        display as error "TP-06b FAIL: dash `c' -- twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc', sort named `r(found)' (want 0)"
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-06b(`c')"
    }
}
foreach c in "line mpg weight, sort(price)" "(line mpg weight, sort(price)) (scatter mpg weight)" {
    local sep ""
    if !strpos("`c'", ",") | substr("`c'", 1, 1) == "(" local sep ","
    capture graph drop _all
    capture cert_tw twoway `c'`sep' nodraw
    local tw_rc = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'`sep' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local dnote = r(note)
    if `tw_rc' != 0 | `drc' != 0 | `dnote' != 0 {
        display as error "TP-06b FAIL: dash `c' -- twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc', note `dnote' (want none)"
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-06b(`c')"
    }
}
display as text "TP-06b: a bare sort, and sort(varlist), are not named on a connected type, nor on scatter and bar"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// JO -- sort() as twoway checks it (WP-29 S02)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// twoway checks sort()'s names with -syntax-'s namelist on every plot
// type (twoway_yxview_parse.class:187), so a malformed name is refused
// on all forty, r(198), with one line naming the first bad character or
// token.  On the 23 types that draw a serset, serset create then reads
// the names as variables: one that is not a usable variable is refused
// with Stata's varlist line and "option sort() incorrectly specified",
// r(198), and so are more than ten names (_all counting the variables in
// memory and two of twoway's own).  On the other 17 types sort() is not
// read.  dash used to accept every sort() with a note.  Every expectation
// is asked of twoway in the same run.
local jologtw "`c(tmpdir)'dash_jo_twoway.log"
// twoway's answer -- its rc and the words its log holds -- asked here in a
// live run and read back otherwise (cert_truth.do), the same words in the
// same log either way.
capture program drop _zjo_tw
program define _zjo_tw, rclass
    args cmdtext logpath
    capture log close _zjotw
    capture erase "`logpath'"
    python: _dct = __import__("sys").modules["_dash_cert_truth"]
    python: _dct.flag("_ct_l")
    if `_ct_l' {
        log using "`logpath'", name(_zjotw) text replace
        capture noisily `cmdtext'
        local rc = _rc
        log close _zjotw
        python: _dct.log_put("cmdtext", "rc", "logpath")
    }
    else {
        python: _dct.log_get("cmdtext", "logpath", "rc")
        if "`rc'" == "" local rc 9
    }
    return scalar rc = `rc'
end
// twoway and dash given one plot type, varlist and option: r(ok) is 1
// when both return `wrc' and both logs carry each wanted line.
capture program drop _zjo_pair
program define _zjo_pair, rclass
    args t v o ltw ld wrc l1 l2
    local sep ","
    if strpos(`"`v'"', ",") local sep ""
    capture graph drop _all
    _zjo_tw `"twoway `t' `v'`sep' `o' nodraw"' "`ltw'"
    local trc = r(rc)
    capture graph drop _all
    _ztp_run `"dash `t' `v'`sep' `o' name(zqtp)"' "`ld'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local dnote = r(note)
    local ok = (`trc' == `wrc' & `drc' == `wrc')
    local miss ""
    foreach l in l1 l2 {
        if `"``l''"' == "" continue
        foreach f in ltw ld {
            cert_log_has "``f''", needle(`"``l''"')
            if r(found) < 1 {
                local ok = 0
                local miss "`miss' `f'"
            }
        }
    }
    return scalar ok = `ok'
    return scalar note = `dnote'
    return local why "twoway r(`trc'), dash r(`drc'), a wanted line missing from:`miss'"
end
local v_pccapsym "mpg weight turn length"
local v_pcarrowi "20 3000 30 4000"
local jo_all "`types' pccapsym pcarrowi"
local jo_ser "scatter line connected area bar spike dropline dot rarea rbar rspike rcap rcapsym rscatter rline rconnected pcspike pcarrow pcbarrow pcscatter pccapsym mband mspline"
local jo_oth "lfit lfitci qfit qfitci fpfit fpfitci lowess lpoly lpolyci function tsline tsrline histogram kdensity scatteri pci pcarrowi"
local jo_six "line connected area rline rarea rconnected"

// JO-21: a malformed name, on all forty types.
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "JO-21"
foreach tt of local jo_all {
    local v `v_`tt''
    local k = 0
    foreach o in "x*" "z+" "L.x" "-zz" "1x" "z, stable" "z(1)" {
        local ++k
        local w : word `k' of "*" "+" "L.x" "-" "1x" "," "("
        _zjo_pair `tt' `"`v'"' `"sort(`o')"' "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" 198 `"`w' invalid name"'
        if !r(ok) {
            display as error `"JO-21 FAIL: `tt', sort(`o') -- `r(why)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' JO-21"
}
else display as text "JO-21 PASS: a malformed name in sort() is refused r(198) in twoway's words on all forty types"

// JO-22: a name that is no usable variable, on the 23 serset types.
generate zz = mod(_n, 5)
generate zb = mod(_n, 3)
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "JO-22"
foreach tt of local jo_ser {
    local v `v_`tt''
    foreach o in nosuch z _N int in if using with _b "zz nosuch" {
        local w "variable `o' not found"
        if "`o'" == "z" local w "z ambiguous abbreviation"
        if "`o'" == "int" local w "int not allowed"
        if inlist("`o'", "in", "if", "using", "with") local w "`o' is invalid variable name"
        if "`o'" == "zz nosuch" local w "variable nosuch not found"
        _zjo_pair `tt' `"`v'"' `"sort(`o')"' "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" 198 `"`w'"' "option sort() incorrectly specified"
        if !r(ok) {
            display as error `"JO-22 FAIL: `tt', sort(`o') -- `r(why)'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' JO-22"
}
else display as text "JO-22 PASS: a name that is no usable variable is refused r(198) in twoway's two lines on the 23 serset types"

// JO-23: the 17 other types take sort(nosuch); dash names it in the
// note, except on tsline and tsrline, which join in time order.
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "JO-23"
foreach tt of local jo_oth {
    local v `v_`tt''
    _zjo_pair `tt' `"`v'"' "sort(nosuch)" "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" 0
    local ok = r(ok)
    local note = r(note)
    local why `"`r(why)'"'
    cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle("sort()")
    local named = r(found)
    // Flipped (WP-32): on the fits, kdensity, histogram, function and the
    // immediate types sort(nosuch) was named, which was wrong because
    // twoway draws the same picture with it (noted_option_truth.json;
    // BUGS.md "dash names options twoway takes and draws nothing of, where twoway is silent"): taken in silence there.
    local jo_sil "tsline tsrline pci pcarrowi scatteri lfit qfit lfitci qfitci fpfit fpfitci lowess lpoly lpolyci mspline mband kdensity histogram function"
    if `: list tt in jo_sil' local want = (`note' == 0 & `named' == 0)
    else local want = (`note' == 1 & `named' >= 1)
    if !`ok' | !`want' {
        display as error `"JO-23 FAIL: `tt', sort(nosuch) -- `why', note `note', sort() named `named'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' JO-23"
}
else display as text "JO-23 PASS: the 17 types twoway does not sort take sort(nosuch); named except on tsline and tsrline"

// JO-24: an abbreviation is unabbreviated, and _all where twoway takes it.
local bad = 0
drop zb
cert_truth_ctx "JO-24"
_zjo_pair line "mpg weight" "sort(z)" "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" 0
mata: st_local("hv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "sortvars", "zz")))
if !r(ok) | !`hv' {
    display as error "JO-24 FAIL: sort(z) with zz alone -- `r(why)', sortvars zz `hv'"
    local bad = 1
}
preserve
keep mpg weight zz
cert_truth_ctx "JO-24 three variables"
_zjo_pair line "mpg weight" "sort(_all)" "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" 0
mata: st_local("hv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "sortvars", "mpg weight zz")))
if !r(ok) | !`hv' {
    display as error "JO-24 FAIL: sort(_all) over three variables -- `r(why)', sortvars `hv'"
    local bad = 1
}
restore
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' JO-24"
}
else display as text "JO-24 PASS: sort(z) is written as zz and sort(_all) as every variable, where twoway takes them"

// JO-25: repeated copies, as twoway reads them: the rightmost non-empty
// copy is checked and used.
generate z = -_n
local bad = 0
local k = 0
cert_truth_ctx "JO-25"
foreach o in "sort(x*) sort(z)" "sort(z) sort(x*)" "sort(nosuch) sort(z)" "sort(z) sort(nosuch)" "sort(zz) sort()" "sort() sort(zz)" "sort()" {
    local ++k
    local wrc : word `k' of 0 198 0 198 0 0 0
    local w1 : word `k' of "" "* invalid name" "" "variable nosuch not found" "" "" ""
    local sv : word `k' of "z" "" "z" "" "zz" "zz" ""
    _zjo_pair line "mpg weight" `"`o'"' "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" `wrc' `"`w1'"'
    local ok = r(ok)
    local why `"`r(why)'"'
    local note = r(note)
    if "`sv'" != "" mata: st_local("hv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "sortvars", st_local("sv"))))
    else {
        _ztp_has zqtp sortvars
        local hv = (r(found) == 0)
    }
    if `wrc' != 0 local hv = 1
    if !`ok' | !`hv' | (`wrc' == 0 & `note' != 0) {
        display as error `"JO-25 FAIL: line, `o' -- `why', sortvars `hv', note `note'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
}
quietly tsset t
_zjo_pair tsline "mpg" "sort(x*)" "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" 198 "* invalid name"
if !r(ok) {
    display as error `"JO-25 FAIL: tsline, sort(x*) -- `r(why)'"'
    local bad = 1
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' JO-25"
}
else display as text "JO-25 PASS: of repeated sort() copies the rightmost non-empty one is checked and used, as twoway does"

// JO-26: the note.  Silent on the six joining types and on tsline and
// tsrline; sort() named once on scatter, bar and lfit.
local bad = 0
foreach tt of local jo_six {
    local v `v_`tt''
    foreach o in "sort" "sort(z)" "sort sort(z)" {
        _ztp_run `"dash `tt' `v', `o' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
        if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) != 0 {
            display as error "JO-26 FAIL: `tt', `o' -- rc `r(rc)', note `r(note)' (want none)"
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
}
foreach tt in tsline tsrline {
    _ztp_run `"dash `tt' `v_`tt'', sort(mpg) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) != 0 {
        display as error "JO-26 FAIL: `tt', sort(mpg) -- rc `r(rc)', note `r(note)' (want none)"
        local bad = 1
    }
}
// Flipped (WP-32): lfit left the list: twoway draws a fit the same with
// sort(z), and dash takes it in silence (BUGS.md "dash names options twoway takes and draws nothing of, where twoway is silent").
// Flipped (WP-32): scatter and bar named sort(z), which was wrong because
// twoway draws their marks in z's order and dash now does (BUGS.md "sort on marker types and contour, and heatmap, outlines and alpattern() on contour, are named where twoway draws them").
foreach tt in scatter bar {
    _ztp_run `"dash `tt' mpg weight, sort(z) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle("ignoring unsupported option(s): sort()")
    if `drc' != 0 | r(count) != 0 {
        display as error "JO-26 FAIL: `tt', sort(z) -- rc `drc', `r(count)' note line(s) naming sort() (want 0)"
        local bad = 1
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' JO-26"
}
else display as text "JO-26 PASS: sort and sort() are silent where dash honours them and named once where it does not"

// JO-27: a name given twice.
cert_truth_ctx "JO-27"
_zjo_pair line "mpg weight" "sort(z z)" "`jologtw'" "`logfile'" 0
mata: st_local("hv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "sortvars", "z z")))
if !r(ok) | !`hv' {
    display as error "JO-27 FAIL: sort(z z) -- `r(why)', sortvars z z `hv'"
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' JO-27"
}
else display as text "JO-27 PASS: sort(z z) is taken, as twoway takes it"
drop z zz
capture erase "`jologtw'"
capture dash clear

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-07 -- what twoway refuses dash refuses, naming it as typed.
// Flipped: WP-32 -- dash named each in its note and drew the graph, a rule
// this group pinned; twoway refuses each, r(198), "option xreverse not
// allowed", and so does dash now (BUGS.md "In a few mixed lists dash
// names another word than twoway names first, and an unknown lower-case
// word is noted where twoway refuses it").
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
cert_truth_ctx "TP-07"
foreach o in xreverse yreverse xalternate yalternate xcommon ycommon lockaspect "zoom(2)" altaxis ddensity "addplot(line mpg weight)" "margin(zero)" "region(fcolor(red))" "bargap(10)" {
    local nm = "`o'"
    local pp = strpos("`o'", "(")
    if `pp' local nm = substr("`o'", 1, `pp' - 1)
    capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, `o' nodraw
    local tw_rc = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, `o' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local dnote = r(note)
    local nmp "`nm'"
    if `pp' local nmp "`nm'()"
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `nmp' not allowed"
    local named = r(found)
    if `tw_rc' != 198 | `drc' != 198 | `dnote' != 0 | `named' != 1 {
        display as error "TP-07 FAIL: `nm' -- twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc', note `dnote', named=`named'"
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' TP-07(`nm')"
    }
    else display as text "TP-07 PASS: `nm' is no twoway option; refused as twoway refuses it"
}

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-08 .. TP-11 -- marker labels and marker outlines (the marker-label
// parity work).  twoway is the oracle in every case, asked in this run:
// its rc for the refusals, and for what it DRAWS, the SVG it exports --
// a label is a <text> element holding the label, a red outline is
// stroke:#FF0000 -- against the saved dashboard's own document.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture mata: mata drop _ztp_count()
capture mata: mata drop _ztp_labelsets()
capture mata: mata drop _ztp_redline()
mata:
// How many times `needle' occurs in the file at `path'; -1 if unreadable.
// The whole file is read as one string, so a needle can never straddle a
// line break the reader introduced.
real scalar _ztp_count(string scalar path, string scalar needle)
{
    real scalar   fh, n
    string scalar s
    fh = _fopen(path, "r")
    if (fh < 0) return(-1)
    fseek(fh, 0, 1)
    n = ftell(fh)
    fseek(fh, 0, -1)
    s = (n > 0 ? fread(fh, n) : "")
    fclose(fh)
    if (strlen(needle) == 0) return(0)
    return((strlen(s) - strlen(subinstr(s, needle, "", .))) / strlen(needle))
}
// How many LabelSet models a saved dashboard's document holds.
real scalar _ztp_labelsets(string scalar path)
{
    string scalar q
    q = char(34)
    return(_ztp_count(path, q + "name" + q + ":" + q + "LabelSet" + q))
}
// How many times a saved dashboard names the colour red (#ff0000), in any
// case.  The page's own script holds no such colour, and the probes below
// set no other red, so on a plot with no line every one is an outline --
// a marker glyph writes it as "line_color":{"type":"value","value":...}.
real scalar _ztp_redline(string scalar path)
{
    real scalar   fh, n
    string scalar s
    fh = _fopen(path, "r")
    if (fh < 0) return(-1)
    fseek(fh, 0, 1)
    n = ftell(fh)
    fseek(fh, 0, -1)
    s = (n > 0 ? strlower(fread(fh, n)) : "")
    fclose(fh)
    return((strlen(s) - strlen(subinstr(s, "#ff0000", "", .))) / 7)
}
end

capture program drop _ztp_count
program define _ztp_count, rclass
    args path needle
    mata: st_local("_zc", strofreal(_ztp_count(st_local("path"), st_local("needle"))))
    return scalar n = `_zc'
end

capture program drop _ztp_page
program define _ztp_page, rclass
    args path
    mata: st_local("_zl", strofreal(_ztp_labelsets(st_local("path"))))
    mata: st_local("_zr", strofreal(_ztp_redline(st_local("path"))))
    return scalar labelsets = `_zl'
    return scalar redlines  = `_zr'
end

local svgfile  "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp_marker.svg"
local htmlfile "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp_marker.html"
capture drop zq
generate str12 zq = "ZQLAB" + string(_n)

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-08 -- mlabel() is refused and ignored where twoway refuses and
// ignores it.  twoway reads the label variable as a third plotted
// variable on mspline and mband ("too many variables specified",
// r(103)); it refuses a variable that does not exist, r(111), on every
// type but histogram and function, which never read the option.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
// The immediate types take their labels from the command line, and
// their branch is not this group's subject.
local mtypes "`types' pccapsym"
local _ztp_imm "scatteri pci"
local mtypes : list mtypes - _ztp_imm
quietly tsset t
cert_truth_ctx "TP-08"
foreach tt of local mtypes {
    local v `v_`tt''
    local sep ","
    if strpos("`v'", ",") local sep ""
    foreach lab in make nosuchvar {
        capture graph drop _all
        capture cert_tw twoway `tt' `v'`sep' mlabel(`lab')
        local tw_rc = _rc
        capture graph drop _all
        _ztp_run `"dash (`tt' `v'`sep' mlabel(`lab')), name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
        local drc = r(rc)
        if `drc' != `tw_rc' {
            display as error "TP-08 FAIL `tt': mlabel(`lab') is r(`tw_rc') in twoway, rc `drc' in dash"
            local bad = 1
            continue
        }
        if `drc' == 103 {
            _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "mlabel()"
            if r(found) != 1 {
                display as error "TP-08 FAIL `tt': mlabel(`lab') refused without naming mlabel()"
                local bad = 1
            }
        }
        if `drc' == 0 & "`lab'" == "make" {
            // where twoway never reads it the spec does not carry it;
            // everywhere else the renderer decides what is drawn
            _ztp_has zqtp mlabel
            local want = !inlist("`tt'", "histogram", "function")
            if r(found) != `want' {
                display as error "TP-08 FAIL `tt': the spec carries mlabel = `r(found)', expected `want'"
                local bad = 1
            }
        }
    }
}
quietly tsset, clear
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-08"
}
else display as text "TP-08 PASS: mlabel() refused (r(103), r(111)) and ignored exactly where twoway refuses and ignores it"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-09 -- marker labels are drawn on exactly the plot types twoway
// draws them on: twoway's SVG holds the label text, the saved
// dashboard's document holds a LabelSet.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
// mspline and mband refuse mlabel() (TP-08): nothing to draw.
local _ztp_ref "mspline mband"
local dtypes : list mtypes - _ztp_ref
quietly tsset t
cert_truth_ctx "TP-09"
foreach tt of local dtypes {
    local v `v_`tt''
    local sep ","
    if strpos("`v'", ",") local sep ""
    // twoway's rc, and how many times its SVG holds the first label: asked
    // in a live run, read back otherwise (cert_truth.do).
    local _ct_q "twoway `tt' `v'`sep' mlabel(zq)"
    if `_ct_l' {
        capture erase "`svgfile'"
        capture graph drop _all
        capture twoway `tt' `v'`sep' mlabel(zq)
        local tw_rc = _rc
        if `tw_rc' == 0 cert_svg_export, file("`svgfile'")
        capture graph drop _all
        // WP-28 S02: cert_svg_has_text, through scripts/svg_truth.py, in place
        // of the raw byte search; guarded because it exits 603 on a missing
        // file where the old mata _ztp_count returned -1 (twoway itself
        // failed to draw for this plot type, so no SVG exists to open).
        capture cert_svg_has_text, file("`svgfile'") text("ZQLAB1")
        local tw_n = cond(_rc == 0, r(count), -1)
        local _ct_a "`tw_rc' `tw_n'"
        python: _dct.val_put("rc and svg count of ZQLAB1", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
    }
    else {
        python: _dct.val_get("rc and svg count of ZQLAB1", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
        if "`_ct_a'" == "" local _ct_a "9 -1"
        local tw_rc : word 1 of `_ct_a'
        local tw_n  : word 2 of `_ct_a'
    }
    if `tw_rc' != 0 | `tw_n' < 0 {
        display as error "TP-09 FAIL `tt': the twoway oracle failed, r(`tw_rc')"
        local bad = 1
        continue
    }
    capture erase "`htmlfile'"
    _ztp_run `"dash (`tt' `v'`sep' mlabel(zq)), saving("`htmlfile'")"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    _ztp_page "`htmlfile'"
    local d_n = r(labelsets)
    if `drc' != 0 | `d_n' < 0 {
        display as error "TP-09 FAIL `tt': dash rc `drc', page readable = `=`d_n' >= 0'"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if (`tw_n' > 0) != (`d_n' > 0) {
        display as error "TP-09 FAIL `tt': twoway draws `tw_n' label(s) for the first observation, the saved dashboard holds `d_n' LabelSet(s)"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else display as text "TP-09 `tt': twoway labels the first observation `tw_n' time(s); LabelSets `d_n'"
}
quietly tsset, clear
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-09"
}
else display as text "TP-09 PASS: marker labels drawn on exactly the plot types twoway labels"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-10 -- a value-labelled variable is labelled with its value labels.
// Both labels, as many times as twoway draws each: this checked for at
// least one ZQFOR, and auto has 22 foreign cars, so a mapping that
// labelled only some values, or only some rows, passed -- ZQDOM was never
// looked for.  Measured 24sep2026, twoway's SVG and the saved page alike:
// scatter and pccapsym ZQFOR 22, ZQDOM 52; rscatter 44 and 104 (a label
// at each end).  A label reaches the page once per labelled point, as a
// string in the LabelSet's source.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
capture label drop zqorigin
label define zqorigin 0 "ZQDOM" 1 "ZQFOR"
capture drop zqf
generate zqf = foreign
label values zqf zqorigin
cert_truth_ctx "TP-10"
foreach spec in "scatter mpg weight" "rscatter lo hi weight" "pccapsym mpg weight turn length" {
    gettoken tt : spec
    // twoway's rc, and how many times its SVG holds each value label:
    // asked in a live run, read back otherwise (cert_truth.do).
    local _ct_q "twoway `spec', mlabel(zqf)"
    if `_ct_l' {
        capture erase "`svgfile'"
        capture graph drop _all
        capture twoway `spec', mlabel(zqf)
        local tw_rc = _rc
        if `tw_rc' == 0 cert_svg_export, file("`svgfile'")
        capture graph drop _all
        // WP-28 S02: cert_svg_has_text (guarded as TP-09's is).
        capture cert_svg_has_text, file("`svgfile'") text("ZQFOR")
        local tw_n = cond(_rc == 0, r(count), -1)
        capture cert_svg_has_text, file("`svgfile'") text("ZQDOM")
        local tw_m = cond(_rc == 0, r(count), -1)
        local _ct_a "`tw_rc' `tw_n' `tw_m'"
        python: _dct.val_put("rc and svg counts of ZQFOR ZQDOM", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
    }
    else {
        python: _dct.val_get("rc and svg counts of ZQFOR ZQDOM", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
        if "`_ct_a'" == "" local _ct_a "9 -1 -1"
        local tw_rc : word 1 of `_ct_a'
        local tw_n  : word 2 of `_ct_a'
        local tw_m  : word 3 of `_ct_a'
    }
    capture erase "`htmlfile'"
    _ztp_run `"dash `spec', mlabel(zqf) saving("`htmlfile'")"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    _ztp_count "`htmlfile'" "ZQFOR"
    local d_n = r(n)
    _ztp_count "`htmlfile'" "ZQDOM"
    local d_m = r(n)
    if `tw_rc' != 0 | `tw_n' < 1 | `tw_m' < 1 {
        display as error "TP-10 FAIL `tt': the twoway oracle did not draw both value labels (ZQFOR `tw_n', ZQDOM `tw_m'), r(`tw_rc')"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `drc' != 0 | `d_n' != `tw_n' | `d_m' != `tw_m' {
        display as error "TP-10 FAIL `tt': twoway draws ZQFOR `tw_n' and ZQDOM `tw_m' time(s); the saved dashboard (rc `drc') holds them `d_n' and `d_m' time(s)"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else display as text "TP-10 `tt': ZQFOR `d_n' and ZQDOM `d_m' time(s), as twoway draws them"
}
label values zqf
capture label drop zqorigin
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-10"
}
else display as text "TP-10 PASS: a value-labelled variable is labelled with its value labels"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-11 -- lcolor() never reaches a marker; mlcolor() draws its outline.
// On these types twoway has no line for lcolor() to style: nothing red
// is drawn.  The saved dashboard must draw no red line either.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-11"
foreach spec in "scatter mpg weight" "dot mpg weight" "rscatter lo hi weight" "pcscatter mpg weight turn length" {
    gettoken tt : spec
    foreach o in lcolor mlcolor {
        // twoway's rc, and how many red strokes its SVG holds: asked in a
        // live run, read back otherwise (cert_truth.do).
        local _ct_q "twoway `spec', `o'(red)"
        if `_ct_l' {
            capture erase "`svgfile'"
            capture graph drop _all
            capture twoway `spec', `o'(red)
            local tw_rc = _rc
            if `tw_rc' == 0 cert_svg_export, file("`svgfile'")
            capture graph drop _all
            _ztp_count "`svgfile'" "stroke:#FF0000"
            local tw_n = r(n)
            local _ct_a "`tw_rc' `tw_n'"
            python: _dct.val_put("rc and svg count of stroke:#FF0000", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
        }
        else {
            python: _dct.val_get("rc and svg count of stroke:#FF0000", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
            if "`_ct_a'" == "" local _ct_a "9 -1"
            local tw_rc : word 1 of `_ct_a'
            local tw_n  : word 2 of `_ct_a'
        }
        capture erase "`htmlfile'"
        _ztp_run `"dash `spec', `o'(red) saving("`htmlfile'")"' "`logfile'"
        local drc = r(rc)
        _ztp_page "`htmlfile'"
        local d_n = r(redlines)
        if `tw_rc' != 0 | `tw_n' < 0 | `drc' != 0 | `d_n' < 0 {
            display as error "TP-11 FAIL `tt' `o'(red): twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc'"
            local bad = 1
        }
        else if (`tw_n' > 0) != (`d_n' > 0) {
            display as error "TP-11 FAIL `tt' `o'(red): twoway draws `tw_n' red outline(s), the saved dashboard `d_n' red line(s)"
            local bad = 1
        }
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-11"
}
else display as text "TP-11 PASS: lcolor() leaves the markers alone, mlcolor() draws their outline, as in twoway"
capture erase "`svgfile'"
capture erase "`htmlfile'"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-12 -- adversarial mlabel() values where dash.ado now refuses it
// (CLAUDE.md rule 18).  Bypass: an abbreviation, a repeated name; resource
// exhaustion: four hundred names -- twoway refuses each with r(103), and so
// must dash, registering nothing.  Injection: SMCL in the value is refused
// (twoway r(198) "invalid name"; dash's variable rule says r(111), "not
// found"), echoed as text, never as SMCL, and registers nothing.  A macro
// reference cannot reach dash from a command line: Stata expands it first
// (test_adversarial.cscript P9-04, P9-05).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
local bad = 0
// "Registers nothing" below is read from ${dash_graph_registry}.  The
// control: a command twoway accepts leaves exactly its name there, so an
// empty registry after a refusal is the refusal's doing and not a global
// dash no longer writes (nothing in this file registered-and-checked it
// before 24sep2026, so a renamed global left both checks nothing to see).
_ztp_run `"dash mspline mpg weight, name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "zqtp" {
    display as error "TP-12 FAIL: the control dash mspline mpg weight, name(zqtp) returned rc `r(rc)' and left the registry [${dash_graph_registry}], not [zqtp]"
    local bad = 1
}
local _ztp_long ""
forvalues i = 1/400 {
    local _ztp_long "`_ztp_long' make"
}
cert_truth_ctx "TP-12"
foreach v in "mak" "make make" `"`_ztp_long'"' {
    capture graph drop _all
    capture cert_tw twoway mspline mpg weight, mlabel(`v')
    local tw_rc = _rc
    capture graph drop _all
    _ztp_run `"dash mspline mpg weight, mlabel(`v') name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local shown = substr(`"`v'"', 1, 20)
    if `tw_rc' != 103 | `drc' != 103 {
        display as error `"TP-12 FAIL mlabel(`shown'...): twoway r(`tw_rc'), dash rc `drc'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    if "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
        display as error `"TP-12 FAIL mlabel(`shown'...): the command registered a graph, where twoway refuses it"'
        local bad = 1
    }
}
_ztp_run `"dash mspline mpg weight, mlabel({bf:ZQINJ}) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "{bf:ZQINJ}"
local echoed = r(found)
if `drc' == 0 | `echoed' != 1 | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
    display as error "TP-12 FAIL: mlabel({bf:ZQINJ}) rc `drc', echoed as text = `echoed', registry ${dash_graph_registry}"
    local bad = 1
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-12"
}
else display as text "TP-12 PASS: hostile mlabel() values on mspline are refused as twoway refuses them, echoed as text, and register nothing"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-13 -- the other side of twoway's minimums, and clwidth()'s ceiling.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// test_twoway_option_parity.py reads dash.ado's -syntax- statements for
// each F3 option's minimum abbreviation (the plot parser's ten, the graph
// parser's xoverhangs and yoverhangs) and its rule table for clwidth()'s
// bounds.  TP-02 to TP-06 run the minimums; but the other side of a
// minimum -- the spelling one letter shorter, which twoway does NOT take
// as the option -- was run for cl() alone, never after the paren-mode
// comma, and clwidth()'s 10000 ceiling nowhere (WP-24's first round).
// Measured 24sep2026: with mlaban( rewritten to mlabangle( before
// _dash_parse_plot_opts's -syntax- runs, with xoverhan read as xoverhangs
// before _dash_parse_graph_opts's, and with the rule written
// clwidth=style,0,100000 -- which still holds the text the source test
// looks for -- test_twoway_option_parity.py and TP-01 to TP-12 all stayed
// green.  Every expectation below is twoway's, asked in this run.
local bad = 0

// TP-13a -- comma mode, the plot parser.  Each row: the minimum, the
// spelling one letter shorter, and what dash must make of the minimum --
// a key in the spec (an option it draws) or its full name in the note (one
// it declares and does not draw).  twoway takes the minimum (rc 0) and
// refuses the shorter one, "option ... not allowed", r(198) (measured
// 24sep2026, each on scatter with mlabel(make)); dash names what twoway
// refuses as typed, as TP-07 does, and neither records the option nor
// names its full name.  The minimum is run first, on the same command:
// the control that shows the key and the note can be seen.
local n13 = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-13a"
foreach row in "mlabang(45) mlaban(45) key mlabangle" ///
               "sort(mpg) sor(mpg) key sortvars" ///
               "xoverhang xoverhan key xoverhangs" ///
               "yoverhang yoverhan key yoverhangs" {
    // Flipped (WP-31 D5): the overhangs' minimum was seen by its name in
    // the note; dash draws them now, so it is the spec's key.
    local ++n13
    tokenize `"`row'"'
    local mn "`1'"
    local sh "`2'"
    local kind "`3'"
    local what "`4'"
    // The shorter spelling as dash's note writes an unknown option: its
    // name and "()".
    local shn "`sh'"
    local pp = strpos("`sh'", "(")
    if `pp' local shn = substr("`sh'", 1, `pp' - 1)
    local shn "`shn'()"
    capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) `mn' nodraw
    local tw_mn = _rc
    capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) `sh' nodraw
    local tw_sh = _rc
    if `tw_mn' != 0 | `tw_sh' != 198 {
        display as error "TP-13a FAIL `mn'/`sh': the twoway oracle gives r(`tw_mn') for the minimum and r(`tw_sh') for the shorter spelling, not rc 0 and r(198)"
        local bad = 1
        continue
    }
    // The minimum: taken.
    _ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) `mn' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    if "`kind'" == "key" _ztp_has zqtp `what'
    else                 _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`what'"
    local took = r(found)
    if `drc' != 0 | `took' != 1 {
        display as error "TP-13a FAIL `mn': the minimum is not taken as the option (rc `drc', `kind' `what' seen = `took')"
        local bad = 1
    }
    // One letter shorter: not the option, and refused as typed.
    // Flipped: WP-32 -- dash named it in the note, rc 0; twoway refuses
    // it, r(198), "option mlaban() not allowed", and so does dash now
    // (BUGS.md "In a few mixed lists dash names another word than twoway
    // names first, and an unknown lower-case word is noted where twoway
    // refuses it").
    local shr "`shn'"
    if !`pp' local shr "`sh'"
    _ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) `sh' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local dnote = r(note)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `shr' not allowed"
    local named = r(found)
    if "`kind'" == "key" _ztp_has zqtp `what'
    else                 _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`what'"
    local took = r(found)
    if `drc' != 198 | `dnote' != 0 | `named' != 1 | `took' != 0 {
        display as error "TP-13a FAIL `sh': twoway r(198) -- dash rc `drc', note `dnote', refused naming `shr' `named', taken as `what' `took'"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else display as text "TP-13a `sh': not `what' -- refused naming `shr', as twoway refuses it"
}
assert `n13' == 4
// mlab() is mlabel()'s own abbreviation in twoway, and one letter short of
// mlabf, mlabt and mlabv: mlab(pos) draws pos's labels, rc 0, and
// mlab(heading) is r(111), no variable heading (measured 24sep2026).  So
// dash must read it as mlabel() and never as mlabformat(),
// mlabtextstyle() or mlabvposition().  The controls: mlabf(%9.2f)
// records mlabformat, and mlabt(heading) and mlabv(pos) are recorded as
// mlabtextstyle and mlabvposition and not named.
// Flipped (WP-30 P1.24): c2v expected 1 (named), which was wrong because
// dash draws mlabvposition() per row as twoway does.
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabf(%9.2f) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local c1 = r(rc)
_ztp_has zqtp mlabformat
local c1k = r(found)
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabt(heading) mlabv(pos) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local c2 = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "mlabtextstyle()"
local c2t = r(found)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "mlabvposition()"
local c2v = r(found)
mata: st_local("c2vk", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "mlabvposition", "pos")))
// Flipped (WP-30 P1.24, part 2): c2t expected 1 (named), which was wrong
// because dash draws mlabtextstyle() as twoway does.
mata: st_local("c2tk", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "mlabtextstyle", "heading")))
if `c1' != 0 | `c1k' != 1 | `c2' != 0 | `c2t' != 0 | `c2tk' != 1 | `c2v' != 0 | `c2vk' != 1 {
    display as error "TP-13a FAIL: the mlab controls -- mlabf(%9.2f) rc `c1' key `c1k'; mlabt() mlabv() rc `c2', named `c2t' `c2v', mlabtextstyle heading `c2tk', mlabvposition pos `c2vk'"
    local bad = 1
}
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlab(pos) nodraw
local tw_p = _rc
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlab(pos) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
local dnote = r(note)
mata: st_local("_zv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zqtp", "mlabel", "pos")))
_ztp_has zqtp mlabformat
local fk = r(found)
if `tw_p' != 0 | `drc' != 0 | `dnote' != 0 | `_zv' != 1 | `fk' != 0 {
    display as error "TP-13a FAIL mlab(pos): twoway r(`tw_p'); dash rc `drc', a note `dnote', mlabel=pos `_zv', mlabformat key `fk'"
    local bad = 1
}
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, mlab(heading) nodraw
local tw_h = _rc
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlab(heading) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "mlabel()"
local named = r(found)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "mlabtextstyle()"
local tsn = r(found)
if `tw_h' != 111 | `drc' != `tw_h' | `named' != 1 | `tsn' != 0 | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
    display as error "TP-13a FAIL mlab(heading): twoway r(`tw_h'); dash rc `drc', mlabel() named `named', mlabtextstyle() named `tsn', registry [${dash_graph_registry}]"
    local bad = 1
}
else display as text "TP-13a mlab(): read as mlabel(), as twoway reads it -- never mlabformat(), mlabtextstyle() or mlabvposition()"

// TP-13b -- after the paren-mode comma, the graph parser: xoverhang and
// yoverhang are taken (TP-06 ran yoverhangs only by its full name there),
// xoverhan and yoverhan are refused by twoway, r(198), and named as typed
// by dash (measured 24sep2026).
local n13b = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-13b"
foreach row in "xoverhang xoverhangs() 0" "yoverhang yoverhangs() 0" ///
               "xoverhan xoverhangs() 198" "yoverhan yoverhangs() 198" {
    local ++n13b
    tokenize "`row'"
    local o "`1'"
    local full "`2'"
    local want "`3'"
    capture cert_tw twoway (scatter mpg weight) (line mpg weight), `o' nodraw
    local tw_rc = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash (scatter mpg weight) (line mpg weight), `o' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local dnote = r(note)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`full'"
    local fulln = r(found)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `o' not allowed"
    local asis = r(found)
    if `want' == 198 & !`asis' local drc -1
    local fullk = subinstr("`full'", "()", "", 1)
    _ztp_has zqtp `fullk'
    local haskey = r(found)
    if `tw_rc' != `want' {
        display as error "TP-13b FAIL `o': the twoway oracle gives r(`tw_rc'), not r(`want')"
        local bad = 1
    }
    // Flipped (WP-31 D5): the minimum was named in the note; it is drawn,
    // so it is the spec's key and named by nothing.
    else if `want' == 0 & (`drc' != 0 | `fulln' != 0 | !`haskey') {
        display as error "TP-13b FAIL `o': the minimum is not taken as `full' (rc `drc', note `dnote', named `fulln')"
        local bad = 1
    }
    // Flipped: WP-32 -- the shorter spelling was named in the note, rc 0;
    // it is refused as twoway refuses it, "option xoverhan not allowed".
    else if `want' == 198 & (`drc' != 198 | `dnote' != 0 | `fulln' != 0) {
        display as error "TP-13b FAIL `o': twoway r(198) -- dash rc `drc', note `dnote', named as typed `asis', named `full' `fulln'"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else display as text "TP-13b `o': r(`tw_rc') in twoway; dash " cond(`want', "refuses `o'", "takes `full'")
}
assert `n13b' == 4

// TP-13c -- clwidth() has lwidth()'s bounds, both ends.  On line, which
// draws the connecting line, twoway draws 0 and 10000 and refuses -0.001
// and 10000.001, "gm_linewidth must be between 0.000 and 1.0e+04", r(198),
// for clwidth() and lwidth() alike (measured 24sep2026; nodraw would not
// ask, the bound is checked when drawn).  dash's rc must be twoway's, a
// refusal must name the option, and the two options must agree.
local n13c = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-13c"
foreach v in -0.001 0 10000 10000.001 {
    foreach o in clwidth lwidth {
        local ++n13c
        capture graph drop _all
        capture cert_tw twoway line mpg weight, `o'(`v')
        local tw_`o' = _rc
        capture graph drop _all
        _ztp_run `"dash (line mpg weight, `o'(`v')), name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
        local d_`o' = r(rc)
        local nm_`o' = 1
        if `d_`o'' == 198 {
            _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`o'()"
            local nm_`o' = r(found)
        }
    }
    local wantv = cond(`v' < 0 | `v' > 10000, 198, 0)
    if `tw_clwidth' != `wantv' | `tw_lwidth' != `wantv' {
        display as error "TP-13c FAIL `v': the twoway oracle gives clwidth r(`tw_clwidth') and lwidth r(`tw_lwidth'), not r(`wantv')"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `d_clwidth' != `tw_clwidth' | `d_lwidth' != `tw_lwidth' | `nm_clwidth' != 1 | `nm_lwidth' != 1 {
        display as error "TP-13c FAIL `v': twoway r(`wantv') -- dash clwidth rc `d_clwidth' (named `nm_clwidth'), lwidth rc `d_lwidth' (named `nm_lwidth')"
        local bad = 1
    }
    else display as text "TP-13c `v': r(`wantv') for clwidth() and lwidth(), in twoway and dash"
}
assert `n13c' == 8
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-13"
}
else display as text "TP-13 PASS: a spelling one letter short of twoway's minimum is not the option, in either parser, and clwidth() stops at lwidth()'s ceiling, as in twoway"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-14 -- an option given more than once (BUGS.md, S3).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// twoway takes most options more than once ([G-4] Concept: repeated
// options): a rightmost one draws its last copy, a merged one -- title(),
// xlabel(), legend(), xscale(), by(), the regions -- joins its copies, and
// a unique one refuses the second, "option scheme() not allowed", r(198).
// dash kept the FIRST copy and named the rest as unsupported (or bound a
// second title() to title2() and a second xlabel() to xlabel2()).
//
// TP-14a: each row is a command R and a command E that twoway draws the
// same: their SVG exports are compared here, byte for byte, on every run.
// dash must then register the same graph for R as for E -- the stored
// spec compared whole -- and name nothing R gives twice.  Measured
// 24sep2026, and asserted below: every R draws what its E draws.
local r1  `"scatter mpg weight, mcolor(red) mcolor(blue)"'
local e1  `"scatter mpg weight, mcolor(blue)"'
local r2  `"scatter mpg weight, mc(red) mcolor(blue)"'
local e2  `"scatter mpg weight, mcolor(blue)"'
local r3  `"scatter mpg weight, mcolor(red) mc(blue)"'
local e3  `"scatter mpg weight, mc(blue)"'
local r4  `"scatter mpg weight, msymbol(O) msymbol(T)"'
local e4  `"scatter mpg weight, msymbol(T)"'
local r5  `"scatter mpg weight, msize(small) msize(huge)"'
local e5  `"scatter mpg weight, msize(huge)"'
local r6  `"line mpg weight, lcolor(red) lcolor(blue)"'
local e6  `"line mpg weight, lcolor(blue)"'
local r7  `"line mpg weight, lwidth(thin) lwidth(vthick)"'
local e7  `"line mpg weight, lwidth(vthick)"'
local r8  `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabel(rep78)"'
local e8  `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(rep78)"'
local r9  `"scatter mpg weight, jitter(1) jitter(8)"'
local e9  `"scatter mpg weight, jitter(8)"'
local r10 `"scatter mpg weight, mcolor(bogus) mcolor(red)"'
local e10 `"scatter mpg weight, mcolor(red)"'
local r11 `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(nosuchvar) mlabel(make)"'
local e11 `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make)"'
local r12 `"(scatter mpg weight, mcolor(red) mcolor(blue)), title(T)"'
local e12 `"(scatter mpg weight, mcolor(blue)), title(T)"'
local r13 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A) title(B)"'
local e13 `"scatter mpg weight, title(B)"'
local r14 `"scatter mpg weight, ti(A) title(B)"'
local e14 `"scatter mpg weight, title(B)"'
local r15 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A) title(, color(red))"'
local e15 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A, color(red))"'
local r16 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A, color(red)) title(B)"'
local e16 `"scatter mpg weight, title(B, color(red))"'
local r17 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A, color(red)) title(B, color(blue))"'
local e17 `"scatter mpg weight, title(B, color(blue))"'
local r18 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A) title(B, suffix)"'
local e18 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A B)"'
local r19 `"scatter mpg weight, xtitle(A) xtitle(B)"'
local e19 `"scatter mpg weight, xtitle(B)"'
local r20 `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(2000 3000) xlabel(4000 5000)"'
local e20 `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(4000 5000)"'
local r21 `"scatter mpg weight, xla(2000 3000) xlabel(4000 5000)"'
local e21 `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(4000 5000)"'
local r22 `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(2000 3000) xlabel(, angle(45))"'
local e22 `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(2000 3000, angle(45))"'
local r23 `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(2000 3000) xlabel(4000, add)"'
local e23 `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(2000 3000 4000)"'
local r24 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(off) legend(on)"'
local e24 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(on)"'
local r25 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(label(1 "A")) legend(label(2 "B"))"'
local e25 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(label(1 "A") label(2 "B"))"'
local r26 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(cols(1)) legend(rows(1))"'
local e26 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(rows(1))"'
local r27 `"scatter mpg weight, xscale(log) xscale(range(1000 6000))"'
local e27 `"scatter mpg weight, xscale(log range(1000 6000))"'
local r28 `"scatter mpg weight, graphregion(color(red)) graphregion(margin(zero))"'
local e28 `"scatter mpg weight, graphregion(color(red) margin(zero))"'
local r29 `"scatter mpg weight, by(foreign) by(, cols(1))"'
local e29 `"scatter mpg weight, by(foreign, cols(1))"'
local r30 `"(scatter mpg weight, title(A)), title(, color(red))"'
local e30 `"(scatter mpg weight), title(A, color(red))"'
local r31 `"(scatter mpg weight, legend(label(1 "A"))) (scatter price weight), legend(label(2 "B"))"'
local e31 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(label(1 "A") label(2 "B"))"'
local r32 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A) || scatter price weight, title(B)"'
local e32 `"scatter mpg weight || scatter price weight, title(B)"'
local r33 `"(scatter mpg weight, title(INSIDE)) (line mpg weight), title(AFTER)"'
local e33 `"(scatter mpg weight) (line mpg weight), title(AFTER)"'
// Rows 34-39 (WP-30 P1.19): copies merge sub-option by sub-option under
// twoway's full names.
local r34 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(lab(1 "A")) legend(lab(2 "B"))"'
local e34 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(lab(1 "A") lab(2 "B"))"'
local r35 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(c(1)) legend(r(1))"'
local e35 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(r(1))"'
local r36 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(posi(9)) legend(pos(3))"'
local e36 `"(scatter mpg weight) (scatter price weight), legend(pos(3))"'
local r37 `"scatter mpg weight, ylabel(, labs(large)) ylabel(, labsize(small))"'
local e37 `"scatter mpg weight, ylabel(, labsize(small))"'
local r38 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A, s(large)) title(, size(small))"'
local e38 `"scatter mpg weight, title(A, size(small))"'
local r39 `"scatter mpg weight, xscale(r(1000 3000)) xscale(range(2000 6000))"'
local e39 `"scatter mpg weight, xscale(range(1000 6000))"'
local n14 39
local bad = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-14a"
forvalues k = 1/`n14' {
    foreach w in r e {
        // twoway's rc and its SVG export's checksum: asked in a live run,
        // read back otherwise (cert_truth.do).
        local _ct_q `"twoway ``w'`k''"'
        if `_ct_l' {
            capture graph drop _all
            capture twoway ``w'`k''
            local _ct_rc = _rc
            local _ct_ck ""
            if !`_ct_rc' {
                quietly graph export "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_`w'.svg", replace
                quietly checksum "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_`w'.svg"
                local _ct_ck = r(checksum)
            }
            local _ct_a "`_ct_rc' `_ct_ck'"
            python: _dct.val_put("rc and svg checksum", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
        }
        else {
            python: _dct.val_get("rc and svg checksum", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
            if "`_ct_a'" == "" local _ct_a 9
        }
        local _ct_rc : word 1 of `_ct_a'
        if `_ct_rc' {
            display as error "TP-14a FAIL row `k': twoway refused the `w' command, r(`_ct_rc')"
            local bad = 1
            continue
        }
        local ck_`w' : word 2 of `_ct_a'
        _ztp_run `"dash ``w'`k'' name(zq14)"' "`logfile'"
        local rc_`w' = r(rc)
        local note_`w' = r(note)
        mata: st_local("js_`w'", st_global("dash_json_zq14"))
    }
    if "`ck_r'" != "`ck_e'" {
        display as error `"TP-14a FAIL row `k': twoway no longer draws `r`k'' as `e`k''"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    else if `rc_r' | `rc_e' {
        display as error `"TP-14a FAIL row `k': dash r(`rc_r') for `r`k'', r(`rc_e') for `e`k''"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    else {
        mata: st_local("same", strofreal(st_local("js_r") == st_local("js_e")))
        if !`same' | `note_r' != `note_e' {
            display as error `"TP-14a FAIL row `k': dash registers `r`k'' (note `note_r') apart from `e`k'' (note `note_e')"'
            local bad = 1
        }
        else display as text `"TP-14a row `k': `r`k'' is `e`k'', in twoway and in dash"'
    }
}
capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_r.svg"
capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_e.svg"

// TP-14b: a unique option given twice -- in one list, spelled twice, in
// two plot groups, beside the one after the comma, in two || segments --
// is refused as twoway refuses it, in twoway's words and with its code,
// and nothing is registered.
local u1  `"scatter mpg weight, scheme(s1mono) scheme(s2color)"'
local m1  "option scheme() not allowed"
local u2  `"scatter mpg weight, sch(s1mono) scheme(s2color)"'
local m2  "option scheme() not allowed"
local u3  `"scatter mpg weight, xsize(3) xsize(4)"'
local m3  "option xsize() not allowed"
local u4  `"scatter mpg weight, aspectratio(1) aspectratio(0.5)"'
local m4  "option aspectratio() not allowed"
local u5  `"line mpg weight, sort sort"'
local m5  "option sort not allowed"
local u6  `"kdensity mpg, bwidth(1) bwid(2)"'
local m6  "option bwid() not allowed"
local u7  `"histogram mpg, percent percent"'
local m7  "option percent not allowed"
local u8  `"lpoly mpg weight, n(50) n(60)"'
local m8  "option n() not allowed"
local u9  `"(scatter mpg weight, scheme(s1mono)), scheme(s2color)"'
local m9  "option scheme() not allowed"
local u10 `"(scatter mpg weight, xsize(3)) (scatter price weight, xsize(4)), title(T)"'
local m10 "option xsize() not allowed"
local u11 `"scatter mpg weight, xsize(3) || scatter price weight, xsize(4)"'
local m11 "option xsize() not allowed"
local u12 `"scatter mpg weight, yaxis(1) yaxis(1)"'
local m12 "option yaxis() not allowed"
cert_truth_ctx "TP-14b"
forvalues k = 1/12 {
    capture graph drop _all
    capture noisily cert_tw twoway `u`k'' nodraw
    local tw = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash `u`k'' name(zq14u)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`m`k''"
    local said = r(found)
    if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | !`said' | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
        display as error `"TP-14b FAIL `u`k'': twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), "`m`k''" said `said'"'
        local bad = 1
    }
    else display as text `"TP-14b `k': `u`k'' refused, r(198), "`m`k''""'
}
// A bare sort and sort(varlist) are two options to -syntax- and one to
// twoway, which takes them together in either order (rc 0, measured
// 24sep2026): not a unique option given twice.
foreach o in "sort(mpg) sort" "sort sort(mpg)" {
    capture cert_tw twoway line mpg weight, `o' nodraw
    local tw = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, `o' name(zq14s)"' "`logfile'"
    if `tw' | r(rc) {
        display as error "TP-14b FAIL `o': twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`r(rc)')"
        local bad = 1
    }
}

// Q3506-2 (WP-35 GW-2): aspectratio() with xoverhangs or yoverhangs --
// after the comma, in a group, in two groups, across ||, under by(), the
// shortest aspect() -- is refused as twoway refuses it, r(198), "may not
// combine option aspectratio() with xoverhangs or yoverhangs", on the
// one-line route and with name(), and nothing is registered; either alone
// is drawn.  twoway's rc and first line are the fixture's
// (test/fixtures/graph_refusal_truth.json asp.*, every key).  Its own
// tally, beside TP-14's.
python:
import json as _q35062_json
from sfi import Macro as _q35062_M
_q35062_fx = _q35062_json.load(open("fixtures/graph_refusal_truth.json", encoding="utf-8"))
_q35062_M.setLocal("q2keys", " ".join(sorted(k for k in _q35062_fx if k.startswith("asp."))))


def _q35062_take(key):
    r = _q35062_fx[key]
    c = r["cmd"].strip()
    if c.startswith("twoway "):
        c = c[len("twoway "):]
    _q35062_M.setLocal("q2c", c.replace(" name(zg1, replace)", "").rstrip())
    _q35062_M.setLocal("q2tw", str(r["rc"]))
    _q35062_M.setLocal("q2m", r["first"])
end
local q2bad 0
foreach q2k of local q2keys {
    python: import __main__ as _q35062_main; _q35062_main._q35062_take("`q2k'")
    foreach q2r in line named {
        if "`q2r'" == "line" {
            _ztp_run `"dash `q2c' nodraw"' "`logfile'"
        }
        else _ztp_run `"dash `q2c' name(zq3506)"' "`logfile'"
        local rc = r(rc)
        local said 0
        if `q2tw' {
            _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`q2m'"
            local said = r(found)
        }
        if `rc' != `q2tw' | (`q2tw' & (!`said' | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "")) {
            display as error `"Q3506-2 FAIL `q2k' (`q2r'): twoway r(`q2tw'), dash r(`rc'), said `said'"'
            local q2bad 1
        }
        else display as text `"Q3506-2 `q2k' (`q2r'): r(`rc') as twoway"'
    }
}
capture dash clear
if `q2bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' Q3506-2"
}
else display as text "Q3506-2 PASS: aspectratio() with an overhang refused as twoway refuses it"

// TP-14c: both routes.  The command drawn at once saves the page of the
// last title(); the command registered with name() and drawn by dash build
// saves the same.  Neither names the repeat.
capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_imm.html"
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, title(FirstTitle) title(LastTitle) saving("`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_imm.html", replace)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
local note = r(note)
cert_file_has "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_imm.html", needle("LastTitle")
local last = r(found)
cert_file_has "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_imm.html", needle("FirstTitle")
if `rc' | `note' | !`last' | r(found) {
    display as error "TP-14c FAIL immediate: rc `rc', note `note', last title `last', first title `r(found)'"
    local bad = 1
}
capture dash clear
capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_bld.html"
capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, name(zq14b) mc(red) title(FirstTitle) mcolor(blue) title(LastTitle)
local rc1 = _rc
capture noisily dash build, saving("`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_bld.html") replace
local rc2 = _rc
mata: st_local("js", st_global("dash_json_zq14b"))
local blue = strpos(`"`macval(js)'"', `""mcolor":"blue""') > 0
cert_file_has "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_bld.html", needle("LastTitle")
local last = r(found)
cert_file_has "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_bld.html", needle("FirstTitle")
if `rc1' | `rc2' | !`blue' | !`last' | r(found) {
    display as error "TP-14c FAIL build: rc `rc1'/`rc2', blue `blue', last title `last', first title `r(found)'"
    local bad = 1
}
capture dash clear
capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_imm.html"
capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp14_bld.html"

// TP-14d: xline()/yline() copies stay apart: the spec holds each copy,
// comma-separated, and the renderer draws each in its own style
// (test_axis_options.py TestReferenceLines).
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, yline(20, lcolor(red)) yline(30) name(zq14y)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
local note = r(note)
local ok = 0
if !`rc' {
    mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zq14y", "yline", "20, lcolor(red), 30")))
}
if `rc' | `note' | !`ok' {
    display as error "TP-14d FAIL: rc `rc', note `note', spec yline `ok'"
    local bad = 1
}

// TP-14e: adversarial (CLAUDE.md rule 18).  Resource exhaustion: an
// option given 10,000 times is "too many options", r(1003), in twoway and
// dash alike, and quickly; 128 copies of mcolor() among 255 options -- the
// most twoway takes with nodraw, and dash with name() -- draw the last, as
// do 127 copies of title(), quickly.  Injection: a hostile value in a
// repeat is stored as text, its macro characters escaped, never run; a copy whose value Stata cannot
// bind is refused with twoway's code as before (P20-18b), and a copy that
// only looks like another option inside a title() is text.
cert_truth_ctx "TP-14e"
local many ""
forvalues i = 1/10000 {
    local many "`many' mcolor(blue)"
}
timer clear 14
timer on 14
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, `many' nodraw
local tw = _rc
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, name(zq14x) `many'"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
timer off 14
quietly timer list 14
if `tw' != 1003 | `rc' != 1003 | r(t14) >= 10 | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
    display as error "TP-14e FAIL 10000 copies: twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), `r(t14)' s"
    local bad = 1
}
local many ""
forvalues i = 1/127 {
    local many "`many' mcolor(red) title(T`i')"
}
local many "`many' mcolor(blue)"
timer clear 14
timer on 14
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, `many' nodraw
local tw = _rc
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, `many' name(zq14x)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
local note = r(note)
timer off 14
quietly timer list 14
local ok = 0
if !`rc' {
    mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zq14x", "mcolor", "blue") & _ztp_hasval("zq14x", "title", "T127")))
}
if `tw' | `rc' | `note' | !`ok' | r(t14) >= 10 {
    display as error "TP-14e FAIL 255 copies: twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), note `note', last `ok', `r(t14)' s"
    local bad = 1
}
// A hostile value: SMCL, a global's name, a local's quotes, compound
// quotes.  Typed on the command line with macval(), as a user's do-file
// would hand it over unexpanded.
local hv = "{bf:B} " + char(36) + "S_ADO " + char(96) + "c(pwd)" + char(39) + " " + char(96) + char(34) + "q" + char(34) + char(39)
capture dash clear
capture log close _ztplog
quietly log using "`logfile'", name(_ztplog) text replace
capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, title(safe) title(`"`macval(hv)'"') name(zq14h)
local rc = _rc
quietly log close _ztplog
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "ignoring unsupported"
local note = r(found)
mata: st_local("js", st_global("dash_json_zq14h"))
// Flipped (WP-31 D13b): $S_ADO is the global's value, as twoway reads a
// graph text option again (global_text_truth.json); the local's quotes
// stay text and nothing is run.
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(strpos(st_local("js"), "{bf:B} ") > 0 & !strpos(st_local("js"), "\u0024S_ADO") & strpos(st_local("js"), " \u0060c(pwd)\u0027") > 0 & !strpos(st_local("js"), "safe")))
if `rc' | `note' | !`ok' {
    display as error "TP-14e FAIL hostile value: rc `rc', note `note', stored as text `ok'"
    local bad = 1
}
// A copy Stata cannot bind: refused as twoway refuses it, no directive run.
local brk = "x" + char(34) + char(39) + " _dup(3) " + char(34) + "INJ" + char(34) + " " + char(96) + char(34)
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, jitter(1) jitter(`brk') nodraw
local tw = _rc
capture dash clear
quietly log using "`logfile'", name(_ztplog) text replace
capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, jitter(1) jitter(`brk') name(zq14h)
local rc = _rc
quietly log close _ztplog
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "INJINJINJ"
if `rc' != `tw' | !inlist(`tw', 109, 198) | r(found) | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
    display as error "TP-14e FAIL unbindable copy: twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), directive run `r(found)'"
    local bad = 1
}
// An option's name inside a title's text is text, not a second copy.
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, title("scheme(s1mono) mcolor(red)") mcolor(blue) scheme(s2color) name(zq14h)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zq14h", "mcolor", "blue")))
if `rc' | !`ok' {
    display as error "TP-14e FAIL option text inside a title: rc `rc', mcolor blue `ok'"
    local bad = 1
}

// TP-14f: a repeated option dash does not declare (BUGS.md, S3).  twoway
// refuses the second copy of some of the options dash names in its note
// -- atobs, nofit, clegend(), nodropbase and the rest measured 24sep2026
// beside _dash_rep_und_tab in dash_parse.mata -- "option atobs not
// allowed", r(198), naming the second copy as typed, or the noX copy of an
// X and noX pair; dash named both copies in the note.  Each row is asked
// of twoway in this run, under a log, and dash must give twoway's code and
// words, and register nothing.  x<k> is the code measured: the run fails
// if twoway no longer gives it.
local f1  `"lfit mpg weight, atobs atobs"'
local g1  "option atobs not allowed"
local f2  `"lfit mpg weight, ato atobs"'
local g2  "option atobs not allowed"
local f3  `"qfitci mpg weight, atobs ato"'
local g3  "option ato not allowed"
local f4  `"lfitci mpg weight, nofit nofit"'
local g4  "option nofit not allowed"
local f5  `"lpolyci mpg weight, fit nofit"'
local g5  "option nofit not allowed"
local f6  `"lfitci mpg weight, nofit fit"'
local g6  "option nofit not allowed"
local f7  `"kdensity mpg, gaussian gaussian"'
local g7  "option gaussian not allowed"
local f8  `"kdensity mpg, boundary boundary"'
local g8  "option boundary not allowed"
local f9  `"lpolyci mpg weight, var(1) v(2)"'
local g9  "option v() not allowed"
local f10 `"rbar lo hi weight, baroffset(1) baroffset(2)"'
local g10 "option baroffset() not allowed"
local f11 `"scatter mpg weight, nodropbase nodropbase"'
local g11 "option nodropbase not allowed"
local f12 `"line mpg weight, dropbase nodropbase"'
local g12 "option nodropbase not allowed"
local f13 `"scatter mpg weight, clegend(red) clegend(blue)"'
local g13 "option clegend() not allowed"
local f14 `"scatter mpg weight, colorstart(red) colorst(blue)"'
local g14 "option colorst() not allowed"
local f15 `"pcspike mpg weight turn length, headlabel headlabel"'
local g15 "option headlabel not allowed"
local f16 `"pcarrowi 20 3000 30 4000, headlabel headlabel"'
local g16 "option headlabel not allowed"
local f17 `"tsline mpg, onepanel onepanel"'
local g17 "option onepanel not allowed"
local f18 `"mspline mpg weight, noback noback"'
local g18 "option noback not allowed"
local f19 `"lowess mpg weight, w weight"'
local g19 "option weight not allowed"
local f20 `"histogram mpg, mwidth mwidth"'
local g20 "option mwidth not allowed"
local f21 `"kdensity mpg, epan2 epan2"'
local g21 "option epan2 not allowed"
local f22 `"lfit mpg weight, atobs mcolor(red) atobs"'
local g22 "option atobs not allowed"
local f23 `"qfit mpg weight, xlog xlog"'
local g23 "option xlog not allowed"
local f24 `"scatter mpg weight, log log"'
local g24 "option log not allowed"
local f25 `"scatter mpg weight, nologging logging"'
local g25 "option nologging not allowed"
local f26 `"scatter mpg weight, titling notitling"'
local g26 "option notitling not allowed"
local f27 `"(scatter mpg weight), clegend(red) clegend(red)"'
local g27 "option clegend() not allowed"
local f28 `"(scatter mpg weight, plegend(red)), plegend(red)"'
local g28 "option plegend() not allowed"
local f29 `"(scatter mpg weight, notitling) (scatter price weight, notitling), title(T)"'
local g29 "option notitling not allowed"
local f30 `"scatter mpg weight, pcycle(2) || scatter price weight, pcycle(2)"'
local g30 "option pcycle() not allowed"
local f31 `"(scatter mpg weight, below) (line mpg weight, below), title(T)"'
local g31 "option below not allowed"
local f32 `"scatter mpg weight, colorvarminmax colorvarminmax"'
local g32 "option colorvarminmax not allowed"
local n14f 32
forvalues k = 1/`n14f' {
    local x`k' 198
}
// Taken more than once by twoway, so named in the note as before: the
// same word on a type that takes it again (dlalign() on dot), a plot
// option in two plot groups or two || segments, and two options each
// given once.
// Flipped (WP-31 C5): rows 33 and 38 were bar's baroffset() and
// scatter's nodropbase, which was wrong once dash draws the one and takes
// the other in silence where twoway draws nothing different; dot's
// baroffset(), which dash does not draw yet, and rbar's stand in.
// Flipped (WP-31 B5b): row 33's dot baroffset() was wrong because twoway
// draws nothing different with it on dot (dot_truth.json D28, D29), so
// dash takes it in silence; dot's dlalign(), which dash names, stands in.
// Flipped (WP-32): dlalign() is taken in silence on dot, as twoway draws
// dot the same with it (BUGS.md "dash names options twoway takes and draws nothing of, where twoway is silent");
// the row expects it drawn in silence.
local f33 `"dot mpg weight, dlalign(inside) dlalign(outside)"'
local g33 "dlalign()"
local s33 1
// Flipped (WP-31 C4): rows 34 and 35 expected atobs and nofit named in
// the note, which was wrong once dash draws them; twoway's answer is the
// same, and dash now draws both layers in silence (s34, s35).
local f34 `"(lfit mpg weight, atobs) (lfit price weight, atobs), title(T)"'
local g34 "atobs"
local s34 1
local f35 `"lfitci mpg weight, nofit || lfitci price weight, nofit"'
local g35 "nofit"
local s35 1
local f36 `"scatter mpg weight, clegend(red) plegend(red)"'
local g36 "clegend() plegend()"
local f37 `"(scatter mpg weight, colorstart(red)) (scatter price weight, colorstart(red)), title(T)"'
local g37 "colorstart()"
// Flipped (WP-31 C8b): rows 36 and 37 named in the note was wrong,
// because dash draws clegend(), plegend() and colorstart() as twoway does
// (colorvar_options_truth.json); taken once, drawn in silence.
local s36 1
local s37 1
local f38 `"rbar mpg price weight, baroffset(1)"'
local g38 "baroffset()"
// Flipped (WP-32): row 38's baroffset() named on rbar was wrong, because
// twoway moves rbar's bars as bar's and dash now draws them so (BUGS.md "Options twoway draws that dash still names...").
local s38 1
forvalues k = 33/38 {
    local x`k' 0
}
// log is logging on lowess too, though lowess's own logit is spelled lo:
// twoway takes the graph's options out first.  An X and noX pair names
// the noX copy, whichever comes second.
local f39 `"lowess mpg weight, log logging"'
local g39 "option logging not allowed"
local f40 `"scatter mpg weight, nodropb dropb"'
local g40 "option nodropb not allowed"
local x39 198
local x40 198
local n14f 40
capture drop _t14f
generate _t14f = _n
quietly tsset _t14f
cert_truth_ctx "TP-14f"
forvalues k = 1/`n14f' {
    capture graph drop _all
    _ztp_run `"twoway `f`k'' nodraw"' "`logfile'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    local twsaid 1
    if `x`k'' {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`g`k''"
        local twsaid = r(found)
    }
    _ztp_run `"dash `f`k'' name(zq14f)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    local note = r(note)
    if `tw' != `x`k'' | !`twsaid' {
        display as error `"TP-14f FAIL row `k': twoway gave r(`tw') (said "`g`k''": `twsaid') for `f`k'', not r(`x`k'') as measured"'
        local bad = 1
        continue
    }
    if `x`k'' {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`g`k''"
        local said = r(found)
        if `rc' != 198 | !`said' | `note' | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
            display as error `"TP-14f FAIL row `k': `f`k'': dash r(`rc'), "`g`k''" said `said', note `note', registry ${dash_graph_registry}"'
            local bad = 1
        }
        else display as text `"TP-14f row `k': `f`k'' refused, r(198), "`g`k''""'
    }
    else if "`s`k''" == "1" {
        if `rc' | `note' {
            display as error `"TP-14f FAIL row `k': `f`k'': dash r(`rc'), note `note' (drawn in silence expected)"'
            local bad = 1
        }
        else display as text `"TP-14f row `k': `f`k'' drawn, "`g`k''" honoured"'
    }
    else {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "ignoring unsupported option(s): `g`k''"
        local said = r(found)
        if `rc' | !`note' | !`said' {
            display as error `"TP-14f FAIL row `k': `f`k'': dash r(`rc'), note `note', naming "`g`k''" `said'"'
            local bad = 1
        }
        else display as text `"TP-14f row `k': `f`k'' drawn, "`g`k''" named in the note"'
    }
}
// Adversarial (CLAUDE.md rule 18).  Injection: a hostile value in the
// repeated option -- SMCL, a global's name, a local's quotes, compound
// quotes, a directive -- is refused naming the option alone: the value is
// never echoed, expanded or run, and nothing is registered.
local hv = "{bf:B} " + char(36) + "S_ADO " + char(96) + "c(pwd)" + char(39) + " _dup(3) " + char(96) + char(34) + "INJ" + char(34) + char(39)
capture graph drop _all
capture cert_tw twoway scatter mpg weight, colorotherlabel(`"`macval(hv)'"') colorotherlabel(`"`macval(hv)'"') nodraw
local tw = _rc
capture dash clear
capture log close _ztplog
quietly log using "`logfile'", name(_ztplog) text replace
capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, colorotherlabel(`"`macval(hv)'"') colorotherlabel(`"`macval(hv)'"') name(zq14f)
local rc = _rc
quietly log close _ztplog
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option colorotherlabel() not allowed"
local said = r(found)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "INJINJINJ"
local ran = r(found)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "S_ADO"
local echoed = r(found)
if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | !`said' | `ran' | `echoed' | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
    display as error "TP-14f FAIL hostile value: twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), said `said', directive run `ran', value echoed `echoed'"
    local bad = 1
}
// A hostile name: an option name that only looks like a repeat once its
// case is folded is no option twoway takes -- it is not a second copy of
// atobs, and it is refused as typed, as twoway refuses an option in upper
// case (TP-15), "option ATOBS not allowed", r(198).
_ztp_run `"dash lfit mpg weight, ATOBS atobs name(zq14f)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option ATOBS not allowed"
if `rc' != 198 | !r(found) {
    display as error "TP-14f FAIL case-folded name: dash r(`rc'), said `r(found)'"
    local bad = 1
}
// The Mata helpers, each on its own: the scan names the copy twoway names
// and hands back the graph-wide words; the cross check counts a word
// given in an earlier list; a word inside a title's text is text.
local _u_ok = 1
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("atobs mcolor(red) ato", "lfit")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "ato" | "`_rp_gund'" != "" local _u_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("nodropb dropbase", "scatter")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "nodropb" local _u_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("dropbase nodropbase", "bar")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "nodropbase" local _u_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("atobs atobs", "kdensity")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "" local _u_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan(`"title("atobs atobs") atobs clegend(red) notitling"', "lfit")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "" | "`_rp_gund'" != "clegend:clegend():- titling:notitling:no" local _u_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("atobs clegend(a) clegend(b)", "")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "clegend()" local _u_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("colo(red) colorend(red) c(blue) ATOBS ATOBS", "scatter")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "" local _u_ok = 0
local _u_acc "titling:titling:-"
local _u_add "pcycle:pcyc():- titling:notitling:no"
mata: _dash_rep_und_cross("_u_acc", "_u_add")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "notitling" local _u_ok = 0
local _u_acc "titling:titling:-"
local _u_add "pcycle:pcyc():-"
mata: _dash_rep_und_cross("_u_acc", "_u_add")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "" | "`_u_acc'" != "titling:titling:- pcycle:pcyc():-" local _u_ok = 0
if !`_u_ok' {
    display as error "TP-14f FAIL: _dash_rep_und_scan or _dash_rep_und_cross read a list wrongly"
    local bad = 1
}
// Resource exhaustion: 250 copies of an option twoway takes again, then a
// pair it takes once, are refused as twoway refuses them, quickly; 10,000
// copies are "too many options", r(1003), in twoway and dash alike.
local many ""
forvalues i = 1/250 {
    local many "`many' baroffset(1)"
}
timer clear 14
timer on 14
capture cert_tw twoway bar mpg weight, `many' nodropbase nodropbase nodraw
local tw = _rc
_ztp_run `"dash bar mpg weight, `many' nodropbase nodropbase name(zq14f)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option nodropbase not allowed"
local said = r(found)
timer off 14
quietly timer list 14
if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | !`said' | r(t14) >= 10 | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
    display as error "TP-14f FAIL 250 copies then a pair: twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), said `said', `r(t14)' s"
    local bad = 1
}
local many ""
forvalues i = 1/10000 {
    local many "`many' atobs"
}
timer clear 14
timer on 14
capture cert_tw twoway lfit mpg weight, `many' nodraw
local tw = _rc
_ztp_run `"dash lfit mpg weight, name(zq14f) `many'"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
timer off 14
quietly timer list 14
if `tw' != 1003 | `rc' != 1003 | r(t14) >= 10 | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
    display as error "TP-14f FAIL 10000 copies: twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), `r(t14)' s"
    local bad = 1
}
capture dash clear
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-14"
}
else display as text "TP-14 PASS: a repeated option draws what twoway draws -- the last copy, the copies merged, or refused as unique -- in both routes, with no note"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-15 -- log and logit, a plot option after a plot group's comma, an
// option in upper case, and two kernels (BUGS.md, S1 and S3).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Measured 24sep2026, and asked of twoway again below on every run:
//   * log is the graph option logging on every plot type, lowess too:
//     twoway takes the graph's options out of each list first, so only
//     lo, logi and logit are lowess's logit, and log, logg .. logging and
//     nolog .. nologging draw what no option draws (the serset of lowess
//     zb weight, log is the serset of lowess zb weight).  nolo, nologi and
//     nologit are logit's off form: taken on lowess, refused elsewhere,
//     "option nolo not allowed", r(198), as lo, logi and logit are.
//   * after the plot groups' comma twoway takes only graph options: a
//     plot option there -- atobs, mcolor(), kernel(), lo -- is refused even
//     once, "option atobs not allowed", naming the first word it does not
//     take; clegend(), below, logging and the other graph-wide ones are
//     taken.
//   * an option written in upper case -- ATOBS, MCOLOR(red), Title(x), and
//     dash's own HOVER() -- is no option: "option MCOLOR() not allowed",
//     r(198), in comma mode, in a plot group and after the comma, naming the
//     first word twoway does not take.
//   * on lpoly, lpolyci and kdensity two kernel flags are "only one kernel
//     may be specified", and a flag beside kernel() "kernel(): old syntax
//     may not be combined with new syntax" (kdensity: "option kernel():
//     ..."), whatever kernel() holds, after the repeats' refusals.
// dash read log as logit (a different lowess curve), and named the rest in
// its note or took it.
local bad15 = 0
capture drop zb
generate byte zb = mpg > 20
cert_truth_ctx "TP-15"
// twoway's serset: the smooth of the plain lowess and of its logit (its
// mean asked in a live run, read back otherwise: cert_truth.do).
foreach k in plain lo {
    if "`k'" == "plain" local _ct_q "twoway lowess zb weight"
    else local _ct_q "twoway lowess zb weight, lo"
    if `_ct_l' {
        capture graph drop _all
        if "`k'" == "plain" quietly twoway lowess zb weight
        else quietly twoway lowess zb weight, lo
        preserve
        quietly serset use, clear
        quietly ds
        local _sv : word 1 of `r(varlist)'
        quietly summarize `_sv'
        local m15_`k' = r(mean)
        restore
        local _ct_v "`m15_`k''"
        python: _dct.val_put("serset mean", "_ct_q", "_ct_v")
    }
    else {
        python: _dct.val_get("serset mean", "_ct_q", "_ct_v")
        if "`_ct_v'" == "" local _ct_v .
        local m15_`k' `_ct_v'
    }
}
if abs(`m15_plain' - `m15_lo') < 1e-6 {
    display as error "TP-15a FAIL: the twoway oracle draws lowess zb weight, lo as the plain curve"
    local bad15 = 1
}
// TP-15a: each spelling on four types, lowess in three forms; twoway's rc,
// words and serset asked here, dash's rc, words and spec held to them.
local sp15 "lo log logi logit logg loggi logging nolo nolog nologi nologit nologg nologging LOG LOGIT Lo"
local fm15 "c p a"
cert_truth_ctx "TP-15a"
foreach tt in lowess scatter line lfit {
    foreach s of local sp15 {
        foreach f of local fm15 {
            if "`tt'" != "lowess" & "`f'" != "c" continue
            if "`f'" == "c" local cmd "`tt' zb weight, `s'"
            if "`f'" == "p" local cmd "(`tt' zb weight, `s'), title(T)"
            if "`f'" == "a" local cmd "(`tt' zb weight), `s'"
            capture graph drop _all
            _ztp_run `"twoway `cmd' nodraw"' "`logfile'"
            local tw = r(rc)
            local twsaid 1
            if `tw' {
                _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `s' not allowed"
                local twsaid = r(found)
            }
            local twlogit 0
            if !`tw' & "`tt'" == "lowess" {
                // the serset's mean: asked in a live run, read back
                // otherwise (cert_truth.do)
                local _ct_q "twoway `cmd'"
                if `_ct_l' {
                    capture graph drop _all
                    quietly twoway `cmd'
                    preserve
                    quietly serset use, clear
                    quietly ds
                    local _sv : word 1 of `r(varlist)'
                    quietly summarize `_sv'
                    local _ct_v = r(mean)
                    restore
                    python: _dct.val_put("serset mean", "_ct_q", "_ct_v")
                }
                else {
                    python: _dct.val_get("serset mean", "_ct_q", "_ct_v")
                    if "`_ct_v'" == "" local _ct_v .
                }
                local twlogit = abs(`_ct_v' - `m15_lo') < 1e-6
            }
            _ztp_run `"dash `cmd' name(zq15)"' "`logfile'"
            local rc = r(rc)
            local said 1
            local dlogit 0
            if `rc' {
                _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `s' not allowed"
                local said = r(found)
            }
            else {
                _ztp_has zq15 logit
                local dlogit = r(found)
            }
            if !`twsaid' | `rc' != `tw' | !`said' | `dlogit' != `twlogit' {
                display as error `"TP-15a FAIL `cmd': twoway r(`tw') (said `twsaid', logit `twlogit'); dash r(`rc') (said "option `s' not allowed": `said', logit `dlogit')"'
                local bad15 = 1
            }
            else display as text `"TP-15a `cmd': r(`tw'), logit `twlogit', in twoway and dash"'
        }
    }
}
// Both routes: the command drawn at once answers each lowess spelling as
// the registered one does.
foreach s of local sp15 {
    capture cert_tw twoway lowess zb weight, `s' nodraw
    local tw = _rc
    capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp15_imm.html"
    _ztp_run `"dash lowess zb weight, `s' saving("`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp15_imm.html", replace)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    local said 1
    if `rc' {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `s' not allowed"
        local said = r(found)
    }
    if `rc' != `tw' | !`said' {
        display as error "TP-15a FAIL immediate lowess, `s': twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), said `said'"
        local bad15 = 1
    }
}
capture erase "`c(tmpdir)'dash_tp15_imm.html"

// TP-15b..d: each row a command twoway answers with code x<k> and first
// words g<k> (asked in the run); dash must answer the same and register
// nothing, or draw it where twoway does.
local k = 0
cert_truth_ctx "TP-15b"
foreach r in ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), atobs~198~option atobs not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), ato~198~option ato not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), mcolor(red)~198~option mcolor() not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), mc(red)~198~option mc() not allowed"' ///
    `"(scatter mpg weight), msymbol(O)~198~option msymbol() not allowed"' ///
    `"(line mpg weight), sort~198~option sort not allowed"' ///
    `"(line mpg weight), sort(mpg)~198~option sort() not allowed"' ///
    `"(lpoly mpg weight), kernel(gaussian)~198~option kernel() not allowed"' ///
    `"(lpoly mpg weight), bwidth(1)~198~option bwidth() not allowed"' ///
    `"(kdensity mpg), gaussian~198~option gaussian not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfitci mpg weight), nofit~198~option nofit not allowed"' ///
    `"(lowess mpg weight), logit~198~option logit not allowed"' ///
    `"(lowess mpg weight), mean~198~option mean not allowed"' ///
    `"(histogram mpg), bin(5)~198~option bin() not allowed"' ///
    `"(scatter mpg weight), colorstart(red)~198~option colorstart() not allowed"' ///
    `"(scatter mpg weight), nodropbase~198~option nodropbase not allowed"' ///
    `"(scatter mpg weight), mlabvposition(pos)~198~option mlabvposition() not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight) (scatter mpg weight), mcolor(red) atobs~198~option mcolor() not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight) (scatter mpg weight), atobs mcolor(red)~198~option atobs not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight) (scatter mpg weight), title(x) atobs~198~option atobs not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), bogus atobs~198~option bogus not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), atobs bogus~198~option atobs not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), title(A) title(B) title(C) atobs~198~option atobs not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), title(x)~0~"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), xsize(4)~0~"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), clegend(red)~0~"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), below~0~"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), logging~0~"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), log~0~"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), xoverhangs~0~"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), title(A) title(B) title(C)~0~"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, ATOBS~198~option ATOBS not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, Atobs~198~option Atobs not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, MCOLOR(red)~198~option MCOLOR() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, mColor(red)~198~option mColor() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, MC(red)~198~option MC() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, Title(x)~198~option Title() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, TITLE(x)~198~option TITLE() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, HOVER(x)~198~option HOVER() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, LINK(g)~198~option LINK() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, SORT~198~option SORT not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, NODRAW~198~option NODRAW not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, LOGGING~198~option LOGGING not allowed"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, N(5)~198~option N() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, MCOLOR(red) mcolor(blue)~198~option MCOLOR() not allowed"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, mcolor(blue) MCOLOR(red)~198~option MCOLOR() not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, ATOBS atobs~198~option ATOBS not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, bogus ATOBS~198~option bogus not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, ATOBS bogus~198~option ATOBS not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, xreverse ATOBS~198~option xreverse not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, ATOBS MCOLOR(red)~198~option ATOBS not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight, MCOLOR(red)), title(T)~198~option MCOLOR() not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), TITLE(x)~198~option TITLE() not allowed"' ///
    `"(lfit mpg weight), MC(red) atobs~198~option MC() not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight || scatter mpg weight, TITLE(x)~198~option TITLE() not allowed"' ///
    `"lfit mpg weight, TITLE(x) || scatter mpg weight~198~option TITLE() not allowed"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian epan2~198~only one kernel may be specified"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, biweight gaussian~198~only one kernel may be specified"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, ep epan2~198~only one kernel may be specified"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian kernel(epan2)~198~kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, kernel(epan2) gaussian~198~kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gau k(gaussian)~198~kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian kernel(bogus)~198~kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian epan2 kernel(gaussian)~198~kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"lpolyci mpg weight, gaussian cosine~198~only one kernel may be specified"' ///
    `"lpolyci mpg weight, kernel(epan2) triangle~198~kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"kdensity mpg, gaussian epan2~198~only one kernel may be specified"' ///
    `"kdensity mpg, parzen rectangle~198~only one kernel may be specified"' ///
    `"kdensity mpg, gaussian kernel(epan2)~198~option kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"kdensity mpg, kernel(gaussian) gaussian~198~option kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, kernel(gau) kernel(epan2)~198~option kernel() not allowed"' ///
    `"kdensity mpg, kernel(gaussian) kernel(gaussian)~198~option kernel() not allowed"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, bwidth(1) bwidth(2) gaussian epan2~198~option bwidth() not allowed"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian epan2 gaussian~198~option gaussian not allowed"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian GAUSSIAN~198~option GAUSSIAN not allowed"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian epan2 ATOBS~198~option ATOBS not allowed"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian epan2 mcolor(bogus)~198~only one kernel may be specified"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, gaussian || lpoly mpg weight, epan2~0~"' ///
    `"lpoly mpg weight, kernel(gaussian) || lpoly price weight, kernel(epan2)~0~"' {
    local ++k
    gettoken c15 rest : r, parse("~")
    gettoken x15 rest : rest, parse("~")
    gettoken x15 rest : rest, parse("~")
    gettoken g15 rest : rest, parse("~")
    gettoken g15 rest : rest, parse("~")
    if "`g15'" == "~" local g15 ""
    local sep15 ""
    if strpos(`"`c15'"', ", ") == 0 & substr(`"`c15'"', -1, 1) == ")" local sep15 ","
    capture graph drop _all
    _ztp_run `"twoway `c15'`sep15' nodraw"' "`logfile'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    local twsaid 1
    if `x15' {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`g15'"
        local twsaid = r(found)
    }
    if `tw' != `x15' | !`twsaid' {
        display as error `"TP-15 FAIL row `k': twoway gave r(`tw') (said "`g15'": `twsaid') for `c15', not r(`x15') as measured"'
        local bad15 = 1
        continue
    }
    _ztp_run `"dash `c15' name(zq15)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    local said 1
    if `x15' {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`g15'"
        local said = r(found)
    }
    if `rc' != `x15' | !`said' | (`x15' & "${dash_graph_registry}" != "") {
        display as error `"TP-15 FAIL row `k': `c15': dash r(`rc'), "`g15'" said `said', registry ${dash_graph_registry}"'
        local bad15 = 1
    }
    else display as text `"TP-15 row `k': `c15' r(`x15') `g15'"'
}

// The Mata helpers, each on its own.  _dash_log_split takes log and nolog
// out of a list, and no word inside a value; _dash_logit_typed finds the
// first logit spelling as typed; _dash_foreign_scan marks what twoway takes
// and what is a plot option or in upper case; _dash_kernel_clash tells
// two kernels from one, and reads no word inside a title's text.
local _k_ok = 1
local _k_src `", mcolor(red) log title("log nolog") nolog"'
mata: _dash_log_split("_k_src", "_k_out")
if `"`_k_src'"' != `", mcolor(red) title("log nolog")"' | "`_k_out'" != "log nolog" local _k_ok = 0
local _k_src ", mcolor(red) logging lo"
mata: _dash_log_split("_k_src", "_k_out")
if "`_k_src'" != ", mcolor(red) logging lo" | "`_k_out'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_logit_typed(`"title("lo") log nolog nologi lo"'))
if "`_k_t'" != "nologi" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_logit_typed("log nolog logging logg"))
if "`_k_t'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_foreign_scan("atobs mcolor(red) clegend(red)", "", "atobs mcolor(red)", 1)
if "`_fs_go'`_fs_n'" != "13" | "`_fs_acc1'`_fs_acc2'`_fs_acc3'" != "001" | "`_fs_plot1'`_fs_plot2'`_fs_plot3'" != "100" | "`_fs_nm2'" != "mcolor()" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_foreign_scan("mcolor(red) ATOBS atobs", "lfit", "ATOBS", 0)
if "`_fs_go'`_fs_n'" != "13" | "`_fs_uc1'`_fs_uc2'`_fs_uc3'" != "010" | "`_fs_acc3'" != "1" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_foreign_scan("atobs bogus", "lfit", "atobs bogus", 0)
if "`_fs_go'" != "0" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_kernel_clash("gaussian epan2", "lpoly"))
if "`_k_t'" != "one" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_kernel_clash("gau k(bogus)", "kdensity"))
if "`_k_t'" != "old" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_kernel_clash("ep epan2", "lpolyci"))
if "`_k_t'" != "one" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_kernel_clash("gaussian", "lpoly"))
if "`_k_t'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_kernel_clash("gaussian epan2", "lowess"))
if "`_k_t'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
mata: st_local("_k_t", _dash_kernel_clash(`"title("gaussian epan2") gaussian"', "lpoly"))
if "`_k_t'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("lo nolo", "lowess")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "nolo" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_rep_und_scan("log lo", "lowess")
if "`_rp_refuse'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
if !`_k_ok' {
    display as error "TP-15 FAIL: _dash_log_split, _dash_logit_typed, _dash_foreign_scan, _dash_kernel_clash or the logit rows read a list wrongly"
    local bad15 = 1
}
// lowess's logit given as lo and as its off form is one option given
// twice, as twoway reads it.
cert_truth_ctx "TP-15 lowess"
foreach r in "lo nolo|nolo" "nologit lo|nologit" "logit logi|logi" {
    gettoken o15 w15 : r, parse("|")
    local w15 = substr("`w15'", 2, .)
    capture graph drop _all
    _ztp_run `"twoway lowess mpg weight, `o15' nodraw"' "`logfile'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `w15' not allowed"
    local twsaid = r(found)
    _ztp_run `"dash lowess mpg weight, `o15' name(zq15)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `w15' not allowed"
    if `tw' != 198 | !`twsaid' | `rc' != 198 | !r(found) {
        display as error "TP-15 FAIL lowess, `o15': twoway r(`tw') said `twsaid', dash r(`rc') said `r(found)'"
        local bad15 = 1
    }
}

// TP-15e: adversarial (CLAUDE.md rule 18).  Injection: a hostile value in
// an upper-case option, in a plot option after the comma and beside two
// kernels is refused naming the option alone -- never echoed, expanded or
// run -- and nothing is registered.  Resource exhaustion: 200 words twoway
// does not take after the comma, or in comma mode, then the word that
// refuses them, are answered as twoway answers them, quickly.
local hv = "{bf:B} " + char(36) + "S_ADO " + char(96) + "c(pwd)" + char(39) + " _dup(3) " + char(96) + char(34) + "INJ" + char(34) + char(39)
cert_truth_ctx "TP-15e"
foreach form in u a k {
    if "`form'" == "u" {
        local pre "scatter mpg weight, MCOLOR("
        local post ")"
        local want "option MCOLOR() not allowed"
    }
    if "`form'" == "a" {
        local pre "(scatter mpg weight), mcolor("
        local post ")"
        local want "option mcolor() not allowed"
    }
    if "`form'" == "k" {
        local pre "lpoly mpg weight, gaussian kernel("
        local post ")"
        local want "kernel(): old syntax may not be combined with new syntax"
    }
    capture graph drop _all
    capture cert_tw twoway `pre'`"`macval(hv)'"'`post' nodraw
    local tw = _rc
    capture dash clear
    capture log close _ztplog
    quietly log using "`logfile'", name(_ztplog) text replace
    capture noisily dash `pre'`"`macval(hv)'"'`post' name(zq15)
    local rc = _rc
    quietly log close _ztplog
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`want'"
    local said = r(found)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "INJINJINJ"
    local ran = r(found)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "S_ADO"
    local echoed = r(found)
    if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | !`said' | `ran' | `echoed' | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
        display as error "TP-15e FAIL hostile value (`form'): twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), said `said', directive run `ran', value echoed `echoed'"
        local bad15 = 1
    }
}
// dash's time is judged as a ratio, not a wall-clock bound: 200 words take
// under 8 times what 50 take (linear is about 4), with half a second of
// slack and a 60-second ceiling; an absolute 10-second bound failed at
// 10.69 s on a loaded machine (26oct2026).
foreach form in a c {
    foreach z15n in 50 200 {
        local many ""
        forvalues i = 1/`z15n' {
            local many "`many' zqbogus"
        }
        if "`form'" == "a" local cmd15 "(lfit mpg weight),`many' atobs"
        else local cmd15 "lfit mpg weight,`many' ATOBS"
        // twoway is asked the recorded 200-word command only (its answers
        // replay from the truth record); dash is timed at both sizes.
        local tw = 198
        if `z15n' == 200 {
            capture cert_tw twoway `cmd15' nodraw
            local tw = _rc
        }
        timer clear 15
        timer on 15
        _ztp_run `"dash `cmd15' name(zq15)"' "`logfile'"
        local rc = r(rc)
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option zqbogus not allowed"
        local said = r(found)
        timer off 15
        quietly timer list 15
        local z15t`z15n' = r(t15)
        if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | !`said' | "${dash_graph_registry}" != "" {
            display as error "TP-15e FAIL `z15n' words then a refusal (`form'): twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), said `said'"
            local bad15 = 1
        }
    }
    if `z15t200' >= 8 * `z15t50' + 0.5 | `z15t200' >= 60 {
        display as error "TP-15e FAIL 200 words then a refusal (`form'): `z15t200' s against `z15t50' s for 50 words"
        local bad15 = 1
    }
}
capture dash clear
capture drop zb
if `bad15' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-15"
}
else display as text "TP-15 PASS: log is logging and only lo, logi and logit are lowess's logit; a plot option after the comma, an option in upper case and two kernels are refused in twoway's words"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TP-16 -- a kernel written as an option of its own (BUGS.md, S2).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Measured 24sep2026, and asked of twoway again below on every run: on
// lpoly, lpolyci and kdensity each kernel name taken as an option of its
// own -- bi .. biweight, cos .. cosine, ep .. epanechnikov (so ep, epa and
// epan are epanechnikov), epan2 in full, gau .. gaussian, par .. parzen,
// rec .. rectangle, tri .. triangle -- draws the serset of kernel(<name>);
// a shorter spelling (e, b, co, ga, pa, re, tr) is "option ga not
// allowed", r(198), and so is every spelling on another plot type
// (scatter, line, lfit, lowess, histogram, mspline, lfitci, area).  dash
// named the flag in its note and drew the default epanechnikov.
local bad16 = 0
capture program drop _ztp_sersum
program define _ztp_sersum, rclass
    preserve
    quietly serset use, clear
    local s 0
    foreach v of varlist _all {
        quietly summarize `v'
        local s = `s' + r(sum) + 7 * r(sd)
    }
    restore
    return scalar s = `s'
end
cert_truth_ctx "TP-16"
foreach t16 in lpoly lpolyci kdensity {
    local v16 "mpg weight"
    if "`t16'" == "kdensity" local v16 "mpg"
    foreach r in bi|biweight biweight|biweight cos|cosine cosine|cosine ///
        ep|epanechnikov epan|epanechnikov epanechnikov|epanechnikov ///
        epan2|epan2 gau|gaussian gaus|gaussian gaussian|gaussian ///
        par|parzen parzen|parzen rec|rectangle rectangle|rectangle ///
        tri|triangle triangle|triangle {
        gettoken f16 k16 : r, parse("|")
        local k16 = substr("`k16'", 2, .)
        // twoway's serset of kernel(<name>), and its rc and serset for the
        // flag: asked in a live run, read back otherwise (cert_truth.do).
        local _ct_q "twoway `t16' `v16', kernel(`k16')"
        if `_ct_l' {
            capture graph drop _all
            quietly twoway `t16' `v16', kernel(`k16')
            _ztp_sersum
            local ref16 = r(s)
            python: _dct.val_put("serset sum", "_ct_q", "ref16")
        }
        else {
            python: _dct.val_get("serset sum", "_ct_q", "ref16")
            if "`ref16'" == "" local ref16 .
        }
        local _ct_q "twoway `t16' `v16', `f16'"
        if `_ct_l' {
            capture graph drop _all
            capture quietly twoway `t16' `v16', `f16'
            local tw = _rc
            local s16 .
            if !`tw' {
                _ztp_sersum
                local s16 = r(s)
            }
            local _ct_a "`tw' `s16'"
            python: _dct.val_put("rc and serset sum", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
        }
        else {
            python: _dct.val_get("rc and serset sum", "_ct_q", "_ct_a")
            if "`_ct_a'" == "" local _ct_a "9 ."
            local tw  : word 1 of `_ct_a'
            local s16 : word 2 of `_ct_a'
        }
        local same16 0
        if !`tw' {
            local same16 = reldif(`s16', `ref16') < 1e-9
        }
        if `tw' | !`same16' {
            display as error "TP-16 FAIL: twoway `t16' `v16', `f16' gave r(`tw'), the serset of kernel(`k16') `same16', not as measured"
            local bad16 = 1
            continue
        }
        _ztp_run `"dash `t16' `v16', `f16' name(zq16)"' "`logfile'"
        local rc = r(rc)
        local note = r(note)
        mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zq16", "kernel", "`k16'")))
        if `rc' | `note' | !`ok' {
            display as error "TP-16 FAIL: dash `t16' `v16', `f16': r(`rc'), note `note', kernel(`k16') in the spec `ok'"
            local bad16 = 1
        }
        else display as text "TP-16 `t16', `f16': kernel(`k16'), as twoway draws it"
    }
}
// Plot groups, one flag in each, and a || segment each: both kernels.
foreach c16 in "(lpoly mpg weight, gau) (kdensity mpg, par), name(zq16)" ///
    "lpolyci mpg weight, tri || lpoly price weight, cos name(zq16)" {
    capture graph drop _all
    local tc16 : subinstr local c16 "name(zq16)" "nodraw"
    capture quietly cert_tw twoway `tc16'
    local tw = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash `c16'"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    local note = r(note)
    if strpos("`c16'", "gau") {
        mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zq16", "kernel", "gaussian") & _ztp_hasval("zq16", "kernel", "parzen")))
    }
    else {
        mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zq16", "kernel", "triangle") & _ztp_hasval("zq16", "kernel", "cosine")))
    }
    if `tw' | `rc' | `note' | !`ok' {
        display as error "TP-16 FAIL: `c16': twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), note `note', both kernels in the spec `ok'"
        local bad16 = 1
    }
}
// What twoway refuses: a spelling one letter short, and a flag on another
// type.  dash reads none of them as a kernel (whether it notes or refuses
// the word is BUGS.md's separate entry on an undeclared lower-case word).
foreach c16 in "lpoly mpg weight, ga" "kdensity mpg, co" "lpolyci mpg weight, e" ///
    "lpoly mpg weight, b" "scatter mpg weight, gaussian" "lowess mpg weight, gau" ///
    "lfit mpg weight, epan2" "line mpg weight, tri" {
    capture graph drop _all
    capture quietly cert_tw twoway `c16' nodraw
    local tw = _rc
    _ztp_run `"dash `c16' name(zq16)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_has zq16 kernel
    local has = r(found)
    if `tw' != 198 | `has' {
        display as error "TP-16 FAIL: `c16': twoway r(`tw') (measured 198), dash r(`rc') wrote a kernel `has'"
        local bad16 = 1
    }
}
// The Mata helper on its own: the first kernel word, the rest kept as
// typed, nothing on another type, no word inside a value.
local _k_ok = 1
mata: _dash_kernel_flag(`"zqa(1) gau zqb"', "lpoly")
if "`_kf_name'" != "gaussian" | "`_kf_rest'" != "zqa(1) zqb" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_kernel_flag("epan2", "kdensity")
if "`_kf_name'" != "epan2" | "`_kf_rest'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_kernel_flag("ep", "lpolyci")
if "`_kf_name'" != "epanechnikov" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_kernel_flag("gaussian", "lowess")
if "`_kf_name'" != "" | "`_kf_rest'" != "gaussian" local _k_ok = 0
mata: _dash_kernel_flag(`"zqa("gaussian") ga GAUSSIAN gaussian()"', "lpoly")
if "`_kf_name'" != "" local _k_ok = 0
if !`_k_ok' {
    display as error "TP-16 FAIL: _dash_kernel_flag read a list wrongly"
    local bad16 = 1
}
// Adversarial (CLAUDE.md rule 18).  Injection: a hostile value in an
// undeclared option beside the flag is kept as text, never expanded or
// run, and the kernel is still read.  Resource exhaustion: 200 unknown
// words then the flag, read quickly.
local hv = "{bf:B} " + char(36) + "S_ADO " + char(96) + "c(pwd)" + char(39) + " _dup(3) " + char(96) + char(34) + "INJ" + char(34) + char(39)
capture dash clear
capture log close _ztplog
quietly log using "`logfile'", name(_ztplog) text replace
// Flipped: WP-32 -- the value rode on zqbogus(), an option twoway refuses
// and dash now refuses as twoway does; it rides on afcolor(), which twoway
// takes on every type and dash names in its note.
capture noisily dash lpoly mpg weight, afcolor(`"`macval(hv)'"') gau name(zq16)
local rc = _rc
quietly log close _ztplog
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "INJINJINJ"
local ran = r(found)
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zq16", "kernel", "gaussian")))
if `rc' | `ran' | !`ok' {
    display as error "TP-16 FAIL hostile value beside a flag: dash r(`rc'), directive run `ran', kernel read `ok'"
    local bad16 = 1
}
local many ""
forvalues i = 1/200 {
    local many "`many' zqbogus`i'"
}
timer clear 16
timer on 16
_ztp_run `"dash kdensity mpg,`many' rec name(zq16)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
timer off 16
quietly timer list 16
local t16 = r(t16)
// Flipped: WP-32 -- 200 words twoway does not take are refused at the
// first, "option zqbogus1 not allowed", r(198), quickly, where dash named
// them all and read the flag.
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option zqbogus1 not allowed"
local ok = r(found)
if `rc' != 198 | !`ok' | `t16' >= 10 {
    display as error "TP-16 FAIL 200 words then a flag: dash r(`rc'), the first named `ok', `t16' s"
    local bad16 = 1
}
capture dash clear
if `bad16' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TP-16"
}
else display as text "TP-16 PASS: a kernel written as an option of its own is kernel(<name>) on lpoly, lpolyci and kdensity, where twoway reads it so, and nowhere else"

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// AX -- axis(#) routed to the axis it names (WP-29 S10, P0.5)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// twoway's ParseAndLogAxes (graph_g.class:1300-1422) routes ytitle(),
// ylabel(), ymlabel(), ytick(), ymtick(), yline() and yscale() (x too) to
// the axis axis(#) names, and refuses an axis no layer uses, AXIS(), a
// second axis() and a second comma, r(198), in its own order: side (X
// before Y), then family (SCale Labels MLabels TICks MTicks Title LInes),
// then where it was typed, every plot segment before the options after
// the comma.  dash drew every one on the first axis.  Each case asks
// twoway in the same run.  test/fixtures/axis2_truth.json holds the same
// measurements (scripts/extract_axis2_truth.do).
local saved_ls = c(linesize)
set linesize 255

capture mata: mata drop _zax_first_line()
mata:
// The first non-blank line of a text log (a command run inside a program
// under capture noisily prints no echo, so it is the error line).
string scalar _zax_first_line(string scalar path)
{
    real scalar   fh
    string scalar ln
    fh = _fopen(path, "r")
    if (fh < 0) return("")
    while ((ln = fget(fh)) != J(0, 0, "")) {
        if (strtrim(ln) != "") {
            fclose(fh)
            return(strtrim(ln))
        }
    }
    fclose(fh)
    return("")
}
end

// twoway under its own quiet log: r(rc), and r(err) its first error line.
// twoway's answer -- its rc and the words its log holds -- is asked here
// in a live run and read back otherwise (cert_truth.do), the same words in
// the same log either way.
capture program drop _zax_tw
program define _zax_tw, rclass
    args cmdtext logpath
    capture log close _zaxlog
    capture erase "`logpath'"
    capture graph drop _all
    python: _dct = __import__("sys").modules["_dash_cert_truth"]
    python: _dct.flag("_ct_l")
    if `_ct_l' {
        quietly log using "`logpath'", name(_zaxlog) text replace
        capture noisily `cmdtext'
        local rc = _rc
        quietly log close _zaxlog
        python: _dct.log_put("cmdtext", "rc", "logpath")
    }
    else {
        python: _dct.log_get("cmdtext", "logpath", "rc")
        if "`rc'" == "" local rc 9
    }
    capture graph drop _all
    mata: st_local("err", _zax_first_line(st_local("logpath")))
    return local err `"`macval(err)'"'
    return scalar rc = `rc'
end

local twlog "`c(tmpdir)'dash_ax_twoway.log"
local B "(scatter mpg weight) (line price weight, yaxis(2) sort)"
local L "line price weight, yaxis(2) sort"

// ---- AX-01 (direct): _dash_route_axis2 rewrites each family ----------
local bad01 = 0
local n = 0
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ylabel(5000 10000, axis(2)) ylabel(10 20)"'
local out`n' `"ylabel2(5000 10000) ylabel(10 20)"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"yscale(log ax(2))"'
local out`n' `"yscale2(log)"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"yline(5000, axis(2) lcolor(red))"'
local out`n' `"yline2(5000, lcolor(red))"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ytitle(T, ax(2))"'
local out`n' `"ytitle2(T)"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"xt(V, axis(2))"'
local out`n' `"xtitle2(V)"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ylabels(5000)"'
local out`n' `"ylabel(5000)"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ytick(5000, axis(2),)"'
local out`n' `"ytick2(5000)"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"yticks(1, axis(1))"'
local out`n' `"ytick(1)"'
// Flipped (WP-31 C10c): an axis(3) option leaves the text for the graph's
// "axisn" record (asked of _dash_axisn_json below).
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ylabel(1, axis(3))"'
local out`n' `""'
// Flipped (WP-31 D1): ymlabel(1, axis(2)) "byte for byte" was wrong once
// minor ticks and labels are drawn: it is dash's ymlabel2(), and a t
// option's mlabel on axis 2, which no key routes, stays as typed.
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ymlabel(1, axis(2))"'
local out`n' `"ymlabel2(1)"'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ymtick(1 2, axis(2))"'
local out`n' `"ymtick2(1 2)"'
// Flipped (WP-31 D1b): tmlabel(1, axis(2)) and ymtick(1, axis(3)) "byte
// for byte" was wrong once twoway was measured drawing them
// (axisn_minor_truth.json m3.tmlabel, m3.mtick): the t option's mlabel on
// axis 2 is the x one's, xmlabel2(), and an axis-3 mtick joins "axisn".
// Flipped (WP-31 C10e): xmlabel2(1) was wrong once its dates are read: a
// t option's mlabel on axis 2 is a "t" row, which _dash_taxis_fold reads
// in the axis's unit and joins to xmlabel2() (axisn_date_truth.json
// x3.tmlabel2); the route leaves no text and the axisn object no t row.
local ++n
local in`n'  `"tmlabel(1, axis(2))"'
local out`n' `""'
local ++n
local in`n'  `"ymtick(1, axis(3))"'
local out`n' `""'
// byte for byte
foreach w in `"ylabel(5000, AXIS(2))"' `"ylabel(5000, axis(2) axis(1))"' `"ylabel(5000, angle(0), axis(2))"' {
    local ++n
    local in`n'  `"`w'"'
    local out`n' `"`w'"'
}
mata: _dash_axisn_clear()
forvalues i = 1/`n' {
    capture mata: st_local("got", _dash_route_axis2(st_local("in`i'")))
    if _rc {
        display as error "AX-01 FAIL _dash_route_axis2 r(" _rc ")"
        local bad01 = 1
        continue
    }
    mata: st_local("eq", strofreal(st_local("got") == st_local("out`i'")))
    if !`eq' {
        mata: _dash_say("err", "AX-01 FAIL got ", st_local("got"), " for " + st_local("in`i'"))
        local bad01 = 1
    }
}
mata: st_local("axn", _dash_axisn_json())
mata: st_local("eq", strofreal(st_local("axn") == char(123) + char(34) + "y3" + char(34) + ":" + char(123) + char(34) + "label" + char(34) + ":" + char(34) + "1" + char(34) + "," + char(34) + "mtick" + char(34) + ":" + char(34) + "1" + char(34) + char(125) + char(125)))
if !`eq' {
    mata: _dash_say("err", "AX-01 FAIL axisn ", st_local("axn"), "")
    local bad01 = 1
}
mata: _dash_axisn_clear()
// hostile text: a $, a backtick and a quoted "axis(2)" come back as typed;
// a routed body is kept byte for byte.
mata: st_local("h1", "ylabel(1 " + char(34) + char(36) + "x" + char(96) + "y'" + char(34) + ")")
mata: st_local("h2", "ylabel(1 " + char(34) + "axis(2)" + char(34) + ")")
mata: st_local("h3", "ylabel(1 " + char(34) + char(36) + "x" + char(34) + ", axis(2))")
mata: st_local("w3", "ylabel2(1 " + char(34) + char(36) + "x" + char(34) + ")")
foreach h in h1 h2 h3 {
    local want "`h'"
    if "`h'" == "h3" local want "w3"
    capture mata: st_local("got", _dash_route_axis2(st_local("`h'")))
    if _rc {
        local bad01 = 1
        continue
    }
    mata: st_local("eq", strofreal(st_local("got") == st_local("`want'")))
    if !`eq' {
        mata: _dash_say("err", "AX-01 FAIL hostile ", st_local("got"), "")
        local bad01 = 1
    }
}
if `bad01' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-01"
}
else display as text "AX-01 PASS: _dash_route_axis2 routes every family's axis(2), drops axis(1), renames plurals and leaves the refused forms as typed"

// ---- AX-02 (direct): _dash_axis_num, twoway's integer rule ------------
local bad02 = 0
local cases `"2=2 02=2 2.0=2 +2=2 2e0=2 1.0x+1=2 a=1 2.5=1 #2=1 .=1 1e300=1 2147483648=1 -2147483649=1 2147483647=2147483647 -2147483648=-2147483648 1e9=1000000000 -0=0 1e1=10"'
foreach c of local cases {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("=")
    local want = substr("`rest'", 2, .)
    local got ""
    capture mata: st_local("got", strofreal(_dash_axis_num(st_local("a")), "%11.0f"))
    if _rc | strtrim("`got'") != "`want'" {
        display as error "AX-02 FAIL _dash_axis_num(`a') = `got' (r(" _rc "), want `want')"
        local bad02 = 1
    }
}
foreach a in " 2 " "" "2 1" {
    local want = cond("`a'" == " 2 ", "2", "1")
    local got ""
    capture mata: st_local("got", strofreal(_dash_axis_num(st_local("a")), "%11.0f"))
    if _rc | strtrim("`got'") != "`want'" {
        display as error "AX-02 FAIL _dash_axis_num('`a'') = `got' (want `want')"
        local bad02 = 1
    }
}
if `bad02' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-02"
}
else display as text "AX-02 PASS: the axis number is a whole number within twoway's integer bounds, else 1"

// ---- AX-03 (refusal parity): twoway r(198), dash r(198), same message -
local bad03 = 0
local n = 0
cert_truth_ctx "AX-03"
foreach c in ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, ylabel(20 30, axis(2))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, yscale(log axis(2))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, yline(20, axis(2))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, ytick(20 30, axis(2))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, ymlabel(20 30, axis(2))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, ymtick(20 30, axis(2))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, ytitle(T, axis(2))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, xlabel(2000, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(3))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(0))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(-1))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(10))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(3) axis(1))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(1) axis(3))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, AXIS(3))"' ///
    `"`B', ytitle(T, AXIS(2))"' ///
    `"`B', yscale(log AXIS(2))"' ///
    `"`B', yline(5000, AXIS(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, Axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', xlabel(2000, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`L' ylabel(5000 10000)"' ///
    `"`L' ytitle(T)"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(2147483647))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(-2147483648))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(1e9))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(-0))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(1e1))"' {
    local ++n
    _zax_tw `"twoway `c'"' "`twlog'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    local err `"`r(err)'"'
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle(`"`macval(err)'"')
    local hit = r(count)
    if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | `hit' != 1 {
        display as error `"AX-03 FAIL (`n') `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), twoway's line found `hit' time(s): `macval(err)'"'
        local bad03 = 1
    }
}
// SD-2: a quoted value breaks twoway's own message (r(133)); dash refuses
// it, r(198), with the message intact.
_zax_tw `"twoway scatter mpg weight, ytitle("T", axis(2))"' "`twlog'"
local tw = r(rc)
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, ytitle("T", axis(2))"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle(`"ytitle("T", axis(2)) not allowed, yaxis2 does not exist"')
if `tw' == 0 | `rc' != 198 | !r(found) {
    display as error "AX-03 FAIL quoted ytitle: twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), message found " r(found)
    local bad03 = 1
}
if `bad03' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-03"
}
else display as text "AX-03 PASS: every form twoway refuses for axis(#) dash refuses, r(198), in twoway's words"

// ---- AX-04 (order): the first refusal is twoway's ---------------------
local bad04 = 0
local n = 0
cert_truth_ctx "AX-04"
foreach c in ///
    `"`B', ylabel(1, axis(3)) xscale(log axis(3))"' ///
    `"`B', yline(1, axis(3)) ylabel(1, axis(4))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(3) axis(1))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, AXIS(2) axis(3))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(2)) yscale(axis(3))"' ///
    `"(scatter mpg weight, ylabel(1, axis(3))) (line price weight, yaxis(2) sort), yscale(log axis(4))"' ///
    `"`B', ytitle(T, axis(3)) ylabel(1, AXIS(2))"' ///
    `"(scatter mpg weight, ylabel(1, axis(3))) (line price weight, yaxis(2) sort), ylabel(1, axis(4))"' ///
    `"scatter mpg weight, ylabel(1, axis(4)) || line price weight, yaxis(2) sort ylabel(1, axis(5))"' ///
    `"`L' ylabel(5000, AXIS(2))"' {
    local ++n
    _zax_tw `"twoway `c'"' "`twlog'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    local err `"`r(err)'"'
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle(`"`macval(err)'"')
    local hit = r(count)
    cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle("not allowed")
    local all = r(count)
    if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | `hit' != 1 | `all' != 1 {
        display as error `"AX-04 FAIL (`n') `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), twoway's line `hit', refusals `all': `macval(err)'"'
        local bad04 = 1
    }
}
if `bad04' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-04"
}
else display as text "AX-04 PASS: dash names the refusal twoway names first: side, family, then position, segments before the options after the comma"

// ---- AX-05 (double comma) ---------------------------------------------
local bad05 = 0
cert_truth_ctx "AX-05"
foreach c in ///
    `"`B', yscale(log, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ytitle(TT, size(small), axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', yline(5000, lcolor(red), axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, angle(0), axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ytick(20 30, grid, axis(1))"' ///
    `"`B', ytitle(TT, size(small), color(red))"' ///
    `"`B', yscale(log, range(1 50))"' ///
    `"`B', yscale(, log)"' ///
    `"`B', yline(20, lcolor(red), lwidth(thick))"' {
    _zax_tw `"twoway `c'"' "`twlog'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    local err `"`r(err)'"'
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle(`"`macval(err)'"')
    if `tw' != 198 | `rc' != 198 | !r(found) | substr(`"`macval(err)'"', 1, 9) != "invalid '" {
        display as error `"AX-05 FAIL `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'): `macval(err)'"'
        local bad05 = 1
    }
}
foreach c in `"`B', ytitle(TT, size(small),) name(zax5)"' `"`B', ytick(5000, axis(2),) name(zax5)"' {
    _zax_tw `"twoway `c'"' "`twlog'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    if `tw' | `rc' {
        display as error `"AX-05 FAIL `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc')"'
        local bad05 = 1
    }
}
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax5", "ytick2", "5000")))
if !`ok' {
    display as error "AX-05 FAIL ytick(5000, axis(2),) is not stored as ytick2 5000"
    local bad05 = 1
}
capture dash clear
if `bad05' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-05"
}
else display as text "AX-05 PASS: a second comma is refused as twoway refuses it, and a trailing empty one is not"

// ---- AX-06 (accepted parity) ------------------------------------------
local bad06 = 0
cert_truth_ctx "AX-06"
foreach c in ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, ax(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axi(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(02))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(2.0))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(a))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(1e300))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000, axis(1.0x+1))"' ///
    `"(scatter mpg weight, ylabel(5000, axis(2))) (line price weight, yaxis(2) sort)"' ///
    `"`B', by(foreign) ylabel(5000 10000, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ylabels(5000 10000, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', yticks(5000, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ylines(5000, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ymticks(5000, axis(2))"' ///
    `"`B', ytic(5000, ax(2)) yli(5000, ax(2)) ysc(log ax(2)) yml(6000, ax(2)) ymt(6000, ax(2)) ytitle(T, ax(2))"' {
    _zax_tw `"twoway `c'"' "`twlog'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    if `tw' | `rc' {
        display as error `"AX-06 FAIL `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc')"'
        local bad06 = 1
    }
}
if `bad06' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-06"
}
else display as text "AX-06 PASS: every spelling twoway accepts for axis(#), its plurals included, dash accepts"

// ---- AX-07 (the spec after the merge) ---------------------------------
local bad07 = 0
local n = 0
foreach c in ///
    `"`B', ylabel(10 20) ylabel(5000 10000, axis(2)) name(zax7)"' ///
    `"`B', ylabel(5000 10000, axis(2)) ylabel(10 20) name(zax7)"' {
    local ++n
    _ztp_run `"dash `c'"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    mata: st_local("a", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax7", "ylabel", "10 20")))
    mata: st_local("b", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax7", "ylabel2", "5000 10000")))
    if `rc' | !`a' | !`b' {
        display as error `"AX-07 FAIL `c': r(`rc'), ylabel 10 20 `a', ylabel2 5000 10000 `b'"'
        local bad07 = 1
    }
}
_ztp_run `"dash `B', yscale(log axis(2)) yscale(reverse) name(zax7)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
mata: st_local("a", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax7", "yscale", "reverse")))
mata: st_local("b", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax7", "yscale2", "log")))
if r(rc) | !`a' | !`b' {
    display as error "AX-07 FAIL yscale: r(`rc'), yscale reverse `a', yscale2 log `b'"
    local bad07 = 1
}
_ztp_run `"dash `B', yline(5000, axis(2)) yline(20) name(zax7)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
mata: st_local("a", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax7", "yline", "20")))
mata: st_local("b", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax7", "yline2", "5000")))
if `rc' | !`a' | !`b' {
    display as error "AX-07 FAIL yline: r(`rc'), yline 20 `a', yline2 5000 `b'"
    local bad07 = 1
}
_ztp_run `"dash `B', ylabels(5000) name(zax7)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
mata: st_local("a", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zax7", "ylabel", "5000")))
if `rc' | !`a' {
    display as error "AX-07 FAIL ylabels(5000): r(`rc'), ylabel 5000 `a'"
    local bad07 = 1
}
capture dash clear
if `bad07' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-07"
}
else display as text "AX-07 PASS: each axis keeps its own copy through the repeat merge"

// ---- AX-08 (exhaustion) ------------------------------------------------
local bad08 = 0
cert_truth_ctx "AX-08"
local many ""
forvalues i = 1/10000 {
    local many "`many' ylabel(1, axis(2))"
}
_zax_tw `"twoway `B',`many'"' "`twlog'"
local tw = r(rc)
timer clear 18
timer on 18
_ztp_run `"dash `B',`many'"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
timer off 18
quietly timer list 18
local t18 = r(t18)
capture mata: st_local("rows", strofreal(rows(_dash_axreq)))
if _rc local rows "(no _dash_axreq)"
if `tw' != 1003 | `rc' != 1003 | `t18' >= 10 | "`rows'" != "0" {
    display as error "AX-08 FAIL 10000 copies: twoway r(`tw'), dash r(`rc'), `t18' s, _dash_axreq rows `rows'"
    local bad08 = 1
}
capture dash clear
if `bad08' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AX-08"
}
else display as text "AX-08 PASS: 10,000 copies of an axis(2) option end r(1003) as in twoway, quickly, keeping nothing"
capture erase "`twlog'"
set linesize `saved_ls'

// ---- BG-07..BG-09: barwidth() on rcap and rcapsym (WP-30 P1.17a) -------
// twoway refuses barwidth() on rcap and rcapsym, "option barwidth() not
// allowed", r(198), naming the spelling typed (measured 03oct2026,
// test/fixtures/bar_geometry_truth.json); dash refuses it alike.
// twoway is asked live here (nodraw, no export): these questions are not
// in the replayed fixture of _ztp_run.
capture program drop _zbg_tw
program define _zbg_tw, rclass
    args cmdtext logpath
    capture log close _zbglog
    capture erase "`logpath'"
    log using "`logpath'", name(_zbglog) text replace
    capture noisily `cmdtext'
    local rc = _rc
    log close _zbglog
    return scalar rc = `rc'
end
preserve
clear
quietly input x1 lo hi y
1 1 4 3
2 2 5 4
3 1 3 2
4 3 6 5
5 0 2 1
end
local bad07 = 0
foreach t in rcap rcapsym {
    foreach form in comma group bars {
        if "`form'" == "comma" {
            local tw "twoway `t' lo hi x1, barwidth(.5) nodraw"
            local dc "dash `t' lo hi x1, barwidth(.5) name(zbg7)"
        }
        else if "`form'" == "group" {
            local tw "twoway (`t' lo hi x1, barwidth(.5)), nodraw"
            local dc "dash (`t' lo hi x1, barwidth(.5)), name(zbg7)"
        }
        else {
            local tw "twoway scatter hi x1 || `t' lo hi x1, barwidth(.5) nodraw"
            local dc "dash scatter hi x1 || `t' lo hi x1, barwidth(.5) name(zbg7)"
        }
        capture graph drop _all
        _zbg_tw `"`tw'"' "`logfile'"
        local rtw = r(rc)
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option barwidth() not allowed"
        local twsaid = r(found)
        _ztp_run `"`dc'"' "`logfile'"
        local rc = r(rc)
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option barwidth() not allowed"
        if `rtw' != 198 | !`twsaid' | `rc' != 198 | !r(found) {
            display as error "BG-07 FAIL `t' (`form'): twoway r(`rtw') said `twsaid', dash r(`rc') said `r(found)'"
            local bad07 = 1
        }
        capture dash clear
    }
}
if `bad07' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' BG-07"
}
else display as text "BG-07 PASS: barwidth() on rcap and rcapsym is refused r(198) in twoway's words, in comma mode, a plot group and after ||"

local bad08 = 0
foreach w in barw barwi barwidth {
    capture graph drop _all
    _zbg_tw `"twoway rcap lo hi x1, `w'(.5) nodraw"' "`logfile'"
    local rtw = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `w'() not allowed"
    local twsaid = r(found)
    _ztp_run `"dash rcap lo hi x1, `w'(.5) name(zbg8)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option `w'() not allowed"
    if `rtw' != 198 | !`twsaid' | `rc' != 198 | !r(found) {
        display as error "BG-08 FAIL `w'(): twoway r(`rtw') said `twsaid', dash r(`rc') said `r(found)'"
        local bad08 = 1
    }
    capture dash clear
}
if `bad08' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' BG-08"
}
else display as text "BG-08 PASS: barw(), barwi() and barwidth() on rcap are refused naming the spelling typed, as twoway names it"

local bad09 = 0
foreach c in "bar y x1, barwidth(.5)" "rbar lo hi x1, barwidth(.5)" "spike y x1, barwidth(.5)" `"rcap lo hi x1, legend(label(1 "barwidth(2)"))"' {
    capture noisily dash `c' name(zbg9)
    if _rc {
        display as error `"BG-09 FAIL dash `c': r(`=_rc')"'
        local bad09 = 1
    }
    capture dash clear
}
_ztp_run `"dash rcap lo hi x1, bw(.5) name(zbg9)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "bw"
if `rc' != 0 | !r(found) {
    display as error "BG-09 FAIL dash rcap bw(.5): r(`rc'), its note found `r(found)'"
    local bad09 = 1
}
capture dash clear
if `bad09' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' BG-09"
}
else display as text "BG-09 PASS: bar, rbar and spike take barwidth(), quoted text is not read, and rcap bw() keeps its note"
restore

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// NP-20..NP-25 (WP-30 P1.14a): the named styles at the spec and the folds.
// p() is one name whose first copy wins and, given, drops every style
// option twoway discards under it (the label style included), keeping
// mlabel(); the outline styles are named on area and rarea, the marker
// styles on the pc arrows; clstyle() leaves the types with no connecting
// line; a style a type does not draw is silent (M6).
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture program drop _znp_spec
program define _znp_spec, rclass
    // r(found) 1 when graph g's spec holds the text "key":"val" (val ""
    // matches any value of key), read by value.
    args g key val
    mata: _znp_s = st_global("dash_json_" + st_local("g"))
    mata: _znp_k = char(34) + st_local("key") + char(34) + ":" + (st_local("val") == "" ? "" : char(34) + st_local("val") + char(34))
    mata: st_local("_zf", strofreal(strpos(_znp_s, _znp_k) > 0))
    return scalar found = `_zf'
end
local bad = 0
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, p(p3) p(p4) name(np20a)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_znp_spec np20a p p3
local f1 = r(found)
_znp_spec np20a p p4
if `rc' != 0 | !`f1' | r(found) local bad = 1
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) p(p3) mcolor(red) lcolor(red) mlabcolor(red) name(np20b)"' "`logfile'"
foreach k in mcolor lcolor mlabcolor {
    _znp_spec np20b `k' ""
    if r(found) local bad = 1
}
_znp_spec np20b mlabel make
if !r(found) local bad = 1
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' NP-20"
    display as error "NP-20 FAIL: ${dash_json_np20a} :: ${dash_json_np20b}"
}
else display as text "NP-20 PASS: p(p3) p(p4) writes p3; under p() the style options go and mlabel() stays"

_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, pstyle(p4) p(p3) name(np21)"' "`logfile'"
_znp_spec np21 pstyle ""
local f1 = r(found)
_znp_spec np21 p p3
if `f1' | !r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' NP-21"
    display as error "NP-21 FAIL: ${dash_json_np21}"
}
else display as text "NP-21 PASS: pstyle(p4) p(p3) writes p only"

local bad = 0
foreach t in area rarea {
    local v = cond("`t'" == "area", "mpg weight", "mpg turn weight")
    // Flipped (WP-32): lstyle() alstyle() blstyle() named was wrong,
    // because twoway strokes the outline in the named style and dash now
    // does (BUGS.md "Options twoway draws that dash still names...").
    _ztp_run `"dash `t' `v', sort lstyle(p3) alstyle(p3) blstyle(p3) astyle(p3) name(np22)"' "`logfile'"
    if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) local bad = 1
    foreach nm in lstyle() alstyle() blstyle() {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`nm'"
        if r(found) local bad = 1
    }
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" " astyle()"
    if r(found) local bad = 1
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' NP-22"
    display as error "NP-22 FAIL: area/rarea outline styles"
}
else display as text "NP-22 PASS: on area and rarea lstyle() alstyle() blstyle() and astyle() are drawn, named by nothing"

local bad = 0
// Flipped (WP-32): mstyle() and mlstyle() named on pcarrow was wrong,
// because twoway strokes the heads in the named style and dash now does.
_ztp_run `"dash pcarrow mpg weight turn length, mstyle(p3) mlstyle(p3) name(np23)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) local bad = 1
foreach nm in mstyle() mlstyle() {
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`nm'"
    if r(found) local bad = 1
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' NP-23"
    display as error "NP-23 FAIL: pcarrow marker styles"
}
else display as text "NP-23 PASS: on pcarrow mstyle() and mlstyle() are drawn, named by nothing"

_ztp_run `"dash spike mpg weight, clstyle(p3) name(np24)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_znp_spec np24 clstyle ""
if `rc' != 0 | r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' NP-24"
    display as error "NP-24 FAIL: ${dash_json_np24}"
}
else display as text "NP-24 PASS: spike, clstyle(p3) writes no clstyle"

_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, astyle(p3) name(np25)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 | r(note) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' NP-25"
    display as error "NP-25 FAIL: rc `r(rc)', note `r(note)'"
}
else display as text "NP-25 PASS: scatter, astyle(p3) is silent, rc 0"
capture dash clear

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// MV: mlabvposition(), read as twoway reads it (WP-30 P1.24)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// twoway appends the variable to the layer's varlist, so the types that
// count their variables refuse it, in its words; a second copy, two names,
// an expression and a missing variable are refused as twoway refuses
// them.  Each case: twoway's rc and first error line, dash's rc, and
// twoway's line in dash's log.
local mv_ls = c(linesize)
set linesize 255
capture drop p9
capture drop q9
capture drop sp9
generate double p9 = 9
generate double q9 = 9
generate str4 sp9 = "9"
quietly tsset t
local mvlog "`c(tmpdir)'dash_mv_twoway.log"
capture program drop _zmv_pair
program define _zmv_pair, rclass
    args c twlog logfile
    _zax_tw `"twoway `c'"' "`twlog'"
    local tw = r(rc)
    local err `"`r(err)'"'
    // twoway's {p 0 8} message leaves its paragraph open; closed here, so
    // dash's log is not run into it.
    display as text "{p_end}"
    _ztp_run `"dash `c' name(zmv)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    local note = r(note)
    display as text "{p_end}"
    // twoway's fit types print their line through {p}: the tags are not
    // words.  lowess, lpoly, lpolyci and kdensity print theirs where the
    // quiet log does not keep it; their words (measured, E9) stand in.
    mata: st_local("err", strtrim(ustrregexra(st_local("err"), "[{][^}]*[}]", "")))
    if `tw' == 103 & `"`macval(err)'"' == "" local err "too many variables specified"
    local hit 1
    if `tw' {
        local hit 0
        if `"`macval(err)'"' != "" {
            cert_log_has "`logfile'", needle(`"`macval(err)'"')
            local hit = r(found)
        }
    }
    return scalar tw = `tw'
    return scalar rc = `rc'
    return scalar hit = `hit'
    return scalar note = `note'
    return local err `"`macval(err)'"'
end
// Each case group: the commands, the rc twoway and dash must both give.
cert_truth_ctx "MV-01"
local mv_cases ""
foreach tt in rarea rbar rcap rcapsym rconnected rline rscatter rspike {
    local mv_cases `"`mv_cases' `"`tt' lo hi weight, mlabvposition(p9)"'"'
}
local mv_cases `"`mv_cases' `"tsrline lo hi, mlabvposition(p9)"'"'
foreach tt in lfit qfit fpfit lfitci qfitci fpfitci mspline mband lowess lpoly lpolyci {
    local mv_cases `"`mv_cases' `"`tt' mpg weight, mlabvposition(p9)"'"'
}
local mv_cases `"`mv_cases' `"kdensity mpg, mlabvposition(p9)"'"'
local mv_want_01 103
local mv_02 `"`"rscatter mp tu wei, mlabel(ma) mlabvposition(q)"' `"lfit mp wei, mlabel(ma) mlabvposition(q)"' `"mspline mp wei, mlabel(ma) mlabvposition(q)"' `"lowess mp wei, mlabel(ma) mlabvposition(q)"'"'
local mv_03 `"`"rscatter lo hi weight, mlabvposition(sp9)"' `"lfit mpg weight, mlabvposition(sp9)"'"'
local mv_04 `"`"rscatter lo hi weight, mlabvposition(nosuch)"' `"lfit mpg weight, mlabvposition(nosuch)"' `"line mpg weight, mlabvposition(nosuch)"'"'
local mv_05 `"`"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabvposition(p9) mlabvposition(pos)"' `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabv(p9) mlabvposition(pos)"'"'
local mv_06 `"`"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabvposition(p9 pos)"'"'
local mv_07 `"`"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabvposition(p9*1)"'"'
local mv_11b `"`"rscatter lo hi weight, mlabel(. make) mlabvposition(p9)"'"'
foreach id in 01 02 03 04 05 06 07 11b {
    local want 103
    if "`id'" == "04" local want 111
    if inlist("`id'", "05", "07") local want 198
    local list : copy local mv_`id'
    if "`id'" == "01" local list : copy local mv_cases
    if "`id'" != "01" cert_truth_ctx "MV-`id'"
    local bad 0
    foreach c of local list {
        _zmv_pair `"`c'"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
        if r(tw) != `want' | r(rc) != `want' | r(hit) != 1 {
            display as error `"MV-`id' FAIL `c': twoway r(`r(tw)') dash r(`r(rc)'), twoway's line in dash's log `r(hit)': `r(err)'"'
            local bad 1
        }
    }
    if `bad' {
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' MV-`id'"
    }
    else if "`id'" == "01" display as text "MV-01 PASS: refused r(103) on the 21 counting types, in twoway's words"
    else if "`id'" == "02" display as text "MV-02 PASS: abbreviated variables and mlabel() named in full, as twoway names them"
    else if "`id'" == "03" display as text "MV-03 PASS: a string variable counts as a variable, r(103)"
    else if "`id'" == "04" display as text "MV-04 PASS: a variable that does not exist is r(111)"
    else if "`id'" == "05" display as text "MV-05 PASS: a second copy is r(198), option mlabvposition() not allowed"
    else if "`id'" == "06" display as text "MV-06 PASS: two names are r(103), too many names specified"
    else if "`id'" == "07" display as text "MV-07 PASS: an expression is r(198), invalid name"
    else if "`id'" == "11b" display as text "MV-11b PASS: mlabel(. make) counts make, r(103) as twoway"
}
// MV-08: the empty option and the abbreviations are taken, the variable
// unabbreviated, and the layer's other options kept (s() survives).
cert_truth_ctx "MV-08"
local bad 0
foreach c in `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabvposition() mcolor(red)"' `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabv(po) mcolor(red)"' `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabvp(pos) mcolor(red)"' `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabvposi(pos) mcolor(red)"' {
    _zmv_pair `"`c'"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
    local tw = r(tw)
    local rc = r(rc)
    local note = r(note)
    mata: st_local("v", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zmv", "mlabvposition", "pos")))
    mata: st_local("m", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zmv", "mlabel", "make") & _ztp_hasval("zmv", "mcolor", "red")))
    if strpos(`"`c'"', "mlabvposition()") local v = !`v'
    if `tw' | `rc' | `note' | !`v' | !`m' {
        display as error `"MV-08 FAIL `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), note `note', mlabvposition pos `v', mlabel and mcolor kept `m'"'
        local bad 1
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' MV-08"
}
else display as text "MV-08 PASS: mlabvposition() and its abbreviations taken, the name unabbreviated, the other options kept"
// MV-09: never read on histogram, function, scatteri, pci, pcarrowi.
cert_truth_ctx "MV-09"
local bad 0
foreach c in `"histogram mpg, mlabvposition(nosuch)"' `"function y = x, mlabvposition(nosuch)"' `"scatteri 1 1 2 2, mlabvposition(nosuch)"' `"pci 1 1 2 2, mlabvposition(nosuch)"' `"pcarrowi 1 1 2 2, mlabvposition(nosuch)"' {
    _zmv_pair `"`c'"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
    local tw = r(tw)
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_has zmv mlabvposition
    if `tw' | `rc' | r(found) {
        display as error `"MV-09 FAIL `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), the key in the spec `r(found)'"'
        local bad 1
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' MV-09"
}
else display as text "MV-09 PASS: not read where twoway never reads it"
// MV-10: checked, taken and silent where twoway draws no label.
cert_truth_ctx "MV-10"
local bad 0
foreach c in `"line mpg weight, mlabvposition(p9)"' `"spike mpg weight, mlabvposition(p9)"' `"area mpg weight, mlabvposition(p9)"' `"pcspike mpg weight turn length, mlabvposition(p9)"' `"tsline mpg, mlabvposition(p9)"' {
    _zmv_pair `"`c'"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
    local tw = r(tw)
    local rc = r(rc)
    local note = r(note)
    mata: st_local("v", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zmv", "mlabvposition", "p9")))
    if `tw' | `rc' | `note' | !`v' {
        display as error `"MV-10 FAIL `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), note `note', key `v'"'
        local bad 1
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' MV-10"
}
else display as text "MV-10 PASS: taken in silence where twoway draws no label"
// MV-11: twoway's count quirks -- a name already in the list adds nothing.
cert_truth_ctx "MV-11"
local bad 0
foreach c in `"rscatter lo hi weight, mlabvposition(lo)"' `"lfit mpg weight, mlabvposition(weight)"' `"rscatter lo hi weight, mlabel(lo) mlabvposition(p9)"' `"rscatter lo hi weight, mlabel(make) mlabvposition(make)"' {
    _zmv_pair `"`c'"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
    if r(tw) | r(rc) {
        display as error `"MV-11 FAIL `c': twoway r(`r(tw)') dash r(`r(rc)')"'
        local bad 1
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' MV-11"
}
else display as text "MV-11 PASS: twoway's count quirks are accepted as twoway accepts them"
// MV-12 (part 2): mlabtextstyle() is taken everywhere twoway takes it,
// silently, the rightmost copy kept and the abbreviation read.
cert_truth_ctx "MV-12"
local bad 0
foreach c in `"line mpg weight, mlabtextstyle(heading)"' `"lfit mpg weight, mlabtextstyle(heading)"' `"rscatter lo hi weight, mlabtextstyle(heading)"' `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabtextstyle(heading) mlabtextstyle(body)"' `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabt(heading)"' `"scatter mpg weight, mlabel(make) mlabtextstyle()"' {
    _zmv_pair `"`c'"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
    local tw = r(tw)
    local rc = r(rc)
    local note = r(note)
    local want "heading"
    if strpos(`"`c'"', "(body)") local want "body"
    mata: st_local("v", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zmv", "mlabtextstyle", st_local("want"))))
    if strpos(`"`c'"', "mlabtextstyle()") local v = 1
    if `tw' | `rc' | `note' | !`v' {
        display as error `"MV-12 FAIL `c': twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), note `note', mlabtextstyle `want' `v'"'
        local bad 1
    }
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' MV-12"
}
else display as text "MV-12 PASS: mlabtextstyle() taken in silence, the rightmost copy kept"
// MV-13 (part 2): a style list, one element per y; a bad list as twoway.
cert_truth_ctx "MV-13"
local bad 0
_zmv_pair `"scatter mpg turn weight, mlabel(make make) mlabtextstyle(heading body)"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
local tw = r(tw)
local rc = r(rc)
mata: st_local("v", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zmv", "mlabtextstyle", "heading") & _ztp_hasval("zmv", "mlabtextstyle", "body")))
if `tw' | `rc' | !`v' {
    display as error "MV-13 FAIL heading body: twoway r(`tw') dash r(`rc'), both styles kept `v'"
    local bad 1
}
_zmv_pair `"scatter mpg turn weight, mlabel(make make) mlabtextstyle(.. heading)"' "`mvlog'" "`logfile'"
if r(tw) != r(rc) {
    display as error "MV-13 FAIL .. heading: twoway r(`r(tw)') dash r(`r(rc)')"
    local bad 1
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' MV-13"
}
else display as text "MV-13 PASS: mlabtextstyle() is a style list, one element per y"
capture dash clear
capture erase "`mvlog'"
set linesize `mv_ls'
// RS: plotregion()/graphregion() sub-options, read as twoway reads them (WP-30 P1.20a)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// twoway's answers here are the region fixture's (test/fixtures/
// region_truth.json, scripts/extract_region_truth.do): its R probes'
// return codes and first error lines, its S probes' spellings.  Each row
// is written by Python to a tab file and read back by -file read-, so no
// typed region text is expanded as a macro inside Python.
local rsrows "`c(tmpdir)'dash_rs_rows.txt"
global ZRS_ROWS "`rsrows'"
python:
import json as _zrs_json
from sfi import Macro as _zrs_M
with open("fixtures/region_truth.json", encoding="utf-8") as _zrs_fh:
    _zrs_p = _zrs_json.load(_zrs_fh)["probes"]
# Each row's shortest spelling twoway takes (its minimum).
_zrs_min = {}
for _zrs_k, _zrs_r in _zrs_p.items():
    if _zrs_k.startswith("S|") and _zrs_r["rc"] == 0:
        _zrs_f, _zrs_t = _zrs_k.split("|")[1:]
        _zrs_min[_zrs_f] = min(_zrs_min.get(_zrs_f, 99), len(_zrs_t))
with open(_zrs_M.getGlobal("ZRS_ROWS"), "w", encoding="utf-8") as _zrs_out:
    for _zrs_k in sorted(_zrs_p):
        _zrs_r = _zrs_p[_zrs_k]
        _zrs_kind = _zrs_k
        if _zrs_k.startswith("S|"):
            # The minimum, the full name, one letter short and the capitals.
            _zrs_f, _zrs_t = _zrs_k.split("|")[1:]
            _zrs_kind = "S"
            if _zrs_t == _zrs_t.lower() and len(_zrs_t) not in (
                    _zrs_min[_zrs_f], _zrs_min[_zrs_f] - 1, len(_zrs_f)):
                continue
        elif not _zrs_k.startswith("R"):
            continue
        _zrs_opts = _zrs_r["cmd"].split(",", 1)[1].strip()
        _zrs_out.write("\t".join((_zrs_kind, str(_zrs_r["rc"]), _zrs_r["err"],
                                  _zrs_opts)) + "\n")
end
local b01 = 0
local b02 = 0
local b03 = 0
local b04 = 0
local n03 = 0
tempname rsfh
file open `rsfh' using "`rsrows'", read text
file read `rsfh' line
while r(eof) == 0 {
    mata: _zrs_f = tokens(st_local("line"), char(9)); _zrs_f = select(_zrs_f, _zrs_f :!= char(9))
    mata: st_local("rid", _zrs_f[1]); st_local("trc", _zrs_f[2])
    mata: st_local("terr", cols(_zrs_f) == 4 ? _zrs_f[3] : ""); st_local("ropts", _zrs_f[cols(_zrs_f)])
    _ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, `ropts' name(zrs)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local ok = (`drc' == `trc')
    if `ok' & `trc' & `"`terr'"' != "" {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" `"`terr'"'
        local ok = r(found)
    }
    local grp "04"
    if "`rid'" == "S" {
        local grp "03"
        local ++n03
    }
    else if inlist("`rid'", "R14", "R15", "R16", "R17") local grp "02"
    else if `trc' local grp "01"
    if !`ok' {
        display as error `"RS-`grp' FAIL `rid' `ropts': twoway r(`trc') `terr', dash r(`drc')"'
        local b`grp' = 1
    }
    file read `rsfh' line
}
file close `rsfh'
capture erase "`rsrows'"
macro drop ZRS_ROWS
capture dash clear
foreach g in 01 02 03 04 {
    if `b`g'' {
        local nfail = `nfail' + 1
        local faillist "`faillist' RS-`g'"
    }
}
if !`b01' display as text "RS-01 PASS: the region refusals twoway gives (unknown, capitalised, short, repeated, a comma) are dash's, rc and words"
if !`b02' display as text "RS-02 PASS: graphregion() is checked before plotregion(), both before legend() and the axis options"
if !`b03' display as text "RS-03 PASS: `n03' spellings: each sub-option from its minimum to its full name, and one letter short and the capitals refused, as twoway"
if !`b04' display as text "RS-04 PASS: a trailing comma, lalign(bogus), lpattern(bogus), margin(bogus), lcolor(notacolour) and lwidth(abc) are rc 0, as twoway"

// RS-10 and RS-12: copies merged by _dash_rep_merge as twoway applies them.
local b10 = 0
foreach row in ///
    "RS-10|plotregion|color(red)|c(blue)|color(blue)" ///
    "RS-10|plotregion|color(red)|lcolor(blue)|fcolor(red) lcolor(blue)" ///
    "RS-10|plotregion|lcolor(blue)|color(red)|color(red)" ///
    "RS-10|plotregion|fcolor(red)|style(none)|style(none)" ///
    "RS-10|plotregion|margin(zero)|margin(l+10)|margin(zero) margin(l+10)" ///
    "RS-10|graphregion|color(red)|margin(zero)|color(red) margin(zero)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|color(red)|lcolor(blue)|fcolor(red) lcolor(blue)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|lcolor(blue)|color(red)|color(red)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|color(red)|c(blue)|color(blue)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|fcolor(red)|style(none)|style(none)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|lcolor(red)|lstyle(none)|lstyle(none)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|fcolor(blue)|color(red)|color(red)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|color(red)|fcolor(blue)|lcolor(red) fcolor(blue)" ///
    "RS-12|plotregion|style(none)|fcolor(red)|style(none) fcolor(red)" ///
    "RS-12|graphregion|color(red)|lcolor(blue)|fcolor(red) lcolor(blue)" {
    mata: _zrs_f = tokens(st_local("row"), "|"); _zrs_f = select(_zrs_f, _zrs_f :!= "|")
    mata: st_local("mid", _zrs_f[1]); st_local("mgot", _dash_rep_merge(_zrs_f[2], _zrs_f[3], _zrs_f[4])); st_local("mwant", _zrs_f[5])
    if `"`mgot'"' != `"`mwant'"' {
        display as error `"`mid' FAIL `row': got `mgot'"'
        if "`mid'" == "RS-10" local b10 = 1
        else local b12 = 1
    }
}
if `b10' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RS-10"
}
else display as text "RS-10 PASS: repeated region copies merge as twoway applies them, every margin() kept"
if 0`b12' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RS-12"
}
else display as text "RS-12 PASS: the nine measured copy pairs (region_truth.json M01-M09) merge to the strings test_region_truth.py draws"

// RS-11: the spec of two abbreviated copies holds the merged full names.
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, plotregion(c(red)) plotregion(lc(blue)) name(zrs11)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
mata: st_local("hv", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zrs11", "plotregion", "fcolor(red) lcolor(blue)")))
capture dash clear
if `rc' | !`hv' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RS-11"
    display as error "RS-11 FAIL: r(`rc'), plotregion fcolor(red) lcolor(blue) `hv'"
}
else display as text "RS-11 PASS: plotregion(c(red)) plotregion(lc(blue)) is written fcolor(red) lcolor(blue)"
capture mata: mata drop _zrs_f

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// CM: connect() and cmissing(), read as twoway reads them (WP-30 P1.8a)
// twoway's answers are test/fixtures/connect_truth.json's probes, from
// scripts/extract_connect_truth.do (StataNow 19.5): the words below are
// its log lines, cited by probe id.  dash runs here.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture program drop _zcm_spec
program define _zcm_spec, rclass
    args needle
    mata: st_local("_zf", strofreal(strpos(st_global("dash_json_zqtp"), st_local("needle")) > 0))
    return scalar found = `_zf'
end
local cmq = char(34)
quietly tsset t

// CM-01: R-01, R-01s -- a misplaced .. is "connect(l .. J):  invalid syntax".
local bad 0
foreach tt in line scatter {
    _ztp_run `"dash `tt' mpg weight, c(l .. J) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "connect(l .. J):  invalid syntax"
    if `rc' != 198 | !r(found) local bad 1
}
if `bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-01"
    display as error "CM-01 FAIL: c(l .. J) is not r(198) connect(l .. J):  invalid syntax"
}
else display as text "CM-01 PASS: c(l .. J) refused r(198) in twoway's words"

// CM-02: R-02 -- "cmissings(n .. y):  invalid syntax", r(198).
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg turn weight, cmissing(n .. y) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "cmissings(n .. y):  invalid syntax"
if `rc' != 198 | !r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-02"
    display as error "CM-02 FAIL: cmissing(n .. y) r(`rc')"
}
else display as text "CM-02 PASS: cmissing(n .. y) refused r(198) as cmissings(n .. y)"

// CM-03: R-03, R-10, R-11, R-12 and the matrix's cmissing(x) rc 101 rows --
// two notes, then " not allowed", r(101), on every type twoway refuses it.
local bad ""
foreach tt in line connected lfit qfit fpfit lpoly lowess mspline mband kdensity function tsline lfitci qfitci lpolyci fpfitci rline rconnected tsrline {
    local v `v_`tt''
    local sep ","
    if strpos("`v'", ",") local sep ""
    foreach o in "cmissing(x)" "cmissing(N)" {
        _ztp_run `"dash `tt' `v'`sep' `o' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
        local rc = r(rc)
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "not found in class yesno, default attributes used)"
        local n1 = r(found)
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "(note:  yesno not found in scheme, default attributes used)"
        if `rc' != 101 | !`n1' | !r(found) local bad "`bad' `tt'/`o'"
    }
}
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg turn weight, cmissing(n x) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 101 local bad "`bad' line/cmissing(n x)"
// R_EXTRA: an element past the last y is not read.
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, cmissing(n x) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) != 0 local bad "`bad' R_EXTRA"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-03"
    display as error "CM-03 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-03 PASS: an unknown cmissing() is r(101) after twoway's two notes on the 19 types"

// CM-04: the matrix's cmissing(x) rc 0 rows: bar, area take it with notes.
local bad ""
foreach tt in bar area {
    _ztp_run `"dash `tt' mpg weight, cmissing(x) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "(note:  yesno not found in scheme, default attributes used)"
    if `rc' != 0 | !r(found) local bad "`bad' `tt'"
}
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-04"
    display as error "CM-04 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-04 PASS: cmissing(x) on bar and area: rc 0, twoway's notes"

// CM-05: P07, S-c-Direct -- an unknown name is noted and drawn direct.
local bad ""
foreach tt in scatter line bar {
    foreach o in bogus Direct {
        _ztp_run `"dash `tt' mpg weight, c(`o') name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
        local rc = r(rc)
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "(note:  named style `o' not found in class connectstyle"
        local nf = r(found)
        _zcm_spec `"`cmq'connect`cmq':`cmq'direct`cmq'"'
        if `rc' != 0 | !`nf' | !r(found) local bad "`bad' `tt'/`o'"
    }
}
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-05"
    display as error "CM-05 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-05 PASS: c(bogus), c(Direct): twoway's note, drawn direct"

// CM-06: R-07, R-08, P28 -- a scatter given connect() takes the cl options.
local bad ""
foreach o in l i {
    _ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, c(`o') clwidth(-1) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "gm_linewidth must be between 0.000 and  1.0e+04"
    if `rc' != 198 | !r(found) local bad "`bad' c(`o')"
}
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, c(l) clcolor(red) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zcm_spec `"`cmq'clcolor`cmq':`cmq'red`cmq'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' clcolor"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-06"
    display as error "CM-06 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-06 PASS: clwidth(-1) r(198) under c(l) and c(i); clcolor() kept"

// CM-07: P26, P27 -- sort and sort(varlist) are honoured, not named.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, c(l) sort name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) | r(note) local bad "`bad' sort"
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg turn weight, c(l) sort(turn) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zcm_spec `"`cmq'sortvars`cmq':`cmq'turn`cmq'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' sort(turn)"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-07"
    display as error "CM-07 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-07 PASS: sort and sort(varlist) on a scatter given c(l), not named"

// CM-08: R-05, R-06 and the S block -- spellings read as twoway reads them.
local bad ""
foreach o in "cmissings(n)" "cmiss(n)" {
    _ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, `o' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    _zcm_spec `"`cmq'cmissing`cmq':`cmq'n`cmq'"'
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' `o'"
}
foreach p in "stair stairstep" "u stepstair" "a ascending" "L ascending" "l direct" "i none" {
    gettoken o c : p
    local c = strtrim("`c'")
    _ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, c(`o') name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    _zcm_spec `"`cmq'connect`cmq':`cmq'`c'`cmq'"'
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' c(`o')"
}
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-08"
    display as error "CM-08 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-08 PASS: cmissings(), cmiss() and the connect spellings read as twoway reads them"

// CM-09: P25, R-09 -- the rightmost copy counts.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, c(l) c(J) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zcm_spec `"`cmq'connect`cmq':`cmq'stairstep`cmq'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' connect"
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, cmissing(n) cmissing(y) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zcm_spec `"`cmq'cmissing`cmq':`cmq'y`cmq'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' cmissing"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-09"
    display as error "CM-09 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-09 PASS: of two copies the rightmost counts"

// CM-10: the matrix's same_as_base rows -- silent where twoway draws the
// same picture.
local bad ""
foreach tt in bar spike dot histogram pcspike {
    local v `v_`tt''
    foreach o in "c(J)" "cmissing(n)" {
        _ztp_run `"dash `tt' `v', `o' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
        if r(rc) | r(note) local bad "`bad' `tt'/`o'"
    }
}
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-10"
    display as error "CM-10 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-10 PASS: c(J) and cmissing(n) are taken in silence where twoway draws the same picture"

// CM-11: drawn and not named.  Flipped (WP-31 C6): "named, not drawn"
// (P2.42, P2.43) was wrong because twoway splits area and rarea and
// breaks lowess at their missing points and steps rarea's bounds, and
// dash now draws them so (area_cmissing_truth.json A01, R01, E01).
local bad ""
foreach c in "area mpg weight, cmissing(n)|cmissing()" "rarea lo hi weight, c(J)|connect()" "lowess mpg weight, cmissing(n)|cmissing()" {
    gettoken cmd nm : c, parse("|")
    local nm = substr("`nm'", 2, .)
    _ztp_run `"dash `cmd' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`nm'"
    if `rc' | r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'"
}
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-11"
    display as error "CM-11 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-11 PASS: cmissing(n) on area and lowess, c(J) on rarea are drawn and not named"

// CM-12: P20, P23 -- per y: a scatter y given an element is connected.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg turn weight, c(l) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zcm_spec `"{`cmq'type`cmq':`cmq'connected`cmq',`cmq'yvar`cmq':`cmq'mpg`cmq',`cmq'xvar`cmq':`cmq'weight`cmq',`cmq'options`cmq':{`cmq'connect`cmq':`cmq'direct`cmq'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' P20-1"
_zcm_spec `"{`cmq'type`cmq':`cmq'scatter`cmq',`cmq'yvar`cmq':`cmq'turn`cmq',`cmq'xvar`cmq':`cmq'weight`cmq',`cmq'options`cmq':{}"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' P20-2"
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg turn length weight, c(J =) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
foreach y in mpg turn {
    _zcm_spec `"{`cmq'type`cmq':`cmq'connected`cmq',`cmq'yvar`cmq':`cmq'`y'`cmq',`cmq'xvar`cmq':`cmq'weight`cmq',`cmq'options`cmq':{`cmq'connect`cmq':`cmq'stairstep`cmq'"'
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' P23-`y'"
}
_zcm_spec `"{`cmq'type`cmq':`cmq'scatter`cmq',`cmq'yvar`cmq':`cmq'length`cmq'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' P23-length"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' CM-12"
    display as error "CM-12 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "CM-12 PASS: each y given a connect() element is connected, the others scatter"
capture program drop _zcm_spec
quietly tsset, clear

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// RC: recast(), read as twoway reads it (WP-30 P1.8b)
// twoway's answers are test/fixtures/recast_truth.json's probes, from
// scripts/extract_recast_truth.do (StataNow 19.5): the words below are
// its log lines.  dash runs here.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
capture program drop _zrc_spec
program define _zrc_spec, rclass
    args needle
    mata: st_local("_zf", strofreal(strpos(st_global("dash_json_zqtp"), st_local("needle")) > 0))
    return scalar found = `_zf'
end
local q = char(34)
local nyn "(note:  yxtype not found in scheme, default attributes used)"

// RC-01: the ci fits refuse recast(), recastas() and type(), r(198).
local bad ""
foreach tt in lfitci qfitci lpolyci fpfitci {
    foreach o in recast recastas type {
        _ztp_run `"dash `tt' mpg weight, `o'(line) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
        local rc = r(rc)
        local w "recastas"
        if "`o'" == "type" local w "type"
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`w'() option not allowed"
        if `rc' != 198 | !r(found) local bad "`bad' `tt'/`o'"
    }
}
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-01"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-01 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-01 PASS: recast(), recastas() and type() on the ci fits are r(198) in twoway's words"

// RC-02: rec() is "option rec() not allowed", r(198).
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, rec(line) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option rec() not allowed"
if `rc' != 198 | !r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RC-02"
    display as error "RC-02 FAIL: rec(line) r(`rc')"
}
else display as text "RC-02 PASS: rec() refused r(198) as twoway refuses it"

// RC-03: a scatter recast as line is a line, the typed type kept.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, recast(line) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) | r(note) local bad "`bad' rc/note"
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'line`q',`q'recast_from`q':`q'scatter`q',`q'yvar`q':`q'mpg`q'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' spec"
_zrc_spec `"`q'recast`q':"'
if r(found) local bad "`bad' recast-key"
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-03"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-03 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-03 PASS: scatter, recast(line) is written as a line"

// RC-04: fallbacks with twoway's two notes (probes FB-*).
local bad ""
foreach row in "line mpg weight, recast(rline)|scatter|rline|yxtype" ///
               "rline lo hi weight, recast(pcspike)|rspike|pcspike|y2xtype" ///
               "pcspike mpg weight turn length, recast(line)|pcspike|line|yxyxtype" ///
               "function y=x, range(1 5) recast(rline)|function|rline|functiontype" {
    gettoken cmd row : row, parse("|")
    gettoken _p row : row, parse("|")
    gettoken want row : row, parse("|")
    gettoken _p row : row, parse("|")
    gettoken nm row : row, parse("|")
    gettoken _p cls : row, parse("|")
    _ztp_run `"dash `cmd' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    if r(rc) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/rc"
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "(note:  named style `nm' not found in class `cls', default attributes used)"
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/note1"
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "(note:  `cls' not found in scheme, default attributes used)"
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/note2"
    _zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'`want'`q'"'
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/type"
}
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-04"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-04 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-04 PASS: out-of-class names fall back with twoway's two notes"

// RC-05: precedence -- recast()/recastas() over type(), rightmost of each.
local bad ""
foreach row in "recast(line) type(bar)|line" "type(bar) recast(line)|line" ///
               "recastas(bar) recast(line)|line" "recast(line) recast(bar)|bar" ///
               "type(line) type(bar)|bar" "recasta(line)|line" "ty(line)|line" {
    gettoken o row : row, parse("|")
    local want = substr("`row'", 2, .)
    _ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, `o' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    local rc = r(rc)
    _zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'`want'`q',`q'recast_from`q'"'
    if `rc' | !r(found) local bad "`bad' `o'"
}
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-05"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-05 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-05 PASS: recast() and recastas() beat type(), the rightmost copy wins"

// RC-06: spellings and case (probes SP-*).
local bad ""
foreach row in "scatter mpg weight, recast(li)|line|" "line mpg weight, recast(sc)|scatter|" ///
               "scatter mpg weight, recast(co)|connected|" "scatter mpg weight, recast(b)|bar|" ///
               "rline lo hi weight, recast(rsc)|rscatter|" "scatter mpg weight, recast(rsc)|scatter|rsc" ///
               "rline lo hi weight, recast(rbarm)|rbar|" ///
               "pcspike mpg weight turn length, recast(pcbar)|pcbarrow|" ///
               "pcspike mpg weight turn length, recast(pccaps)|pccapsym|" ///
               "pcspike mpg weight turn length, recast(pcl)|pcspike|pcline" ///
               "scatter mpg weight, recast(LINE)|scatter|LINE" "line mpg weight, recast(l)|scatter|l" {
    gettoken cmd row : row, parse("|")
    gettoken _p row : row, parse("|")
    gettoken want row : row, parse("|")
    local nm = substr("`row'", 2, .)
    _ztp_run `"dash `cmd' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    if r(rc) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/rc"
    _zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'`want'`q'"'
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/type"
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "(note:  named style `nm' not found in class"
    if "`nm'" != "" & !r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/note"
    if "`nm'" == "" {
        _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "(note:  named style"
        if r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/a-note"
    }
}
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-06"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-06 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-06 PASS: twoway's spellings by class, case-sensitive"

// RC-07: dot, pci and histogram's range targets are named.
// Flipped (WP-31 B5a): dot was silent, which was wrong because twoway
// reads recast() on dot and draws the dot graph unchanged (rc 0, the
// same SVG; test/fixtures/rbar_dot_truth.json), so the option the user
// gave is named rather than dropped in silence.
// Flipped (WP-32): recast() on dot named was wrong, because twoway draws
// the same picture and says nothing (noted_option_truth.json;
// BUGS.md "dash names options twoway takes and draws nothing of, where twoway is silent"): taken in silence.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash dot mpg weight, recast(line) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) | r(note) local bad "`bad' dot"
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "recast()"
if r(found) local bad "`bad' dot/named"
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'dot`q'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' dot/type"
// Flipped (WP-31 C7): pci's and histogram's range targets named was
// wrong because twoway draws them as the type named
// (area_cmissing_truth.json P01, H07); dash now draws them, writes the
// target as options.recast and names nothing.
foreach cmd in "pci 20 3000 30 4000, recast(pcarrow)|pcarrow" "histogram mpg, recast(rline)|rline" {
    gettoken cmd tg : cmd, parse("|")
    local tg = substr("`tg'", 2, .)
    _ztp_run `"dash `cmd' name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
    if r(rc) local bad "`bad' `cmd'"
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "recast()"
    if r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/named"
    _zrc_spec `"`q'recast`q':`q'`tg'`q'"'
    if !r(found) local bad "`bad' `cmd'/spec"
}
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-07"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-07 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-07 PASS: recast() on dot is taken in silence; pci's and histogram's range targets are drawn and not named"

// RC-08: one value for every y; a two-name value is an unknown name.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg turn weight, recast(line line) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'line`q',`q'recast_from`q':`q'scatter`q',`q'yvar`q':`q'turn`q'"'
if `rc' | !r(found) local bad "`bad' line-line"
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg turn weight, recast(line scatter) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`nyn'"
if `rc' | !r(found) local bad "`bad' line-scatter/note"
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'line`q'"'
if r(found) local bad "`bad' line-scatter/type"
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-08"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-08 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-08 PASS: recast() is one value for every y"

// RC-09: tsline recast joins in time order.
quietly tsset t
_ztp_run `"dash tsline mpg, recast(connected) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'connected`q',`q'recast_from`q':`q'tsline`q'"'
local f1 = r(found)
_zrc_spec `"`q'sortvars`q':`q't`q'"'
if !`f1' | !r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RC-09"
    display as error "RC-09 FAIL: tsline, recast(connected)"
}
else display as text "RC-09 PASS: tsline, recast(connected) is connected in time order"
quietly tsset, clear

// RC-10: a range type cast to a yx name draws its first bound.
_ztp_run `"dash rline lo hi weight, recast(line) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'line`q',`q'recast_from`q':`q'rline`q',`q'yvar`q':`q'lo`q',`q'xvar`q':`q'weight`q'"'
local f1 = r(found)
_zrc_spec `"`q'yvar2`q'"'
if !`f1' | r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RC-10"
    display as error "RC-10 FAIL: rline, recast(line)"
}
else display as text "RC-10 PASS: rline, recast(line) is a line of the first bound"

// RC-11: a derived layer keeps its type and records the target.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash lfit mpg weight, recast(scatter) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'lfit`q',`q'yvar`q'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' type"
_zrc_spec `"`q'recast`q':`q'scatter`q'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' target"
_ztp_run `"dash lfit mpg weight, recast(rline) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "`nyn'"
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' rline/note"
_zrc_spec `"`q'recast`q':`q'scatter`q'"'
if !r(found) local bad "`bad' rline/target"
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-11"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-11 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-11 PASS: lfit, recast(scatter) keeps lfit and is drawn as scatter"

// RC-12: connect() judges the drawn type (twoway's yxview order).
_ztp_run `"dash line mpg weight, recast(scatter) c(l) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
local rc = r(rc)
_zrc_spec `"{`q'type`q':`q'connected`q',`q'recast_from`q':`q'line`q'"'
if `rc' | !r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RC-12"
    display as error "RC-12 FAIL: line, recast(scatter) c(l)"
}
else display as text "RC-12 PASS: line, recast(scatter) c(l) is connected"

// RC-13: each later step judges the right type.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"dash lfit mpg weight, recast(scatter) msymbol(O) name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) | r(note) local bad "`bad' lfit/msymbol"
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, recast(line) sort name(zqtp)"' "`logfile'"
if r(rc) | r(note) local bad "`bad' scatter/sort"
if "`bad'" != "" local faillist "`faillist' RC-13"
if "`bad'" != "" local nfail = `nfail' + 1
if "`bad'" != "" display as error "RC-13 FAIL:`bad'"
else display as text "RC-13 PASS: a recast layer's options are judged on the drawn type"
capture program drop _zrc_spec

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// RM: plot-region margins and inner box (WP-30 P1.20b)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Live twoway and dash, rc and notes from the logs.
local rm_ls = c(linesize)
set linesize 255
local rmpg "`c(tmpdir)'dash_rm_page.html"
// The data in memory are kept: the cases before and after read lo/hi.
// RM-01: an unknown margin is twoway's note, word for word.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"twoway scatter mpg weight, plotregion(margin(bogus))"' "`logfile'"
local trc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "named style bogus not found in class margin, default attributes used"
local tf = r(found)
quietly graph drop _all
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, plotregion(margin(bogus)) saving("`rmpg'", replace)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "named style bogus not found in class margin, default attributes used"
if `trc' | `drc' | !`tf' | !r(found) local bad " rc `trc'/`drc', notes `tf'/`=r(found)'"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RM-01"
    display as error "RM-01 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "RM-01 PASS: plotregion(margin(bogus)) is rc 0 with twoway's note in both"
// RM-02: the documented forms are rc 0 and draw with no note.
local bad ""
foreach m in "margin(zero)" "margin(l+10)" "mar(t-5)" "m(1 2 3 4)" "margin(10-pt)" {
    _ztp_run `"twoway scatter mpg weight, plotregion(`m')"' "`logfile'"
    local trc = r(rc)
    quietly graph drop _all
    _ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, plotregion(`m') saving("`rmpg'", replace)"' "`logfile'"
    local drc = r(rc)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "class margin"
    local f1 = r(found)
    _ztp_logged "`logfile'" "plotregion() sub-option"
    if `trc' | `drc' | `f1' | r(found) local bad "`bad' `m': rc `trc'/`drc'"
}
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RM-02"
    display as error "RM-02 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "RM-02 PASS: zero, l+10, mar(t-5), m(1 2 3 4) and 10-pt are rc 0 in both, with no dash note"
// RM-03: two margin() in one copy is refused as twoway refuses it.
_ztp_run `"twoway scatter mpg weight, plotregion(margin(zero) margin(l+10))"' "`logfile'"
local trc = r(rc)
quietly graph drop _all
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, plotregion(margin(zero) margin(l+10)) saving("`rmpg'", replace)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "option margin() not allowed"
if `trc' != 198 | `drc' != 198 | !r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RM-03"
    display as error "RM-03 FAIL: rc `trc'/`drc'"
}
else display as text "RM-03 PASS: margin() twice in one plotregion() is r(198) in both"
// RM-04: graphregion's inner outline is named, not drawn.  Flipped
// (WP-31 D11): margin(l+10) and ifcolor(red) were named; that was wrong
// because twoway draws them, and dash now does (_dash_graph_margin, the
// border fill), so only ilc(blue) is named.
local bad ""
_ztp_run `"twoway scatter mpg weight, graphregion(margin(l+10) ifcolor(red) ilc(blue))"' "`logfile'"
local trc = r(rc)
quietly graph drop _all
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, graphregion(margin(l+10) ifcolor(red) ilc(blue)) saving("`rmpg'", replace)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "graphregion() sub-option(s) not implemented and ignored: ilc(blue)"
local f1 = r(found)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "plotregion() sub-option"
if `trc' | `drc' | !`f1' | r(found) local bad " rc `trc'/`drc', named `f1'"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RM-04"
    display as error "RM-04 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "RM-04 PASS: graphregion(margin() ifcolor() ilc()) is rc 0 and names ilc() only, no plotregion note"
// RM-05: plotregion's ilalign() is still named; ifcolor() is drawn.
_ztp_run `"twoway scatter mpg weight, plotregion(ifcolor(red) ilalign(inside))"' "`logfile'"
local trc = r(rc)
quietly graph drop _all
_ztp_run `"dash scatter mpg weight, plotregion(ifcolor(red) ilalign(inside)) saving("`rmpg'", replace)"' "`logfile'"
local drc = r(rc)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "plotregion() sub-option(s) not implemented and ignored: ilalign(inside)"
local f1 = r(found)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "ignored: ilalign(inside) ifcolor"
local f2 = r(found)
_ztp_logged "`logfile'" "ignored: ifcolor"
if `trc' | `drc' | !`f1' | `f2' | r(found) {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' RM-05"
    display as error "RM-05 FAIL: rc `trc'/`drc', named `f1'/`f2'"
}
else display as text "RM-05 PASS: plotregion(ifcolor() ilalign()) is rc 0 and names ilalign() only"
capture dash clear
capture erase "`rmpg'"
set linesize `rm_ls'

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// TA: the t-options, read as twoway reads them (WP-30 P1.6)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// tlabel() ttick() tmlabel() tmtick() ttitle() tscale() tline() fold onto
// x axis 1 after the x options, each date literal in the unit of the
// axis's label format (test/fixtures/taxis_truth.json holds the same
// probes; scripts/extract_taxis_truth.do).  Each case asks twoway (rc and
// the first line of its log) and dash (rc, first line, the registered
// spec of graph zta).  The data are the extractor's 60 months, put in
// memory here and the script's own restored after the block.
cert_truth_ctx "TA"
local ta_ls = c(linesize)
set linesize 255
global zta_log "`c(tmpdir)'dash_zta.log"
capture mata: mata drop _zta_line()
capture mata: mata drop _zta_same()
mata:
// The first line of a probe's log that is no header, rule, note or
// registration message: the error twoway or dash printed, or "".
string scalar _zta_line(string scalar path)
{
    string colvector L
    string scalar    s
    real scalar      i

    L = cat(path)
    for (i = 1; i <= rows(L); i++) {
        s = strtrim(subinstr(L[i], char(160), " "))
        if (s == "" | substr(s, 1, 1) == "-" | substr(s, 1, 1) == "(") continue
        if (substr(s, 1, 5) == "name:" | substr(s, 1, 4) == "log:" |
            substr(s, 1, 9) == "log type:" | substr(s, 1, 10) == "opened on:" |
            substr(s, 1, 10) == "closed on:" | substr(s, 1, 6) == "dash: ") continue
        return(s)
    }
    return("")
}
real scalar _zta_same(string scalar a, string scalar b)
{
    return(st_local(a) == st_local(b))
}
end
capture program drop _zta_data
program define _zta_data
    clear
    quietly set obs 60
    quietly generate t = tm(2000m1) + _n - 1
    format t %tm
    quietly tsset t
    quietly generate y = 100 + _n
    quietly generate y2 = y + 5
    quietly generate n = _n
    quietly generate d = dofm(t)
    format d %td
    quietly generate w = wofd(d)
    format w %tw
    quietly generate q = qofd(d)
    format q %tq
    quietly generate h = hofd(d)
    format h %th
    quietly generate yr = yofd(d) + _n
    format yr %ty
    quietly generate double tc = cofd(d)
    format tc %tc
    quietly generate tmon = t
    format tmon %tmMon_CCYY
    quietly generate t2 = t
    format t2 %-tm
end
// _zta_cmp `"<twoway arguments, ending in options>"': twoway (with nodraw)
// and dash (with name(zta)) on it.  Sets the caller's _zta_trc/_zta_drc
// (rcs), _zta_tl/_zta_dl (first lines) and _zta_note (dash's ignoring
// note present); the dash spec is $dash_json_zta.
capture program drop _zta_cmp
program define _zta_cmp
    args a
    _ztp_run `"twoway `a' nodraw"' "$zta_log"
    local trc = r(rc)
    mata: st_local("tl", _zta_line(st_global("zta_log")))
    _ztp_run `"dash `a' name(zta)"' "$zta_log"
    local drc = r(rc)
    local note = r(note)
    mata: st_local("dl", _zta_line(st_global("zta_log")))
    c_local _zta_trc `trc'
    c_local _zta_drc `drc'
    c_local _zta_note `note'
    c_local _zta_tl : copy local tl
    c_local _zta_dl : copy local dl
end
// _zta_val `"<arguments>"' key `"<value>"': twoway and dash rc 0, and the
// spec's key holds value (JSON-escaped); _zta_bad says what differed.
capture program drop _zta_val
program define _zta_val
    args a key val
    _zta_cmp `"`a'"'
    local bad ""
    if `_zta_trc' | `_zta_drc' local bad " [`a': rc `_zta_trc'/`_zta_drc' `_zta_dl']"
    else {
        mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zta", st_local("key"), st_local("val"))))
        if !`ok' {
            mata: st_local("js", st_global("dash_json_zta"))
            local bad " [`a': `key' not `val' in `js']"
        }
    }
    c_local _zta_bad : copy local bad
    c_local _zta_trc `_zta_trc'
    c_local _zta_drc `_zta_drc'
end
// _zta_err `"<arguments>"': dash's rc and first line are twoway's.
capture program drop _zta_err
program define _zta_err
    args a
    _zta_cmp `"`a'"'
    local bad ""
    mata: st_local("same", strofreal(_zta_same("_zta_tl", "_zta_dl")))
    if `_zta_trc' != `_zta_drc' | !`same' {
        local bad " [`a': twoway `_zta_trc' `_zta_tl' | dash `_zta_drc' `_zta_dl']"
    }
    c_local _zta_bad : copy local bad
    c_local _zta_trc `_zta_trc'
    c_local _zta_drc `_zta_drc'
end
preserve
_zta_data

// TA-01: the Overview's command folds every option onto its x key, with
// the date literals as twoway reads them on a %tm axis, and no note
// names them.
local bad ""
_zta_cmp `"tsline y, tlabel(2000m1(12)2004m1) ttitle("Month") tline(2002m1) tscale(range(1999m1 2006m1)) ttick(2000m7(12)2004m7)"'
if `_zta_trc' | `_zta_drc' | `_zta_note' local bad " rc `_zta_trc'/`_zta_drc' note `_zta_note'"
// Flipped (WP-31 D1c): a lone a(b)c reaches the renderer as typed (it
// expands it), so the rules are 480(12)528 and 486(12)534.
foreach kv in "xlabel|480(12)528" "xtick|486(12)534" "xline|504" "xscale|range(468 552)" {
    gettoken k v : kv, parse("|")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zta", st_local("k"), st_local("v"))))
    if !`ok' local bad "`bad' `k'"
}
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zta", "xtitle", char(92) + char(34) + "Month" + char(92) + char(34))))
if !`ok' local bad "`bad' xtitle"
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(strpos(st_global("dash_json_zta"), char(34) + "t") > 0 & (strpos(st_global("dash_json_zta"), char(34) + "tlabel") | strpos(st_global("dash_json_zta"), char(34) + "tline")) > 0))
if `ok' local bad "`bad' t-key"
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-01"
    mata: st_local("js", st_global("dash_json_zta"))
    display as error `"TA-01 FAIL:`bad' (`js')"'
}
else display as text "TA-01 PASS: the five options fold onto xlabel xtick xtitle xline xscale in twoway's numbers"

// TA-02: the T copy after every X copy, a later copy replacing or merging
// as twoway's does, lines accumulating, in a plot group and after ||,
// and tlabel(2001m1, add) stored as xlabel "492, add" (S52 draws it).
local bad ""
foreach c in ///
    `"tsline y, xlabel(480(12)528) tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)!xlabel!492 516"' ///
    `"tsline y, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1) xlabel(480(12)528)!xlabel!492 516"' ///
    `"tsline y, tlabel(2001m1) tlabel(2003m1)!xlabel!516"' ///
    `"tsline y, xtitle("X") ttitle("T")!xtitle!\"T\""' ///
    `"tsline y, ttitle("T") xtitle("X")!xtitle!\"T\""' ///
    `"tsline y, tline(2002m1) xline(490)!xline!490, 504"' ///
    `"tsline y, tline(2002m1) tline(2003m1)!xline!504, 516"' ///
    `"tsline y, tscale(range(1999m1)) tscale(range(2006m1))!xscale!range(468 552)"' ///
    `"(tsline y, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)) (line y2 t),!xlabel!492 516"' ///
    `"tsline y || line y2 t, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)!xlabel!492 516"' ///
    `"tsline y, tlabel(2001m1, add)!xlabel!492, add"' {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : rest, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : v, parse("!")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    _zta_val `"`a'"' `k' `"`v'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-02"
    display as error `"TA-02 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-02 PASS: T after X, the last copy or the union, lines added, in groups and after ||, and add kept"

// TA-03: twoway's abbreviations (its minimums; the plurals are routed
// with axis(), TA-11), t() still t1title(), tm() and ts() refused.
local bad ""
foreach c in "tl(2001m1 2003m1)|xlabel|492 516" "tlab(2001m1 2003m1)|xlabel|492 516" ///
    "tt(M)|xtitle|M" "tti(M)|xtitle|M" "ttit(M)|xtitle|M" ///
    "tli(2002m1)|xline|504" "tlin(2002m1)|xline|504" ///
    "ttic(2001m1 2003m1)|xtick|492 516" "ttick(2001m1 2003m1)|xtick|492 516" ///
    "tsc(range(1999m1))|xscale|range(468)" "tsca(range(1999m1))|xscale|range(468)" ///
    "tml(2001m1)|xmlabel|492" "tmt(2001m1)|xmtick|492" {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("|")
    gettoken k v : rest, parse("|")
    gettoken k v : v, parse("|")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    _zta_val `"tsline y, `a'"' `k' `"`v'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
}
foreach a in "tm(2001m1)" "ts(range(1999m1))" {
    _zta_err `"tsline y, `a'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    if `_zta_drc' != 198 local bad `"`bad' [`a' rc `_zta_drc']"'
}
_zta_cmp `"tsline y, t("x")"'
_ztp_logged "$zta_log" "t1title()"
// Flipped (WP-31 D2): !r(found) -- t() named as t1title() in the note --
// was wrong because dash draws t1title() now, as twoway does: not named.
if `_zta_trc' | `_zta_drc' | r(found) local bad `"`bad' [t(): rc `_zta_trc'/`_zta_drc' named `=r(found)']"'
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-03"
    display as error `"TA-03 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-03 PASS: tl tlab tt tti ttit tli tlin ttic ttick tsc tsca tml tmt read as twoway's; t() is t1title(); tm() ts() r(198)"

// TA-04: the unit is the axis's label format: d w m q h y; %tc, an
// unformatted x and a numeric first plot take numbers only; %tmMon_CCYY
// reads m(); an operated x keeps its variable's unit; tscale(log) on a
// date axis gives xscale(log)'s note at build.
local bad ""
foreach c in ///
    "line y d, tlabel(01jan2000 01apr2000 01jul2000)|xlabel|14610 14701 14792" ///
    "line y w, tline(2000w20)|xline|2099" ///
    "line y t, tline(2002m1)|xline|504" ///
    "line y q, tline(2001q1)|xline|164" ///
    "line y h, tline(2002h1)|xline|84" ///
    "line y yr, tline(2020)|xline|2020" ///
    "line y tc, tline(1300000000000)|xline|1300000000000" ///
    "line y tmon, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)|xlabel|492 516" ///
    "line y L.t, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)|xlabel|492 516" ///
    "line y D.t, tlabel(2001m1)|xlabel|492" ///
    "pcspike y t y2 d, tline(2002m1)|xline|504" {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("|")
    gettoken k v : rest, parse("|")
    gettoken k v : v, parse("|")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    _zta_val `"`a'"' `k' `"`v'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
}
foreach a in "line y tc, tlabel(2000m1)" "line y n, tlabel(2000m1)" ///
    "line y n, tline(2002m1)" "line y d, tline(2000m3)" ///
    "(line y d) (line y t), tline(2002m1)" "pcspike y d y2 t, tline(2002m1)" {
    _zta_err `"`a'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    if !`_zta_drc' local bad `"`bad' [`a' rc 0]"'
}
local tapg "`c(tmpdir)'dash_zta_page.html"
foreach o in tscale xscale {
    capture dash clear
    quietly graph drop _all
    capture log close _ztalog
    quietly log using "$zta_log", name(_ztalog) text replace
    capture noisily dash tsline y, `o'(log) name(zl)
    capture noisily dash build, saving("`tapg'", replace)
    local rc_`o' = _rc
    quietly log close _ztalog
    cert_log_has "$zta_log", needle("xscale(log) is meaningless for the date variable")
    local n_`o' = r(found)
}
if `rc_tscale' | `rc_xscale' | !`n_tscale' | !`n_xscale' local bad `"`bad' [log: rc `rc_tscale'/`rc_xscale' note `n_tscale'/`n_xscale']"'
capture erase "`tapg'"
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-04"
    display as error `"TA-04 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-04 PASS: d w m q h y units, numbers on %tc and numeric axes, the first plot's unit, operators, and tscale(log)'s note"

// TA-05: twoway's refusals of the t-options, rc and words.
local bad ""
foreach a in "tlabel(foo)" "tline(foo)" "tscale(range(foo))" "tlabel(2000m13)" ///
    "tline(2000m13)" "tline(2002m1 foo)" `"tlabel(2000m1(12)2004m1 "x")"' ///
    "tline(2000m6.5)" "tlabel(2000.5m1)" "tlabel(2000m1;2001m1)" ///
    "tlabel(2000m1,2001m1)" "tline(2000m1(1)2400m1)" `"tlabel("a" 2000m1)"' {
    _zta_err `"tsline y, `a'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    if !`_zta_drc' local bad `"`bad' [`a' rc 0]"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-05"
    display as error `"TA-05 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-05 PASS: every t-option refusal is twoway's rc and words"

// TA-06: the first plot decides: a date literal is refused after the
// eleven numeric-x types and read after every other (42 types; rpcap
// and rpspike since WP-31 B1, measured here beside dash).
local bad ""
local m6 `"rpcap "rpcap y y2 y t" rpspike "rpspike y y2 y t" scatter "scatter y t" line "line y t" connected "connected y t" scatteri "scatteri 100 480" area "area y t" bar "bar y t" spike "spike y t" dropline "dropline y t" dot "dot y t" rarea "rarea y y2 t" rbar "rbar y y2 t" rspike "rspike y y2 t" rcap "rcap y y2 t" rcapsym "rcapsym y y2 t" rscatter "rscatter y y2 t" rline "rline y y2 t" rconnected "rconnected y y2 t" pcspike "pcspike y t y2 t" pccapsym "pccapsym y t y2 t" pcarrow "pcarrow y t y2 t" pcbarrow "pcbarrow y t y2 t" pcscatter "pcscatter y t y2 t" pci "pci 100 480 110 490" pcarrowi "pcarrowi 100 480 110 490" tsline "tsline y" tsrline "tsrline y y2" mband "mband y t" mspline "mspline y t" lowess "lowess y t" lfit "lfit y t" qfit "qfit y t" fpfit "fpfit y t" lfitci "lfitci y t" qfitci "qfitci y t" fpfitci "fpfitci y t" lpoly "lpoly y t" lpolyci "lpolyci y t" kdensity "kdensity y" histogram "histogram t" function "function y = x, range(480 539)""'
local i 0
foreach w of local m6 {
    local ++i
    if mod(`i', 2) continue
    foreach o in "tline(2002m1)" "tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)" {
        _zta_err `"(`w') (tsline y), `o'"'
        local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    }
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-06"
    display as error `"TA-06 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-06 PASS: over 42 first plots, tline() and tlabel() literals are refused or read as twoway's"

// TA-07: on any twoway graph, not only tsline (sysuse auto).
local bad ""
// Flipped (WP-31 D1c): the rule as typed, which the renderer expands.
_zta_val `"line y t, tlabel(2000m1(12)2004m1)"' xlabel "480(12)528"
local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
quietly sysuse auto, clear
foreach c in "tlabel(2000 3000 4000)|xlabel|2000 3000 4000" "tline(3000)|xline|3000" ///
    "tscale(range(0 6000))|xscale|range(0 6000)" `"ttitle("W")|xtitle|\"W\""' {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("|")
    gettoken k v : rest, parse("|")
    gettoken k v : v, parse("|")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    _zta_val `"scatter mpg weight, `a'"' `k' `"`v'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
}
_zta_err `"scatter mpg weight, tlabel(2000m1)"'
local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
_zta_data
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-07"
    display as error `"TA-07 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-07 PASS: line and scatter take the t-options as twoway does"

// TA-08: twoway's lenient literals, its refused ones, and numbers first.
local bad ""
foreach c in m:2000x1 m:2000/1 m:2000-1 m:2000+1 m:2000*1 m:2000@1 m:2000=1 ///
    m:2000M1 m:2000m13 m:2000m0 m:99m1 m:2000m1x m:-2000m1 m:10000m1 ///
    m:2000.5m1 d:1+jan+2000 d:1january2000 d:01JAN2000 d:2000-01-01 ///
    w:2000w20 w:2000w53 q:2001q1 q:2001q5 h:2002h1 h:2002h3 {
    gettoken u tok : c, parse(":")
    local tok = substr("`tok'", 2, .)
    capture scalar zta_s = `u'(`tok')
    local trc = _rc
    local tv = cond(`trc', ., scalar(zta_s))
    mata: zta_v = .
    mata: st_local("dk", strofreal(_dash_tdate_value(st_local("tok"), st_local("u"), zta_v)))
    mata: st_local("dv", strofreal(zta_v, "%21.0g"))
    if (`trc' == 0 & (`dk' != 1 | `dv' != `tv')) | (`trc' != 0 & `dk' == 1) {
        local bad "`bad' `u'(`tok'): twoway `trc' `tv', dash `dk' `dv'"
    }
}
capture scalar drop zta_s
_zta_val `"line y d, tlabel(15000 01012001)"' xlabel "15000 1012001"
local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
_zta_val `"line y d, tline(01012001 01jul2001)"' xline "1012001 15157"
local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-08"
    display as error `"TA-08 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-08 PASS: lenient and refused literals as twoway's pseudo-functions read them; numbers first"

// TA-09: a date token is never run as Stata code: a backtick, $ and a
// quote are refused as twoway's words say, the global is untouched and
// nothing is registered; 10,000 positions convert in under 2 s.
local bad ""
global zta_g "keep"
foreach a in "tlabel(2000m1 \`x')" "tline(\$zta_g)" "tlabel(2000m1 \$zta_g)" {
    mata: st_local("cmd", st_local("a"))
    capture dash clear
    capture noisily dash tsline y, `macval(cmd)' name(zt9)
    local rc = _rc
    if !`rc' local bad "`bad' [rc 0]"
    if `"$zta_g"' != "keep" local bad "`bad' [global changed]"
    if `"$dash_json_zt9"' != "" local bad "`bad' [registered]"
}
mata: st_local("_td_in", invtokens(J(1, 10000, "2001m1")))
timer clear 61
timer on 61
mata: _dash_tdate_ticks("tlabel", "m")
timer off 61
quietly timer list 61
if r(t61) >= 2 | `_td_rc' local bad "`bad' [10,000 positions: `=r(t61)' s, rc `_td_rc']"
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(st_local("_td_out") == invtokens(J(1, 10000, "492"))))
if !`ok' local bad "`bad' [10,000 positions converted wrong]"
global zta_g
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-09"
    display as error `"TA-09 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-09 PASS: hostile tokens refused without evaluation; 10,000 positions in under 2 s"

// TA-10: tmlabel() and tmtick() are stored on xmlabel/xmtick.  Flipped
// (WP-31 D1): "and named until minor ticks are drawn" was wrong once dash
// draws minor ticks and labels as twoway does (minor_tick_truth.json):
// they are drawn and named nowhere.
local bad ""
foreach c in "tmlabel|xmlabel" "tmtick|xmtick" {
    gettoken o k : c, parse("|")
    local k = substr("`k'", 2, .)
    // Flipped (WP-31 D1c): the rule as typed.
    _zta_val `"tsline y, `o'(2000m7(12)2004m7)"' `k' "486(12)534"
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    _ztp_logged "$zta_log" "`o'()"
    if r(found) local bad `"`bad' [`o' named]"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-10"
    display as error `"TA-10 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-10 PASS: tmlabel() and tmtick() stored on xmlabel/xmtick and named nowhere"

// TA-15: a date literal in an x-option is refused as twoway refuses it,
// on axis 1 and axis 2.
local bad ""
foreach a in "tsline y, xlabel(2000m1)" "tsline y, xtick(2000m1)" ///
    "tsline y, xmlabel(2000m1)" "tsline y, xmtick(2000m1)" ///
    "tsline y, xline(2002m1)" "tsline y, xscale(range(1999m1 2006m1))" ///
    "tsline y, xlabel(2000m1(12)2004m1)" ///
    "(tsline y) (line y2 t, xaxis(2)), xlabel(2000m1, axis(2))" ///
    "(tsline y) (line y2 t, xaxis(2)), xtick(2000m1, axis(2))" ///
    "(tsline y) (line y2 t, xaxis(2)), xline(2002m1, axis(2))" ///
    "(tsline y) (line y2 t, xaxis(2)), xscale(range(1999m1) axis(2))" {
    _zta_err `"`a'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    if !`_zta_drc' local bad `"`bad' [`a' rc 0]"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-15"
    display as error `"TA-15 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-15 PASS: date literals in the x-options are refused in twoway's rc and words"

// TA-16: the unit is read at registration; a later format change of the
// axis variable is noted once at build, and the registered value drawn.
local bad ""
capture dash clear
quietly graph drop _all
capture log close _ztalog
quietly log using "$zta_log", name(_ztalog) text replace
capture noisily dash tsline y, tline(2002m1) name(zt16)
local rc1 = _rc
format t %td
capture noisily dash build, saving("`tapg'", replace)
local rc2 = _rc
quietly log close _ztalog
format t %tm
cert_log_has "$zta_log", needle("the t-options' dates were read as m() dates when it was registered")
if `rc1' | `rc2' | r(count) != 1 local bad " rc `rc1'/`rc2', note `=r(count)'"
mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zt16", "xline", "504")))
if !`ok' local bad "`bad' xline"
capture erase "`tapg'"
capture dash clear
if "`bad'" != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-16"
    display as error "TA-16 FAIL:`bad'"
}
else display as text "TA-16 PASS: a format change after registration is noted once, and the line stays at 504"

// TA-11: axis(2) and the t...2() spellings reach the second x axis, in
// its own unit (a %td axis 2 beside the %tm axis 1); the plurals are
// read; an axis no layer uses is refused in twoway's words, X then T
// then Y; a second comma as twoway.  ttitle(, axis(2)) is routed as
// xtitle(, axis(2)) is (twoway's own r(133) there is not followed).
local bad ""
local two "(tsline y) (line y2 d, xaxis(2)),"
foreach c in ///
    "`two' tline(2002m1)!xline!504" ///
    "`two' tline(01jan2002, axis(2))!xline2!15341" ///
    "`two' tlabel(01jan2001 01jan2003, axis(2))!xlabel2!14976 15706" ///
    "`two' ttick(01jan2001, axis(2))!xtick2!14976" ///
    "`two' tscale(range(01jan1999) axis(2))!xscale2!range(14245)" ///
    "tsline y, tlabels(2001m1 2003m1)!xlabel!492 516" ///
    "tsline y, tlines(2002m1)!xline!504" ///
    "tsline y, tticks(2001m1 2003m1)!xtick!492 516" ///
    "tsline y, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1, axis(1))!xlabel!492 516" {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : rest, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : v, parse("!")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    _zta_val `"`a'"' `k' `"`v'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
}
foreach a in "`two' tline(2002m1, axis(2))" "tsline y, tlabel(2001m1, axis(3))" ///
    "tsline y, tline(2002m1, axis(2))" ///
    "tsline y, xlabel(2001m1, axis(3)) tlabel(2001m1, axis(3))" ///
    "tsline y, tlabel(2001m1, axis(3)) ylabel(100, axis(3))" ///
    "tsline y, tlabel(2001m1, , foo)" {
    _zta_err `"`a'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    if !`_zta_drc' local bad `"`bad' [`a' rc 0]"'
}
foreach c in "tline2(01jan2002)!xline2!15341" `"ttitle("A", axis(2))!xtitle2!\"A\""' {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : rest, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : v, parse("!")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    _ztp_run `"dash `two' `a' name(zta)"' "$zta_log"
    local drc = r(rc)
    mata: st_local("ok", strofreal(_ztp_hasval("zta", st_local("k"), st_local("v"))))
    if `drc' | !`ok' local bad `"`bad' [`a': rc `drc', `k' `ok']"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-11"
    display as error `"TA-11 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-11 PASS: axis(2), t...2(), plurals, and twoway's axis refusals in X, T, Y order"

// TA-12: format() decides the unit as twoway's ticksets do: an x
// label's format() serves the t-options read after it; an option's own
// format() applies after its own positions; lines read the first time
// format among the major, minor, major-tick and minor-tick formats.
local bad ""
foreach c in "line y n, xlabel(, format(%tm)) tline(2002m1)!xline!504" ///
    "line y n, xlabel(, format(%tm)) tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)!xlabel!492 516, format(%tm)" ///
    "line y n, tlabel(, format(%tm)) tline(2002m1)!xline!504" ///
    "line y n, xmlabel(, format(%tm)) tline(2002m1)!xline!504" {
    gettoken a rest : c, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : rest, parse("!")
    gettoken k v : v, parse("!")
    local v = substr(`"`v'"', 2, .)
    _zta_val `"`a'"' `k' `"`v'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
}
foreach a in "line y n, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1, format(%tm))" ///
    "tsline y, xlabel(, format(%td)) tline(2002m1)" ///
    "tsline y, xlabel(, format(%td)) tlabel(2002m1)" {
    _zta_err `"`a'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    if !`_zta_drc' local bad `"`bad' [`a' rc 0]"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-12"
    display as error `"TA-12 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-12 PASS: format() overrides read in twoway's tickset order"

// TA-13: on a %-tm axis labels and ticks read m() literals; lines and
// scale ranges do not (twoway's get_time_format tests only %t and %d).
local bad ""
_zta_val `"line y t2, tlabel(2001m1 2003m1)"' xlabel "492 516"
local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
foreach a in "line y t2, tline(2002m1)" "line y t2, tscale(range(2006m1))" ///
    "line y t2, ttick(2001m1) tline(2002m1)" {
    _zta_err `"`a'"'
    local bad `"`bad'`_zta_bad'"'
    if !`_zta_drc' local bad `"`bad' [`a' rc 0]"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TA-13"
    display as error `"TA-13 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "TA-13 PASS: %-tm reads dates in labels and ticks, numbers only in lines and ranges"

restore
set linesize `ta_ls'

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// AT: text() read and refused as twoway reads and refuses it (WP-30
// P1.10).  twoway's answer for each probe -- its rc, its last line and
// its notes -- is test/fixtures/added_text_truth.json's
// (scripts/extract_added_text_truth.do, StataNow 19.5); dash runs here on
// the same command.  _zat_run <probe> sets _zat_trc/_zat_drc (rcs),
// _zat_tl/_zat_dl (twoway's and dash's first error lines), _zat_tn
// (twoway's first note) and _zat_named (dash's ignoring note present);
// the spec is $dash_json_zat.
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
python:
def _zat_get(pid):
    import json
    from sfi import Macro
    with open("fixtures/added_text_truth.json", encoding="utf-8") as fh:
        p = json.load(fh)["probes"][pid]
    cmd = p["cmd"]
    if cmd.startswith("twoway "):
        cmd = cmd[len("twoway "):]
    Macro.setLocal("zat_cmd", cmd)
    Macro.setLocal("zat_ds", p["dataset"])
    Macro.setLocal("zat_trc", str(p["rc"]))
    Macro.setLocal("zat_tl", p["error"].strip())
    Macro.setLocal("zat_tn", (p["notes"] or [""])[0])
import sys as _zat_sys
_zat_sys.modules["_dash_zat"] = type(_zat_sys)("_dash_zat")
_zat_sys.modules["_dash_zat"].get = _zat_get
end
capture program drop _zat_run
program define _zat_run
    args pid
    python: __import__("sys").modules["_dash_zat"].get("`pid'")
    if "`zat_ds'" == "auto" {
        sysuse auto, clear
    }
    else if "`zat_ds'" == "daily" {
        clear
        quietly set obs 100
        quietly generate d = td(01jan2001) + 5 * (_n - 1)
        format d %td
        quietly generate double y = 5 + mod(_n, 9)
    }
    else {
        clear
        quietly set obs 120
        quietly generate t = tm(1995m1) + _n - 1
        format t %tm
        quietly generate tn = t
        quietly generate double y = 10 + mod(_n, 7)
        quietly tsset t
    }
    capture log close _zatlog
    capture erase "$zta_log"
    capture dash clear
    quietly graph drop _all
    log using "$zta_log", name(_zatlog) text replace
    capture noisily dash `zat_cmd' name(zat)
    local drc = _rc
    log close _zatlog
    mata: st_local("dl", _zta_line(st_global("zta_log")))
    cert_log_has "$zta_log", needle("ignoring unsupported")
    c_local _zat_named = r(found)
    local noted 0
    if `"`zat_tn'"' != "" {
        cert_log_has "$zta_log", needle(`"`zat_tn'"')
        local noted = r(found)
    }
    c_local _zat_noted `noted'
    c_local _zat_trc `zat_trc'
    c_local _zat_drc `drc'
    c_local _zat_tl : copy local zat_tl
    c_local _zat_dl : copy local dl
    c_local _zat_tn : copy local zat_tn
end
// _zat_same <probe>...: each probe's rc and first line are twoway's, and
// no ignoring note names text(); _zat_bad says what differed.
capture program drop _zat_same
program define _zat_same
    local bad ""
    foreach pid of local 0 {
        _zat_run `pid'
        mata: st_local("same", strofreal(st_local("_zat_tl") == st_local("_zat_dl")))
        if `_zat_trc' != `_zat_drc' | (`_zat_trc' & !`same') | `_zat_named' {
            local bad `"`bad' [`pid': twoway `_zat_trc' `_zat_tl' | dash `_zat_drc' `_zat_dl' named `_zat_named']"'
        }
    }
    c_local _zat_bad : copy local bad
end
// _zat_records <graph>: the added_text records of $dash_json_<graph> as
// "lines|opts" pairs, in order, into _zat_recs (and their count, _zat_nr).
capture program drop _zat_records
program define _zat_records
    args g
    mata: _zat_recs(st_global("dash_json_" + st_local("g")))
    c_local _zat_recs : copy local _zat_recs
    c_local _zat_nr `_zat_nr'
end
capture mata: mata drop _zat_recs()
capture mata: mata drop _zat_x()
mata:
void _zat_recs(string scalar js)
{
    string scalar out, q, rest, lines, opts
    real scalar   n, p, e

    q = char(34)
    out = ""
    n = 0
    rest = js
    while ((p = strpos(rest, q + "at_lines" + q + ":")) > 0) {
        rest = substr(rest, p + 11, .)
        e = strpos(rest, "]")
        lines = substr(rest, 1, e)
        p = strpos(rest, q + "at_opts" + q + ":" + q)
        rest = substr(rest, p + 11, .)
        e = strpos(rest, q + "}")
        opts = substr(rest, 1, e - 1)
        out = out + (n ? " ; " : "") + subinstr(lines, q, "~") + "|" + opts
        n++
    }
    st_local("_zat_recs", out)
    st_local("_zat_nr", strofreal(n))
}
// The first record's at_x, as written, or "".
string scalar _zat_x(string scalar js)
{
    string scalar q, rest
    real scalar   p

    q = char(34)
    p = strpos(js, q + "at_x" + q + ":")
    if (!p) return("")
    rest = substr(js, p + 7, .)
    return(substr(rest, 1, strpos(rest, ",") - 1))
}
end
preserve
local at_ls = c(linesize)
set linesize 200

// AT-01: a malformed point is refused in twoway's words, r(198), and one
// bad copy refuses the graph; 3e3 is a number.
_zat_same r_onept r_missy r_alpha r_expr r_big r_onebad r_e3
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-01"
    display as error `"AT-01 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-01 PASS: invalid point, <x> <y>, as twoway refuses it"

// AT-02: a bare word or a trailing y is the next point's, as twoway reads
// it: invalid point with an empty x, the double space kept.
_zat_same r_trail1 r_bare
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-02"
    display as error `"AT-02 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-02 PASS: a bare word or a lone y is an invalid point"

// AT-03: an axis pair the graph lacks is refused, even for a copy with no
// point; the pair a second-axis layer draws is accepted.
_zat_same r_y2 r_x2 r_nopt_y2 r_y2ok
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-03"
    display as error `"AT-03 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-03 PASS: specified axis pair (Y X) not in graph, as twoway refuses it"

// AT-04: repeated copies keep their own sub-options, in one option list,
// in a plot group, in a || segment and after the comma; a line naming a
// key is text, so the substring readers find dash's own count only.
// _zat_records writes a record's lines with ~ for each double quote.
local bad ""
foreach c in "two![~AAA~]|size(large) color(red) ; [~BBB~]|" ///
    "level_pg![~PG~]| ; [~GL~]|" "level_seg![~S1~]| ; [~S2~]|" {
    gettoken pid want : c, parse("!")
    local want = substr(`"`want'"', 2, .)
    _zat_run `pid'
    _zat_records zat
    if `_zat_drc' | `"`_zat_recs'"' != `"`want'"' {
        local bad `"`bad' [`pid': rc `_zat_drc' `_zat_recs']"'
    }
}
sysuse auto, clear
capture dash clear
capture noisily dash scatter mpg weight, text(30 3000 `""width":"1" "added_text_n":"0""') text(20 4000 "B", width(5)) name(zat4)
local drc = _rc
// dash writes a "width" key only when width() was given a value.
mata: st_local("hw", strofreal(strpos(st_global("dash_json_zat4"), char(34) + "width" + char(34) + ":" + char(34)) > 0))
mata: st_local("fn", strofreal(_dash_json_first_num(st_global("dash_json_zat4"), "added_text_n")))
if `drc' | `hw' | `fn' != 2 local bad `"`bad' [readers: rc `drc' width `hw' added_text_n `fn']"'
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-04"
    display as error `"AT-04 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-04 PASS: each copy a record with its own sub-options; no key read from text"

// AT-04b: 100,000 one-point copies, joined as _dash_rep_merge joins them,
// are read in linear time.  Measured as linear, not against a wall-clock
// bound: 100,000 copies take under 8 times what 25,000 take (linear is
// about 4, quadratic about 16), with 50 ms of slack for timer noise and a
// 10-second ceiling.  A one-second bound failed under a loaded machine
// (1.12 s, 22oct2026) on code that reads the same 100,000 in 0.77 s alone.
// (zat_sz: _dash_at_parse sets locals of its own, _at_k among them.)
foreach zat_sz in 25000 100000 {
    mata: _zat_big = ("1 1 " + char(34) + "a" + char(34) + char(30)) * `zat_sz'
    timer clear 56
    timer on 56
    local _at_n ""
    capture mata: st_local("_zat_rc", strofreal(_dash_at_parse(_zat_big, 0)))
    local prc`zat_sz' = _rc
    timer off 56
    quietly timer list 56
    local secs`zat_sz' = r(t56)
    local n`zat_sz' "`_at_n'"
    mata: mata drop _zat_big
}
local _at_bad = `prc25000' | `prc100000' | "`n25000'" != "25000"
local _at_bad = `_at_bad' | "`n100000'" != "100000"
local _at_bad = `_at_bad' | `secs100000' >= 8 * `secs25000' + 0.05 | `secs100000' >= 10
if `_at_bad' {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-04b"
    display as error "AT-04b FAIL: `n25000' records in `secs25000' s, `n100000' in `secs100000' s"
}
else display as text "AT-04b PASS: 25,000 copies in `secs25000' s, 100,000 in `secs100000' s"

// AT-05: a sub-option twoway does not take is refused in its words; its
// abbreviations are accepted; an unknown placement() is noted as twoway
// notes it.  (tex(), which twoway refuses as it refuses any option it
// lacks, is named in dash's ignoring note as every unknown option is:
// help dash##differences.)
_zat_same r_nosuch r_ori abbr pl_40
local bad `"`_zat_bad'"'
_zat_run pl_40
if !`_zat_noted' | `"`_zat_tn'"' == "" local bad `"`bad' [place(zz) note: `_zat_tn']"'
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-05"
    display as error `"AT-05 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-05 PASS: option nosuch() not allowed; c() si() orient() read; place(zz) noted"

// AT-06: sub-options twoway takes and dash does not draw are named once.
* flipped WP-31 D13: tstyle() is drawn (the heading's size), so the note
* names width() and linegap() only.
_zat_same noted
local bad `"`_zat_bad'"'
cert_log_has "$zta_log", needle("text() draws no width() linegap();")
if !r(found) local bad `"`bad' [no note naming width() linegap()]"'
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-06"
    display as error `"AT-06 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-06 PASS: width() linegap() named once"

// AT-07: an empty string, no string or no point draws nothing, rc 0.
_zat_same empty nostr none
local bad `"`_zat_bad'"'
foreach pid in empty nostr none {
    _zat_run `pid'
    _zat_records zat
    if `_zat_nr' local bad `"`bad' [`pid': `_zat_nr' records]"'
}
if `"`bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-07"
    display as error `"AT-07 FAIL:`bad'"'
}
else display as text `"AT-07 PASS: text(30 3000 ""), text(30 3000) and text() draw nothing"'

// AT-08: text() is never named as unsupported (every _zat_same case above
// checked the note; here the plain one).
_zat_same aaa
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-08"
    display as error `"AT-08 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-08 PASS: text() is not named in the ignoring note"

// AT-30: ttext() refuses what twoway refuses: text() takes no date, a
// function form is no point, and a literal the axis's format cannot read
// -- 2001m13, a month on a numeric or daily axis, a missing value, a
// month where the first plot's x is unformatted -- is "<x> is not a
// number"; y is a number.
_zat_same tt_text tt_fn tt_m13 tt_auto tt_dot tt_dm tt_two1 tt_rev
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-30"
    display as error `"AT-30 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-30 PASS: ttext()'s date refusals are twoway's"

// AT-31..AT-36: each drawn ttext() at twoway's x in the axis's unit (the
// fixture's measured point, rounded): a month and a quoted month, a
// quarter on a %tm axis, a day on a %td axis, the first plot's format
// deciding (twoway (line y t) (line y tn)), an xlabel() format() on an
// unformatted x and a number format on a %tm x, and a number as text()
// reads it.  _zat_draw "<probe> <x> ...": _zat_bad says what differed.
capture program drop _zat_draw
program define _zat_draw
    local c `"`0'"'
    local bad ""
    while `"`c'"' != "" {
        gettoken pid c : c
        gettoken want c : c
        _zat_run `pid'
        mata: st_local("x", _zat_x(st_global("dash_json_zat")))
        if `_zat_drc' | `_zat_trc' | "`x'" != "`want'" | `_zat_named' {
            local bad `"`bad' [`pid': rc `_zat_drc' (twoway `_zat_trc'), at_x `x' not `want', named `_zat_named']"'
        }
    }
    c_local _zat_bad : copy local bad
end
_zat_draw tt_m 492 tt_mq 492
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-31"
    display as error `"AT-31 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-31 PASS: ttext(12 2001m1) and its quoted form at 492"
_zat_draw tt_q 492
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-32"
    display as error `"AT-32 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-32 PASS: a quarter on a %tm axis at its first month"
_zat_draw tt_d 15127
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-33"
    display as error `"AT-33 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-33 PASS: a day on a %td axis"
_zat_draw tt_two2 492
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-34"
    display as error `"AT-34 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-34 PASS: the first plot's x format decides"
_zat_draw tt_xl 492 tt_xl9 492
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-35"
    display as error `"AT-35 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-35 PASS: xlabel()'s format() read as twoway reads the time format"
_zat_draw tt_num 3000
if `"`_zat_bad'"' != "" {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' AT-36"
    display as error `"AT-36 FAIL:`_zat_bad'"'
}
else display as text "AT-36 PASS: a number is a number"

restore
capture erase "$zta_log"
capture dash clear
set linesize `at_ls'
global zta_log

// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// Summary
// ----------------------------------------------------------------
// twoway's answers: a question the fixture could not answer, or (with
// DASH_CERT_REMEASURE=1) an answer twoway no longer gives, fails the run.
cert_truth_close
if r(problems) > 0 {
    local nfail = `nfail' + 1
    local faillist "`faillist' TRUTH"
}
capture dash clear
capture erase "`logfile'"
display as text ""
display as text "============================================================"
if `nfail' == 0 {
    display as text "  test_twoway_option_parity: ALL CHECKS PASSED"
    display as text "============================================================"
}
else {
    display as error "  test_twoway_option_parity: `nfail' CHECK(S) FAILED"
    display as error "  failing:`faillist'"
    display as text "============================================================"
    exit 9
}
